, then epic R — entrypoints can grow (#170)\n\n* feat(composition): at a monorepo product root, a vertical its services have is an Ok no-op naming them (Q3.1)\n* feat(new): keel new inside a keel project is refused as keel.inside-project (Q3.2)\n* fix(refusals): refusals name what they know — comesWith, elsewhere, the stale product root''s pin, the project above (Q3.3)\n* test(sweep): the weekly report-only composition sweep (Q3.4)\n* fix(persistence): persistence survives the peer context on Micronaut and TypeScript moduliths (Q3.5)\n* docs(roadmap): plan epic R — entrypoints can grow\n* test(composition): the shared-file byte golden (R.1a)\n* feat(composition): rank-anchored README sections (R.1a)\n* feat(composition): rank-anchored module lists, scripts, [[bin]] and the dev container''s attach upgrade (R.1b)\n* fix(harness): the manifest records harness files as keel leaves them (R.2a)\n* feat(growth): the pure growth reading (R.2a)\n* feat(cli): keel add entrypoint <cli|http>, proven byte-identical to the twin preset by grid I10 (R.2b)\n* feat(refusals): the missing-entrypoint refusal carries keel add entrypoint http (R.2c)\n* feat(growth): Go, Rust, TypeScript and JVM moduliths grow with their contexts (R.3a–d)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NQ82n8XipMJyRoKHtuGgzC","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquIRbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlXMQAIfb1DG+TWoLo44X52xObEzr\nSEEl3UveoXUuHoIm9SlG5z3CeqU3W+oRK+d/PyWjAvhaI9p3OkF+5SyOcqxxiP/u\noPu+NajLSr3RsHfqMGFPAe2vFwKHRZbT8OCB90Yp4eCwUAFmQ3dWBn2KIAQqGq9X\n117E9YhSUdzeFspm1miUJ/mwwaKmr6uhxY7JsqKmXH4BEU6UAL2nThWPu/mXjxH6\n7OXDxc/X1U3Pkms/NUONQjQ+6feShw8tDSImWbK+8xf3fmKMQZoJF+oxf9KeF1Sa\noR49/gYa32TaODCMK33/DqwTqM6nYU5AKtuKK9Xh2Bc57qdmO7iOeFXxH3Cz9zvq\npM0VLNak8ILtvhZVkV2mqCV56pfC31d2/XWkv5Pkmh6aMzpVoBda7oCtu6STWA+Y\nmYt+O3DOffZpA5Ag6CHiY91Zc25HCcH0NcBaP24ZX+dxfqMf1PnIGs4N/ZufH+aq\nSfQB19TULSdfNx1BtyWkMsh3Qb0MfHVhuizUWPSs