"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/adab93adff470667f3c8e0eeef2ec714a39786f0","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGFkYWI5M2FkZmY0NzA2NjdmM2M4ZTBlZWVmMmVjNzE0YTM5Nzg2ZjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/c950bf94e54af1c72ecd997b989335fbac9ece75","sha":"c950bf94e54af1c72ecd997b989335fbac9ece75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c950bf94e54af1c72ecd997b989335fbac9ece75"}],"sha":"adab93adff470667f3c8e0eeef2ec714a39786f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/adab93adff470667f3c8e0eeef2ec714a39786f0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c950bf94e54af1c72ecd997b989335fbac9ece75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T04:14:32Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T04:14:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Agent-harness wave 5: dogfood on keel (#145), fullstack product root (#142), vcs conventions (#143) (#168)\n\n#145 — keel dogfoods its own per-directory-docs model. The root\nAGENTS.md is 646 lines down to 111, the same budget keel emits, and\nnothing was deleted: the e2e grid moved to tests/e2e/AGENTS.md, the CI\nand release mechanics to .github/AGENTS.md, the documentation and\nchangelog policy to docs/AGENTS.md, the template-tree and version-pin\nrules to assets/AGENTS.md, the testing approach to tests/AGENTS.md, the\nfour standing engine notes to src/domain/core/AGENTS.md, and the\nrepository tree to docs/development.md. Every documented directory\ndeclares a keel:purpose line the root map row quotes verbatim, and\ncarries a one-line CLAUDE.md pointer. tests/repo-docs.test.ts is the\nrepo-local keel docs check. Measured with evals/lib/context-audit.mjs,\nthe root eager load falls 82.6% — 648 lines / ~8.9k approx. tokens to\n113 / ~1.5k — while total contributor prose grows 874 → 987 lines.\n\nThe dogfood surfaced a latent defect, fixed here: keel:children rows\nwere project-relative like the root map''s, so a row inside\nmodules/AGENTS.md pointed at modules/modules/. Rows are now relative to\nthe document that holds them.\n\n#142 — a composite product root gets a harness. fullstack/product-harness\nlands the pair and the shims over a thin product-root document whose one\nrule is to work inside a service, under that service''s own harness. The\nservice rows are the engine''s keel:map projection over\nmanifest.services[] — the same seam that projects a row per bounded\ncontext — so keel docs sync|check drift-guards them and no handler\nbranches on what kind of root it is looking at. Nothing is hoisted to\nthe root: no settings, no hooks, no skills, and no keel:skills-index\nslot, with the reason stated in the emitted document.\n\n#143 — the vcs vertical grows its working conventions.\nvcs/commit-conventions emits a POSIX sh commit-msg gate into the tracked\n.githooks/, pointed at by core.hooksPath and brownfield-safe;\nvcs/changelog emits keel''s own split-changelog shape outward with a\nPOSIX sh + awk cut script. Both are individually declinable. One source\nof truth for the shape: tests/support/changelog-shape.ts checks keel''s\nown CHANGELOG.md and the emitted template alike.\n\nHARNESS_GENERATION stays 1: nothing here moves a sentinel, a region or a\nharness document an older scaffold carries.\n\nCloses #145\nCloses #142\nCloses #143\nRefs #147\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DKnbj36U6LgWMHbzx4XTBz","tree":{"sha":"1b0f2342d2dc680715180dd0c9b69f897667b2de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/1b0f2342d2dc680715180dd0c9b69f897667b2de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/c950bf94e54af1c72ecd997b989335fbac9ece75","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b0f2342d2dc680715180dd0c9b69f897667b2de\nparent 23bae05bfba17b19aa69da47d9912adbf3788ec2\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1789532072 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789532072 +0200\n\nAgent-harness wave 5: dogfood on keel (#145), fullstack product root (#142), vcs conventions (#143) (#168)\n\n#145 — keel dogfoods its own per-directory-docs model. The root\nAGENTS.md is 646 lines down to 111, the same budget keel emits, and\nnothing was deleted: the e2e grid moved to tests/e2e/AGENTS.md, the CI\nand release mechanics to .github/AGENTS.md, the documentation and\nchangelog policy to docs/AGENTS.md, the template-tree and version-pin\nrules to assets/AGENTS.md, the testing approach to tests/AGENTS.md, the\nfour standing engine notes to src/domain/core/AGENTS.md, and the\nrepository tree to docs/development.md. Every documented directory\ndeclares a keel:purpose line the root map row quotes verbatim, and\ncarries a one-line CLAUDE.md pointer. tests/repo-docs.test.ts is the\nrepo-local keel docs check. Measured with evals/lib/context-audit.mjs,\nthe root eager load falls 82.6% — 648 lines / ~8.9k approx. tokens to\n113 / ~1.5k — while total contributor prose grows 874 → 987 lines.\n\nThe dogfood surfaced a latent defect, fixed here: keel:children rows\nwere project-relative like the root map''s, so a row inside\nmodules/AGENTS.md pointed at modules/modules/. Rows are now relative to\nthe document that holds them.\n\n#142 — a composite product root gets a harness. fullstack/product-harness\nlands the pair and the shims over a thin product-root document whose one\nrule is to work inside a service, under that service''s own harness. The\nservice rows are the engine''s keel:map projection over\nmanifest.services[] — the same seam that projects a row per bounded\ncontext — so keel docs sync|check drift-guards them and no handler\nbranches on what kind of root it is looking at. Nothing is hoisted to\nthe root: no settings, no hooks, no skills, and no keel:skills-index\nslot, with the reason stated in the emitted document.\n\n#143 — the vcs vertical grows its working conventions.\nvcs/commit-conventions emits a POSIX sh commit-msg gate into the tracked\n.githooks/, pointed at by core.hooksPath and brownfield-safe;\nvcs/changelog emits keel''s own split-changelog shape outward with a\nPOSIX sh + awk cut script. Both are individually declinable. One source\nof truth for the shape: tests/support/changelog-shape.ts checks keel''s\nown CHANGELOG.md and the emitted template alike.\n\nHARNESS_GENERATION stays 1: nothing here moves a sentinel, a region or a\nharness document an older scaffold carries.\n\nCloses #145\nCloses #142\nCloses #143\nRefs #147\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DKnbj36U6LgWMHbzx4XTBz","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqheoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcssQAIPRk0ELgOp4mtXNFIOVUGKu\nPlVc3anDzu3a2uP1fcyB2817SVlOyfblAUygyIDyGfP69g80x1pzz8YTXjvQdgX5\nXctLm+UuMs1IVdA2gRXDmOhzlgBn4rUg25htC60XWQBy7k2DpuEEfIBI8n/zWIG3\ndCFYHNV6XryhSxaZ1x4SSdF/hEfLs53yWfv3RBKG3wtC3EIuwKbyCuEDft7bwviH\nPPAKmrJ6jRS3v+JspjEBiTWxKQVQB8REEJ8LNMWZeeSmmX/7C3KkOkMN1hnQ3CU3\nPp6kX6mBneocXAPGwRnQ97Q5udZfPapkTinhiXAhsbdchvsB748l6RG42oaE37CB\nkwv2li3ZED5wSQgZSETgXFOJRpad5pLPaUBTnMAH4r2MyJCBfDkUKW9mTQT4gL84\nkNnS37Jo/dFFhaZhjdd7/xkuSSvDZwyOvlb/pKjrr5C0f/GnL9AE+cN9TKNaRicP\nvXOtShRQl+afp3dXORaeayDB19D6C5yQbzmkPokwRNC9oDMbOH1DdBki3NaosaVF\neem7Sf9AsHVAnWjQRUjAp9bHH4fz1Vt14ID2ec4csx1nrgfzPDD3MKoRCNOe4Hfq\nDYXysb6LAfUMyW3FVdc6IzlSFolRn+vcaurY7yEgccWM3cI5weTF1DbucKXP3lIp\n8Z06jzHR9TGJNA5AkCR3\n=jl2t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T04:14:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":fal