ow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/02c5e0a61224d7d694fa076013c5b139e37e0fd3","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDAyYzVlMGE2MTIyNGQ3ZDY5NGZhMDc2MDEzYzViMTM5ZTM3ZTBmZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d","sha":"1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d"}],"sha":"02c5e0a61224d7d694fa076013c5b139e37e0fd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/02c5e0a61224d7d694fa076013c5b139e37e0fd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T15:50:33Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T15:50:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): put the keel ui stepper in an application shell (#127)\n\nThe wizard''s own rule is that the plan stays visible through every\nstep, and a page that scrolls as a document only keeps that promise on\na short one: reach the questions and the plan is off screen again,\nwhich is the failure the stepper was meant to avoid.\n\nThe page is now a shell — masthead, the rail in a band of its own,\nthen a step column and a plan column that scroll independently,\ncollapsing to one below 62rem. `#scaffold()` is the only part of\n`<keel-app>` whose shape changed; every `data-role` its `#render()`\naddresses is still there, so the stepper''s own logic is untouched.\n\n- A step''s controls survive a re-render that did not change the step,\n  so a text answer keeps its caret; the plan''s skeleton is built once,\n  so the file tree keeps its scroll position.\n- The questions step reads `binding.kind`: a field of the command gets\n  its own heading drawn with the same cards the narrowing steps use,\n  while the adapters'' own questions are grouped under Details by the\n  adapter that asked.\n- The file tree joins single-child directory chains, folds directories\n  and keeps them folded, and counts the files under each. It removes\n  itself rather than hiding when a refusal leaves no plan.\n- The plan carries the command line equivalent to it, with a copy\n  button, derived from the same body the review step posts.\n- `dom.js` is a union: the cards plus the smaller shapes the other\n  halves need. A type scale replaces planks'' 1.5 ratio for text, and\n  one token set covers both themes.\n\nAll 21 `keel ui` browser cases pass unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01243SKRr4vtNxMeSxGwPogB","tree":{"sha":"9d3ea6283c5434561cc797a0a4306fac11f07513","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/9d3ea6283c5434561cc797a0a4306fac11f07513"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d3ea6283c5434561cc797a0a4306fac11f07513\nparent ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787500233 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787500233 +0200\n\nfeat(ui): put the keel ui stepper in an application shell (#127)\n\nThe wizard''s own rule is that the plan stays visible through every\nstep, and a page that scrolls as a document only keeps that promise on\na short one: reach the questions and the plan is off screen again,\nwhich is the failure the stepper was meant to avoid.\n\nThe page is now a shell — masthead, the rail in a band of its own,\nthen a step column and a plan column that scroll independently,\ncollapsing to one below 62rem. `#scaffold()` is the only part of\n`<keel-app>` whose shape changed; every `data-role` its `#render()`\naddresses is still there, so the stepper''s own logic is untouched.\n\n- A step''s controls survive a re-render that did not change the step,\n  so a text answer keeps its caret; the plan''s skeleton is built once,\n  so the file tree keeps its scroll position.\n- The questions step reads `binding.kind`: a field of the command gets\n  its own heading drawn with the same cards the narrowing steps use,\n  while the adapters'' own questions are grouped under Details by the\n  adapter that asked.\n- The file tree joins single-child directory chains, folds directories\n  and keeps them folded, and counts the files under each. It removes\n  itself rather than hiding when a refusal leaves no plan.\n- The plan carries the command line equivalent to it, with a copy\n  button, derived from the same body the review step posts.\n- `dom.js` is a union: the cards plus the smaller shapes the other\n  halves need. A type scale replaces planks'' 1.5 ratio for text, and\n  one token set covers both themes.\n\nAll 21 `keel ui` browser cases pass unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01243SKRr4vtNxMeSxGwPogB","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqixbJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3JkQAFmV1aeuYtIjAb1sJKgq2biu\ncRguJcHKSKunmHwLMZp1utwjB5TcquxwZWBfqUHS5qglUpgLs+VKO+okgCjAEEZv\niwxNYPAxMI3ndT/RJHuxokc2/xkA169XwTtrimjm3IxJFOKLGPSL1xUHxjnAFFS6\nbvTSQlrLMGYD3uF0JjymnmPeKmZh/cYvTuRFgcTbctT3yNm2TKWF/W8cS0eYaqiS\nOQdDPqYM6z546JLxBL/CvKtNKYilb5+wCqF9MesIqLdWaFNNiE/i05yrmHLhttnR\nQWzxNxpwkdclWbOMxqPi2uIrUB+flZb/Id3Bur7T9FU8hC4ZdzLM6ZG/iTPgmSJ/\nSTIawb0S08EtmT+es52xA526PUQWqjxZ5ejCA7WwO7LjMk4xv0/y8oK6hUOiDKBZ\nVQ5vlaC5XnEp/kvrEPxUcQs0a8BaPSMWvtdf29xc7x1rZI5QHq/Tk9N0ogTfTs8S\nKDF/GHCxA3Pikc5ncBIl2ilZPe3eNw2sLWTNdYG72+NBMtBmYaQ0xTdPUNPiW5OW\nMDF1Vd+OJseRwr5mm8pTyQWxEcLGljB4Jtf7Wsnajoyy+Zy6dNaiF9FBQhTSv3Nt\n5v626M/6z2I8aVM/lxE2tlpHFxC98Qvnp2k1VsV2GrNvGley1haQe/2vBG87/wK4\n2K7PURUcuuMuvMksq0FJ\n=if+t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T15:50:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDEwMDBmNGJlNTg1ZjQwM2E2OTEwN2UyNGM5ODlkNjUyNGI0ZjI4M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4","sha":"ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4"}],"sha":"1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1000f4be585f403a69107e24c989d6524b4f283d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:05:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:16:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"fix(build): typecheck the tests, and fix what that surfaced\n\n`tsconfig.json` carried `\"include\": [\"src\", \"tests\"]` and\n`\"exclude\": [..., \"tests\"]`. Exclude wins, so `pnpm typecheck` checked\nno test file at all — which is how an undefined identifier in an e2e\nsuite reached a test run past both `lint` and `typecheck` in the\ncommit before this one. Closing it surfaced 77 errors. None was\ntheoretical:\n\n- **Three imports had rotted.** `AnswerMap` has not existed since it\n  became `PresetAnswers`, and `Vertical` is a composition type, not\n  one `core/stacks.ts` re-exports. Type-only imports of names that are\n  gone compile to nothing, so nothing ever complained.\n- **`noUncheckedIndexedAccess` was being ignored wholesale.**\n  `stack.buildSystems[0].tag` guarded only by `stack.buildSystems`,\n  `match[1]` from a group that may not participate, `cycles[0]` from a\n  fetched feed, `SCENARIOS[5]` — that last one now reads\n  `scenario(''ts-pnpm'')`, which also says which stack the case pins.\n- **`exactOptionalPropertyTypes` likewise.** `{ ...family,\n  formatCommand: undefined }` and `{ buildSystems: undefined }` mean\n  \"this one has none\", and under EOPT that is an absent key rather\n  than one set to `undefined`. The fixtures say so now.\n- **`spawnSync().stdout` is `string | Buffer`** unless the encoding is\n  statically known; both e2e harnesses were assigning it to a `string`.\n\nThe two `@ts-expect-error` suppressions over `assets/web/src/*.js` are\ngone too. `allowJs` lets TS read the page''s own JSDoc, so the pure\nmodules the browser ships are now checked against the DTOs they\nconsume — and it immediately caught `finder.js` declaring mutable\narrays where `Catalog.finder` hands it readonly ones. That coupling is\nthe point: the page''s typedefs are a claim about the engine''s shape,\nand this PR changed that shape.\n\n`dist/` is unaffected — `tsconfig.build.json` still includes `src`\nalone, and carries no test or asset file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NM2iUsxKZSvhxkkietLwuB","tree":{"sha":"9ef93111aed4f540ca2757a4ea1ed92e46240ff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/9ef93111aed4f540ca2757a4ea1ed92e46240ff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGVjZGRiNzI4M2RhMWU3MjNiZWVhYzI2YWM5YWI5ODcyMWM5NDJlYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665","sha":"1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665"}],"sha":"ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ecddb7283da1e723beeac26ac9ab98721c942ec4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:42:30Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:16:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"feat(ui): offer each vertical as a card naming what it buys you\n\nWhich capability to add next is the one real question the brownfield\npage asks, and it asked it with a `<select>` of ids: `iac`, `dev-env`,\n`vcs`. Those mean nothing until you already know keel''s vocabulary,\nwhich is the opposite of what a guided page is for. Each vertical is a\ncard now — the concept it bears, the id `keel add <id>` takes, and one\nline on what installing it gets you.\n\nThe title is a new optional field on `Vertical`, because the id is a\nhandle and not a name. It is resolved rather than read: `verticalTitle`\nspells one out of the id where a vertical declares none, so a plugin''s\nreads as \"Acme widget\" instead of `acme-widget`, and both front ends\nand `keel add --list` agree on it without a table of their own.\n`distribution`, `containerization` and `vcs` described what they *were*\nrather than what they get you, which is fine next to an id in `--list`\nand useless as the body of a card; they now say what appears.\n\nTwo things the cards changed about what is offered. Nothing is\npre-selected: the page used to open on `available[0]`, and since\n`available` is every uninstalled vertical with coverage not consulted,\nthat could be — and on a Go CLI was — one the project cannot carry, so\nthe brownfield page opened on a refusal nobody had asked for. And\nnothing is hidden: a vertical this shape cannot take says so when\npicked, with the tag that would carry it, which is the useful half of\nthat refusal and is lost by filtering it out of the list. The step''s\nown description said the opposite; it was wrong when written.\n\nThe card markup moves to `assets/web/src/dom.js` and the narrowing\nsteps render from it too — a card is a decision the page already made\nabout how it asks its consequential questions, and a second copy is a\nsecond place for that to erode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NM2iUsxKZSvhxkkietLwuB","tree":{"sha":"d0325b3cf95bcf6db86ba18ce038abf14270dfc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/d0325b3cf95bcf6db86ba18ce038abf14270dfc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE1NjE3ODZlMzBiODBkNmViMzYxNGU4ODUxNjczN2VhNTY0Y2Y2NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1","sha":"a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1"}],"sha":"1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1561786e30b80d6eb3614e88516737ea564cf665"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:30:00Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:16:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"fix(test): build dist once across the `keel ui` suites, not once each\n\n`e2e (web)` went red on `ui-plugin-stack` with\n\n    SyntaxError: The requested module ''.../handlers/catalog.js''\n    does not provide an export named ''CatalogHandler''\n\non a file nobody had touched, exporting exactly that. The other two\n`keel ui` suites imported the same module in the same job and passed,\nwhich is the tell: the export was not missing, the file was half\nwritten.\n\nEach of these suites compiled `dist/` in its own `beforeAll`, because\n`bin/keel.js` loads it and the e2e job installs without building.\nVitest parallelises across files, so that was three `tsc` runs into\none directory while a fourth process — a spawned `keel ui` — imported\nout of it. Two suites had been racing all along; the third made it\nlikely enough to land.\n\nThe build is claimed now rather than repeated: `mkdir` is atomic, so\none worker wins and compiles while the rest wait for the marker it\ndrops. The claim is keyed by a digest of `tsconfig.build.json` and\nevery file under `src/`, which is what keeps \"compile, don''t trust\nthe last run''s artefact\" true — a changed file changes the key and\nbuys a fresh build, an untouched tree reuses one that is byte-for-byte\nwhat this suite would have produced. A holder that dies mid-build is\nwaited out and then overwritten.\n\nVerified against the CI condition: `rm -rf dist` and the three suites\nin parallel, 21/21 green with one compile; a second run reuses it; a\ntouched source produces a new key and rebuilds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NM2iUsxKZSvhxkkietLwuB","tree":{"sha":"2ddcff05de320c88e351e149ed70113622e24064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/2ddcff05de320c88e351e149ed70113622e24064"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGE5MjZmODlhMjUxZWQzZGE0YThlNmIwOWY0ZDY4MmVhMDFhNjBkYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267","sha":"11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267"}],"sha":"a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/a926f89a251ed3da4a8e6b09f4d682ea01a60dc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T12:19:47Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:16:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"fix(web): let a refusal from the bottom of the install arrive as one\n\n`resolveVertical` hard-fails when no adapter covers a dimension a\nvertical declares — `keel add containerization` on a CLI-shaped\nproject, which has nothing to serve an image from — and it did so by\nthrowing a bare `Error` out of `installVertical`, past every menu. The\nCLI coped, because any throw is a message to its top-level catch;\n`keel ui` could not. A throw is the one thing an HTTP layer can only\nread as a crash, so it answered 500 with a bare string and the page\nshowed \"POST /api/preview failed with 500\" for a refusal that names\nboth the missing dimension and the tag that would close it.\n\n`preflightCoverage` left a comment saying this decision was about\nevery escape from the install engine rather than about `--with`. It\nis, so it is made at the seam every escape crosses. `ResolutionError`\nis a `DomainError` now, carrying `keel.uncoverable-vertical` — the\nsame code the `--with` preflight already refuses with, it being the\nsame condition — or `keel.adapter-cycle`; and `RegistryMediator`\nnormalises a thrown `DomainError` onto the `Err` rail. `Result` is\nwhat the Mediator promises every primary adapter, so the seam that\npromises it keeps it, rather than the same try/catch in `add-vertical`,\n`add-module` and both halves of `new-project` plus a fifth copy next\ntime. Anything that is not a `DomainError` still throws: a bug must\nnot be dressed up as a refusal.\n\nThe page then has something to show, and shows it three ways — the\nbanner carries the code and the message, the plan says it has no tree\n*because* the run was refused rather than sitting blank beside it, and\nthe review step repeats the reason next to a Generate button it holds\nshut. `tests/e2e/ui-refusal.test.ts` drives all three in a browser and\nthat a carryable vertical clears them, seeding its project in-process\nwith deferred actions faked so it installs nothing.\n\n`keel new` and `keel add` print exactly what they printed before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NM2iUsxKZSvhxkkietLwuB","tree":{"sha":"a41ce2ec7cc6ed2c71d56b044db8b07827b386ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/a41ce2ec7cc6ed2c71d56b044db8b07827b386ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDExZTk2ZjQ1NGQ3OWQ2OTRkYTNhNTQ2NzNmYzJkZjI1N2ExNTgyNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/0ac2f38abf51a4bacf3023e61a30e510fbb5b735","sha":"0ac2f38abf51a4bacf3023e61a30e510fbb5b735","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0ac2f38abf51a4bacf3023e61a30e510fbb5b735"}],"sha":"11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/11e96f454d79d694da3a54673fc2df257a158267"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0ac2f38abf51a4bacf3023e61a30e510fbb5b735/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:35:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T13:16:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"feat(wizard): drill down from what you are building, and step through it\n\nThe stack finder asked language → user-side adapters → framework, which\nmade a newcomer name a \"user-side adapter\" before it asked anything they\nalready knew the answer to. It now narrows widest first — shape →\nlanguage → framework → user-side adapters — where shape is fullstack,\nbackend or frontend, and both front ends walk the same tree.\n\nA shape is derived, never listed: each registered entrypoint declares\nwhich end it is driven from (`ENTRYPOINTS[].side`) and a preset''s shape\nis those sides, counted. That is what finally put the composite products\non the guided path — they carry no `lang.*` tag, so they used to appear\nin no menu at all and `keel new` could reach `fullstack` only through\n\"pick a preset by id\". A composite places itself through its services:\nthe union of their entrypoints gives the shape, and its one back-side\nservice gives the language and framework. Every shipped preset is now\nreachable from some path, which `stack-wizard.test.ts` asserts.\n\n`keel new` says where it is: it prints what it is about to ask, numbers\neach step it actually asks — a step whose answer is already settled is\nstill skipped, so the numbers never claim a question that does not come\n— and names the preset it landed on.\n\n`keel ui` becomes a stepper rather than one long form. Same questions,\nsame order, one per step, with a clickable rail, Back/Next and a review\nlisting every choice with a link back to the step that made it. The\nthree side-by-side facets are gone: a drill-down is a tree, and a grid\nof dependent controls was a shape you had to already understand to use.\nThe plan stays on screen at every step, which is the one thing a stepper\nmust not take away. Which steps exist is derived in `steps.js` from the\nsame tree, so \"a step with one answer is not a step\" is the terminal''s\nrule run over the browser''s data — the frontend shape is one question\nend to end in both.\n\nStepping back keeps what still fits: shape backend → fullstack with Java\n+ Spring lands on `fullstack-spring`, and coming out of a product into a\nbackend carries the half of its entrypoints a backend can still take.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NM2iUsxKZSvhxkkietLwuB","tree":{"sha":"9a37e25752808393b4099b0243d45907a6989963","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/9a37e25752808393b4099b0243d45907a6989963"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/0ac2f38abf51a4bacf3023e61a30e510fbb5b735","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"ht