a1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd","sha":"1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd"}],"sha":"85ef8f9f0b304e533701165a9551189ce6a3637c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/85ef8f9f0b304e533701165a9551189ce6a3637c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T05:25:01Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T05:25:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(compatibility): declared incompatibility, read twice (#120)\n\nAn incompatibility between capabilities becomes a declaration instead\nof a hand-written check, and the engine reads every declaration from\nboth ends: to refuse an assembly, and to keep the offending choice off\nthe menu. A rule stated once cannot have those two answers disagree.\n\nA `Conflict` names a combination of tags that must never be assembled,\nand why. `{ when: [a, b] }` is a mutual exclusion; `{ when: [a],\nunless: [b] }` is a requirement spelled as its violation. The\nevaluation is a `Predicate`''s with the polarity flipped — `violatedBy`\nis `matches` with the fields renamed — so one glob grammar and one\nmatcher serve both, with no second matcher to drift. It stays a\nseparate type because `matches` returning false means \"this piece does\nnot apply\", which is ordinary, where a conflict matching means \"this\nmust not be built\", which is an error.\n\nRules are declared by the piece that owns them: `Stack` and `Vertical`\neach gained a `conflicts` field, and `conflictsOf` gathers them\nstructurally, so `compatibility.ts` names neither type. Never a central\ntable — a central table is precisely what a plugin-supplied preset\ncannot extend.\n\nRefused: `keel new` checks the tag set its dials settled after the last\ndial and before the first file; `keel add` checks a vertical against\nthe manifest''s tags. Both go through `assemblyRefusal` and report every\nviolation with the rule''s own sentence, the tags that matched and the\nrule id, under `keel.incompatible`.\n\nFiltered, from that same sentence: the build-system dial (some layout\nmust still complete it legally), the module-layout dial (exact, with\nthe build system in hand), the peer-context question, the `--with`\nmenu, and the drill-down — whose three steps are guarded at once,\nbeing one walk over the same set. `keel.catalog` reads the same filter,\nso `keel ui`''s facets and the terminal wizard offer the same presets. A\npreset is hidden only when every setting of its dials is refused.\n\nThe first rule to move is the peer context''s: `--with-peer-context`\nneeds the modulith layout. As a hand-written branch it had the refusal\nand not the menu, so the choice was offered under the flat layout and\nthen rejected. Its code changes from keel.invalid-peer-context to\nkeel.incompatible; the separate \"this stack has no peer-context\nadapter\" capability probe keeps the old code and now asks its question\nagainst the layout that creates the seam.\n\nAlso reconciles with main''s `coverageGap`: `resolveVertical` now throws\nfrom it rather than reporting only which dimension was empty, so the\nrefusal a user runs into and the one a front door shows ahead of time\ncannot differ.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WwxNnPnvSHhvXcRDzd2WtT","tree":{"sha":"bdb11d4b4f2450a961eecdd3decf70e6e9efa0da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/bdb11d4b4f2450a961eecdd3decf70e6e9efa0da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd","verification":{"payload":"tree bdb11d4b4f2450a961eecdd3decf70e6e9efa0da\nparent 824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787462701 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787462701 +0200\n\nfeat(compatibility): declared incompatibility, read twice (#120)\n\nAn incompatibility between capabilities becomes a declaration instead\nof a hand-written check, and the engine reads every declaration from\nboth ends: to refuse an assembly, and to keep the offending choice off\nthe menu. A rule stated once cannot have those two answers disagree.\n\nA `Conflict` names a combination of tags that must never be assembled,\nand why. `{ when: [a, b] }` is a mutual exclusion; `{ when: [a],\nunless: [b] }` is a requirement spelled as its violation. The\nevaluation is a `Predicate`''s with the polarity flipped — `violatedBy`\nis `matches` with the fields renamed — so one glob grammar and one\nmatcher serve both, with no second matcher to drift. It stays a\nseparate type because `matches` returning false means \"this piece does\nnot apply\", which is ordinary, where a conflict matching means \"this\nmust not be built\", which is an error.\n\nRules are declared by the piece that owns them: `Stack` and `Vertical`\neach gained a `conflicts` field, and `conflictsOf` gathers them\nstructurally, so `compatibility.ts` names neither type. Never a central\ntable — a central table is precisely what a plugin-supplied preset\ncannot extend.\n\nRefused: `keel new` checks the tag set its dials settled after the last\ndial and before the first file; `keel add` checks a vertical against\nthe manifest''s tags. Both go through `assemblyRefusal` and report every\nviolation with the rule''s own sentence, the tags that matched and the\nrule id, under `keel.incompatible`.\n\nFiltered, from that same sentence: the build-system dial (some layout\nmust still complete it legally), the module-layout dial (exact, with\nthe build system in hand), the peer-context question, the `--with`\nmenu, and the drill-down — whose three steps are guarded at once,\nbeing one walk over the same set. `keel.catalog` reads the same filter,\nso `keel ui`''s facets and the terminal wizard offer the same presets. A\npreset is hidden only when every setting of its dials is refused.\n\nThe first rule to move is the peer context''s: `--with-peer-context`\nneeds the modulith layout. As a hand-written branch it had the refusal\nand not the menu, so the choice was offered under the flat layout and\nthen rejected. Its code changes from keel.invalid-peer-context to\nkeel.incompatible; the separate \"this stack has no peer-context\nadapter\" capability probe keeps the old code and now asks its question\nagainst the layout that creates the seam.\n\nAlso reconciles with main''s `coverageGap`: `resolveVertical` now throws\nfrom it rather than reporting only which dimension was empty, so the\nrefusal a user runs into and the one a front door shows ahead of time\ncannot differ.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WwxNnPnvSHhvXcRDzd2WtT","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqioQtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyTQQAId5XdK5N/y7+kMT2s555DWG\ngMlwd4s+bmsGOl1qLoqEhW1bj7WS7oDVSLUKg+xylHhm3glKwvbqCAk06QLW3X2f\nsgcUx4xfgkA0FKSlSUquRNenGVYjYEamJYMk3oDKJCivakPP0f30h5iKVjq+AuUo\nYZHFnmeM6uw3tNffepoeRHMJMavOSRYkb/B2VjvT5MP3CLGep1fYGmmq8RXFvnoN\nu+6Frau/MVzTYGBeDk98MRXmbpQvfbcP/VHF9fu+5MQXSHyNTD5yUpZi99LrX2Ja\nJiU7ebOAvScsXlppO3GipsjMkYWzCXFQ8V4zv5I8/iE4N+uQx0r40/sjwFDDXmnE\n8S8FAPtty6YtBWXW8Y3xktje7FucIiH54wtlEjCc7TE5ZynIVPzKSC5T2wJMGfQx\nK2iP/dsaw5t+B8kKUtEwXbkUbzoOaPHenhHtZvAL+XtMeqEO6sgNi5J2ZGdxQ7m+\nM2V08x5A874+XfIXwrJuRkhWbXv3yZybSO8WNm+dncD+xMgRKLBlFy7Ycmq6RxYK\n68tZXBMGm9sIRUz0R3GFR0WDIHhzAx0PuwqDDfRJM7w5aAcxgCBVp1HGX4A3H4v7\nXxl0gUIOVH6V30FFaxq9AZXmK6c9n6Dds/ti+NMNGjIgS/DNnLbYeiJHjpfh3Ku/\nasMVyQ3i/JUrzrKY/pHq\n=tVas\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-23T05:25:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE5NDBlZTNkYmRlNWFmYWExZWY5NDE3Y2U4MjU3NmZkYWJhOTdjY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246","sha":"824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246"}],"sha":"1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1940ee3dbde5afaa1ef9417ce82576fdaba97ccd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:12:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:36:44Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: the ui suite finishes inside the web shard''s floor, not far inside it\n\nThe claim shipped as \"an order of magnitude inside the floor\", which\nwas a laptop reading. On the runner the suite takes roughly twice as\nlong — its `beforeAll` compiles `dist/` and launches a browser, and\nboth cost more there — against a shard floor that is `add-module-wc`.\nIt is comfortably inside it and nowhere near becoming it, but the\nquantity was wrong.\n\nRestated qualitatively, which is the form §9 keeps its sharding\nguidance in since the measurements came out of it: finishes inside the\nfloor rather than becoming it, and re-measure on the shape you ship.","tree":{"sha":"4889e98595985afd4010db3904675d36efbbe368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/4889e98595985afd4010db3904675d36efbbe368"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDgyNDM0OWEyNDQ3YzVkNjA5NTE3N2UxNmQwODhkYmFkZWJjN2MyNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b","sha":"fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b"}],"sha":"824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/824349a2447c5d6095177e16d088dbadebc7c246"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:59:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:36:44Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"fix(test): resolve the probed browser to an absolute path for Playwright\n\nThe shared probe answers with a bare command name when it finds one on\nPATH — `google-chrome` on a GitHub-hosted runner, which has no\nPlaywright download layout. That is enough for the other browser-driven\nsuites: they hand it to `spawn`, which resolves through PATH.\n\nPlaywright does not. `browserType.launch` stats `executablePath`\nagainst the working directory and refuses a name it cannot find there,\nso the `web` shard would have failed on the very box the probe was\nwritten for while passing everywhere a download layout exists — the\nworse of the two ways round.\n\nResolved in the suite rather than in the probe: the two consumers want\ndifferent things from it, and widening it would hide that.","tree":{"sha":"d3c1031efcac141a3db3f09907bbcbb8b414c967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/d3c1031efcac141a3db3f09907bbcbb8b414c967"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGZkMzkxOTU3YzM1NzgzMGUxYTY1ZmNiZDhmYTM1NGNkMTk1YmZmNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141","sha":"6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141"}],"sha":"fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/fd391957c357830e1a65fcbd8fa354cd195bff5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:53:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:36:44Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: the keel ui browser suite in CHANGELOG and AGENTS §9\n\nCHANGELOG gets the entry under `Added`, beside the facets it covers.\nAGENTS §9 gets a bullet: one browser-driven `keel ui` suite, not a\ncell, riding the `web` shard — and what it covers that the pure\ntests cannot.\n\nThe shard''s own comments carried two counts this change moves: three\nsuites render in Chromium, now four, and `web` carried fourteen files,\nnow fifteen.","tree":{"sha":"9a42f4567c88adf57626ab36c480cd95d9c413ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/9a42f4567c88adf57626ab36c480cd95d9c413ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDY2ODE4OThkMmFkMjViNzMwYzllMjZhMGRhNWM1N2EzMGQ0ZTMxNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f","sha":"0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f"}],"sha":"6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/6681898d2ad25b730c9e26a0da5c57a30d4e3141"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:52:48Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T19:36:44Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"test(e2e): drive the keel ui stack finder in a real browser\n\nThe three facets shipped verified by hand in Chromium and never\ncommitted as a test. Their narrowing is pure and unit-tested\n(`finder.test.ts`), the tree they walk is tested where it is built\n(`catalog.test.ts`) — but nothing had ever loaded the page, and the\npart between the two is where the risk lives: `<keel-new-form>`\nrebuilds its subtree on every change and `<keel-app>` replaces the\nelement itself, so every claim about keeping a choice is a claim\nabout surviving a DOM replacement.\n\n`tests/e2e/ui-stack-finder.test.ts` spawns `keel ui --port 0`, reads\nthe URL and token the CLI prints, and drives the page with\nPlaywright. Spawning the binary rather than calling `uiServer()` is\ndeliberate: the token in that URL is the page''s only credential, and\na suite minting its own would prove the router accepts a token it was\nhanded, not that the CLI hands the browser one that works.\n\nEight cases: the form opens on `quarkus-cli` and not on the catalog''s\nalphabetically first entry; a language move keeps the entrypoints and\nframework, including off their defaults — from the defaults a move\nlands on the same preset whether it carried anything or not, so that\ncase alone passes a dropped carry-over; ticking the second adapter\ngives the composed preset with no repository-layout control in sight;\nclearing the last checked adapter is refused and the box snaps back;\n`go` drops the framework facet and `typescript@browser` drops both;\nand the `fullstack` product shows the language placeholder and comes\nback out of it. A `pageerror` or `console.error` anywhere in a case\nfails it, in `afterEach` where it cannot be forgotten.\n\nThree details that are load bearing:\n\n  - The refusal case clicks the checkbox for real. Playwright''s\n    `.uncheck()` asserts the box ends up unchecked and would time out\n    for precisely the reason the case exists.\n  - Every interaction waits for the page''s network to go quiet before\n    the next one. `<keel-app>` answers a change twice — synchronously,\n    then when the debounced preview returns, which replaces the form\n    element — and a control acted on between the two dispatches its\n    event from a node about to be detached, where it never reaches\n    the app.\n  - `beforeAll` compiles `dist/`, since `bin/keel.js` loads it and the\n    e2e job installs without building.\n\n`skipE2E()` is the shared opt-in rule with no package manager in it,\nfor a suite that runs none. The browser guard sits on the `describe`\nrather than each `it`: every case here needs Chromium and `beforeAll`\nlaunches it.\n\nThe suite joins the existing `web` shard, which already declares\n`browser` in `tools:`; it runs in ~21s against that shard''s ~110s\nfloor.","tree":{"sha":"85c7de6c930a82b47f69c328bbdf223f37ffc7d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/85c7de6c930a82b47f69c328bbdf223f37ffc7d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDBhOGVmMmMwOTNkMzM2N2ZmMTYwOWE1N2M1YzQ4ODM2NWFmYzhkNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38","sha":"d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38"}],"sha":"0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0a8ef2c093d3367ff1609a57c5c488365afc8d5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:08:50Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:39:56Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: the front door''s refusals, and what a vertical promotes\n\nCHANGELOG under [Unreleased] (the `--with` entry it belongs to is\nitself unreleased, so this extends it rather than opening a Fixed\nsection), `docs/cli.md` with the two refusals and the example, and\n`docs/composition.md` with `Vertical.promotes` and why the\ndeclaration exists. The verticals catalog already listed the\n\"`distribution` first\" prerequisites; it now says that \"first\" is an\norder inside one `keel new --with` run, not a second run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSoeTdHg1bpVfYiKhkHZB1","tree":{"sha":"58788386ffee95186ace399a150ed5a521fd0382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/58788386ffee95186ace399a150ed5a521fd0382"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGQxNjM5MDAyZDA2MzY4OTIxOWU1NTQ2MjU4MjI2YzdlZTZjNmZhMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4","sha":"b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4"}],"sha":"d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d1639002d063689219e5546258226c7ee6c6fa38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:07:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:39:56Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"feat(cli): refuse an uncoverable --with vertical at the front door\n\n`keel new --stack=quarkus-cli --with persistence` validated the id,\nthe duplicates and the overlap with the stack''s own list, then asked\nevery remaining question before dying on a thrown `ResolutionError`\n(\"no adapter covers dimension(s): datasource\"). The menu never offers\nthat choice; the flag accepted it and paid for it eight questions\nlater.\n\nIt cannot be fixed with the menu''s probe. `coversFor` is conservative\nby construction — it sees the tags it is given, not the ones an\nadapter promotes at install time — and conservatism that only hides a\nmenu entry becomes a wrong answer the moment it refuses a command:\n`--with containerization,distribution,iac` is a legal composition on\na REST stack precisely because `distribution` promotes the\n`dist.container-image` tag `iac` is keyed on, and a flat probe rejects\nit.\n\nSo the check walks the extras the way the install runs them — in the\norder named, each against the tags its predecessors promote, seeded\nwith what the stack''s own verticals promote on their way past. Three\noutcomes, and the middle one is why the walk is ordered rather than a\nset operation: covered at its turn; uncovered now but covered once a\nlater extra has run, which is a misordering and is refused naming the\nextra to list it after; or uncovered whatever the rest of the list\ndoes, which is refused naming the dimension and the tag that would\nhave covered it.\n\nThe resolver''s throw stays a throw and stays out of scope: it escapes\n`installVertical` from every caller (`keel add containerization` on a\nCLI project does the same), so converting it is a decision about\nevery escape from the install engine — `ContributionConflictError`\nand the adapters'' own plain `Error`s included — not about `--with`.\nThis path no longer reaches it, and refuses with more than it could\nhave said.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSoeTdHg1bpVfYiKhkHZB1","tree":{"sha":"d813cc8efce20f3b0fe76d38b5c786d8e27bcbe7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/d813cc8efce20f3b0fe76d38b5c786d8e27bcbe7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGI0ODAxODMxYWQzODA1M2E0YTNmODk4MTQ0MTI0Y2Y3NzcxZGY2YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f","sha":"2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f"}],"sha":"b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/b4801831ad38053a4a3f898144124cf7771df6b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:06:20Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:39:56Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"feat(resolver): report why a vertical does not cover, not just that it does not\n\n`coversFor` answers yes/no, which is all a menu needs — an option it\nprunes says nothing and needs to say nothing. A refusal is the other\nhalf: it has to name the vertical, the dimension no adapter covered,\nand what would have covered it.\n\n`coverageGap` is the same check with that reason attached — null when\nthe vertical resolves, otherwise the uncovered dimensions plus the\ntags that would close them. The enablers are the unmet `requires` of\nthe adapter *nearest* to matching, per uncovered dimension: the union\nover every candidate is a list of every stack shape keel supports,\nwhich tells a user nothing, where the nearest adapter on a CLI preset\nis missing only `arch.server-http` — the whole answer. Adapters an\n`excludes` entry rules out are skipped, since no tag un-matches one.\n\n`coversFor` becomes `coverageGap(...) === null`, so the two cannot\ndisagree.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSoeTdHg1bpVfYiKhkHZB1","tree":{"sha":"3048cb935e9959e09759435b74a54107e73e3ec0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/3048cb935e9959e09759435b74a54107e73e3ec0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDI2NDFjMDc1ZGFlNWEzYTE2NWQwMjAwM2M2Nzc0YjY4YjNjMjkwMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb","sha":"7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb"}],"sha":"2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/2641c075dae5a3a165d02003c6774b68b3c2901f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:04:58Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T18:39:56Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"feat(composition): declare the tags a vertical may promote\n\n`Contribution.tagsAdd` is a runtime fact: an adapter promotes\n`dist.container-image` while it renders, so nothing reasoning *before*\nan install can see it. A front door checking `keel new --with\ndistribution,iac` needs to — `iac` is keyed on exactly that tag — so\n`Vertical.promotes` states it statically: the union over the\nvertical''s adapters, including the tags only some answers produce\n(either image flavor, every SQL engine, either CI provider, either\ncloud).\n\nOver-declaring is safe; it only defers a refusal to the resolver.\nUnder-declaring would refuse a legal composition, and nothing about\nwriting `tagsAdd` in an adapter makes an author revisit a list in\nanother file — so `installVertical` checks each contribution against\nthe declaration where the two meet and throws on a tag no vertical\nclaims. An undeclared tag is a keel bug, not a user error, so it\nthrows rather than travelling as an `Err`.\n\nEight verticals promote: walking-skeleton, code-style, dev-container,\ncontainerization, distribution, ci, iac, persistence. Each declares\nfrom the constants its adapters already promote from, so the two\ncannot drift by editing one — which also gave `iac` an `IAC_CLOUDS`\nlist its own validation now reads, and `ci` a `CI_PROVIDER_TAGS`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSoeTdHg1bpVfYiKhkHZB1","tree":{"sha":"8e69681fcdb1e87b2850d63663e044f2c5b9476e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/8e69681fcdb1e87b2850d63663e044f2c5b9476e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDc1NThlNGU2ZjcxZjYyYWQ4Y2E0NGYwMTNmMTljMzUzMTlkMzBiY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf","sha":"ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf"}],"sha":"7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7558e4e6f71f62ad8ca44f013f19c35319d30bcb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:57:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:17:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: drop the CI timing measurements from the guidance\n\nAGENTS.md §9, the `ci.yml` shard comments and `docs/development.md`\nhad accumulated a running log of runner measurements — wall clocks,\ntest totals, per-file breakdowns, divisors, run numbers — one round of\nwhich this branch added. Each entry was written to justify one\nsharding call and then stayed, so the sections had drifted into\nmeasurement narrative with the rules embedded in it, and the numbers\noutnumbered the guidance they existed to support.\n\nThe decisions survive; the evidence for them does not. What a\ncontributor needs is that the matrix floor is a named shard and a new\none should finish inside it, that splitting a file with a cold cache\nbehind it makes things worse, that Maven''s half of the add-module grid\nis the cheap half, that a laptop reads optimistically and you\nre-measure on the shape you ship. None of that needs a figure to be\nactionable, and every figure went stale on the next commit that\ntouched a suite — this file already carried one shard''s timings under\na note saying the shape they described no longer ships.\n\nStructural counts stay, because they define the grids rather than\ndescribe a run: 24 modulith cells, 21 combo cells, 12 stacks × 2 build\nsystems. One of those was already wrong and is corrected here — the\nmatrix has 40 `jvm-*` shards and a `web-combo`, where §9 still said 33\nand named `web` alone.\n\nThe mutation baseline in `docs/development.md` is left alone: it is a\nquality metric the mutation section exists to report, not a sharding\nmeasurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn1UZHtzVsQAqH5LdoB3UT","tree":{"sha":"c79c80df677d701dfdce1b358b1c64305e2a5621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/c79c80df677d701dfdce1b358b1c64305e2a5621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGJhMTYxMDA5NzdiM2Q4ZjgxNjVjNzgwZWM5YWY5MWZhYjEzZjc0Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65","sha":"aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65"}],"sha":"ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ba16100977b3d8f8165c780ec9af91fab13f74cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:17:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:17:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: runner figures for the combo grid, replacing the local ones\n\nThe grid''s first green e2e run (32574792585) is the first time these\nshards have been measured anywhere but a 4-vCPU box, and the test plan\nsaid to read the real numbers off it.\n\n`jvm-combo-quarkus-java`: 265.02s wall, 655.35s of test time across\nthree files, longest `combo-basic-quarkus-cli-rest-gradle` at 263.05s,\n307s as a job. The six shards span 174–307s as jobs against a matrix\nfloor of `jvm-modulith-quarkus-java` at 436s, so the six-shards-not-\neighteen decision holds on the runner and not only locally.\n`web-combo`: 35.82s wall, 53s as a job.\n\nTwo things the runner said that the laptop did not. The shard''s two\nGradle cells are within 1.7s of each other, so no file is its floor\nand splitting one out would buy nothing. And the local run had the\n*other* Gradle cell longest, at 227.55s — a box ~15% faster that\nreorders a tie the runner reorders back. AGENTS.md keeps both, since\nthe re-measure-on-the-shape-you-ship rule is easier to follow with a\nlive example than as a principle.\n\nAGENTS.md also never carried its figures at all: the estimate it\nshipped with (\"~120–190s cold on a 4-core box\") was unlabelled and\nunmeasured, where ci.yml and docs/development.md both marked theirs\nlocal. Corrected here rather than left to look like a third\nmeasurement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn1UZHtzVsQAqH5LdoB3UT","tree":{"sha":"f8cb34a277e662324795c3c8fc762ed12e56cc37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/f8cb34a277e662324795c3c8fc762ed12e56cc37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGFhMDYxNTIxMzMwMTU4ZTcyM2ZmM2E2NzZmZGQxNjQxYjI1ZDFiNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6","sha":"19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6"}],"sha":"aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/aa061521330158e723ff3a676fdd1641b25d1b65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:04:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:17:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"docs: the composed-entrypoint e2e grid and why its halves differ\n\nAGENTS.md §9 documents each grid''s shape and the reasoning behind it,\nso a contributor adding a stack knows which cells they owe. The combo\ngrid needed its own entry for two reasons that are easy to read as\ninconsistency otherwise: it covers `modulith` exhaustively and `basic`\nat one build per stack, and it shards by framework × language where\nthe `add-module` grid one bullet down shards by cell.\n\nBoth are recorded with the measurement that decided them, and both\nfigures are flagged **local** rather than runner — this file''s other\nnumbers are runner numbers and mixing the two misleads. The 406s the\nslowest modulith cell reaches under eight-way contention is recorded\nnext to the 225s it takes in its shipped three-file shard, as a fresh\nexample of the standing rule that you re-measure on the shape you\nintend to ship.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn1UZHtzVsQAqH5LdoB3UT","tree":{"sha":"7ceb69656f1633e309754f1045a953f8b2f47aa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/7ceb69656f1633e309754f1045a953f8b2f47aa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE5ZTU4NmE2OTMwYWUyZDljZGEwYTljZWFhMGM0YjY3MTQ1YWE4ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f","sha":"24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f"}],"sha":"19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/19e586a6930ae2d9cda0a9ceaa0c4b67145aa8d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:03:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:17:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"test(e2e): build every composed-entrypoint cell for real\n\n`grep -rn \"cli-rest\\|cli-http\" tests/e2e/` returned nothing. Ninety-six\nsuites, and not one scaffolded a two-entrypoint hexagon under either\nmodule layout — every claim about composed entrypoints was asserted by\nreading emitted files, and no `gradle`, `mvn`, `npm` or `pnpm` had ever\ncompiled or installed one. Per AGENTS.md §9 that is silent\nnon-coverage: the check names promise a grid the suites do not\npopulate.\n\nTwenty-one cells, one file each, named\n`combo-<layout>-<stack>-<build>.test.ts` so \"every cell has a suite\" is\ncheckable from `ls`.\n\n**The modulith half is exhausted, the basic half sampled.** Modulith is\n6 JVM combo stacks × Gradle and Maven, plus `ts-cli-http` × npm and\npnpm — 14 cells, and it is the half issue #108 is about:\n`jvm-shared-root-modulith.ts` and `ts-shared-root.ts`''s modulith branch\nshipped without a build ever touching them. Basic takes one build per\nstack (7), the build system alternating so both appear against each\nframework and each language, and the TypeScript sample taking pnpm\nbecause its isolated store refuses an undeclared dependency npm''s\nhoisting hides. PR #110 built the whole basic half by hand before\nshipping, so what was missing there was a standing check, not a first\nlook — and the 14 modulith cells re-exercise the shared seed builders\nin `jvm-shared-root.ts` on every run regardless. What is basic-only is\nthe per-arch module list and the README shape, and one build per stack\npins those.\n\n**Every cell ends in a runtime entrypoint check.** A green compile is\nnot the claim; both entrypoints reachable off one hexagon is. The JVM\ncells build once — both assemblies are modules of the same reactor —\nthen run the CLI jar for its greeting and boot the REST jar for the\nwire contract, through the drive steps the single-entrypoint cells\nuse. The TypeScript cells have no build step, so they install for\nreal, run the emitted `typecheck`/`test`/`lint`, then run both\n`main.ts` files off that one `node_modules`. Each cell also asserts\nthe root build file registers every module exactly once, which is the\nregression the shared-root upsert exists to prevent and the one thing\na scaffold-and-read test cannot see.\n\n**Six shards plus `web-combo`, not twenty-one jobs.** This follows the\n`jvm-modulith-*` convention (framework × language), not the\n`jvm-add-module-*` one. A job per cell earned its keep there because\nthose cells run inside the 371s matrix floor with room to spare; a\ncombo cell builds two assemblies. Measured on the shape that ships —\n`jvm-combo-quarkus-java` run exactly as declared, locally on 4 vCPUs\nwith cold caches: 227.55s wall, 546.98s of test time across three\nfiles, longest file at 225.43s. Still inside the floor, so these\nshards cost no wall clock, where twenty-one would buy twenty-one cold\nJDK+Gradle provisions for a red X that framework × language already\nnames. `web-combo` is 41.81s wall and gets a shard of its own because\nits cells render nothing, so probing for Chromium would misdescribe\nthem.\n\nAll 21 cells verified green locally against JDK 25.0.3, Gradle 9.7.0,\nMaven 3.9.11, npm and pnpm.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn1UZHtzVsQAqH5LdoB3UT","tree":{"sha":"2f40ac81d1818f3bc58c02ce710f8c65259faac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/2f40ac81d1818f3bc58c02ce710f8c65259faac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDI0YjA3MmU0NDNkM2M4YzI3OGMwMTU0NWQ5ZWM3NzY5MDI3MjM4M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8","sha":"33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8"}],"sha":"24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/24b072e443d3c8c278c01545d9ec77690272383f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T13:02:04Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:17:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"refactor(test): lift the drive steps out of the JVM and web e2e harnesses\n\nA composed-entrypoint cell runs two entrypoints off one project, so it\nneeds what a CLI cell does after the build and what a REST cell does\nafter the build — but it cannot call either `runJvm*E2E`, because both\nscaffold and build first. Written fresh it would spell those two\ncontracts a second time, and a paraphrase of \"the picocli wiring found\nthe command\" is a second claim rather than the same one.\n\nSo the halves come out where the combo harness can call them.\n`driveCliJar` runs a packaged jar against an argv and asserts its\nstdout; `driveRestJar` boots one on an ephemeral port and drives the\nwhole `/greet` wire contract — named, defaulted and rejected requests,\nboth probes, the correlation id echoed and minted. `runJvmCliE2E` and\n`runJvmRestE2E` now end by calling them, so the existing 40-odd cells\nassert byte-identical things and the combo cells cannot drift from\nthem. `JvmCliE2ESpec`/`JvmRestE2ESpec` keep their shape by extending\nthe extracted contract interfaces.\n\nThe other half is the scaffold. Both e2e scaffolds answered exactly\none bootstrap adapter by id, which is right while one entrypoint means\none bootstrap. A combo tag set resolves two, and they declare the same\n`basePackage`/`projectName` (`npmScope`/`projectName` on Node);\n`sharesAnswersWith` reconciles what one of them was *asked*, which a\nnon-interactive run never is. Answering both by id is deterministic\nwhichever the resolver reaches first, and the cost of the alternative\nis every module''s `<parent>` naming an artifactId the reactor root\ndoes not have.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gn1UZHtzVsQAqH5LdoB3UT","tree":{"sha":"04527528a04a6487d5bb2b6a66af17739227b6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/04527528a04a6487d5bb2b6a66af17739227b6af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDMzNDEzZTNlM2ZiNjEzODNmZjMxMTA2NjI3ODk0ZWVmM2Y3NTFhZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b","sha":"16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b"}],"sha":"33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/33413e3e3fb61383ff31106627894eef3f751af8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:03:29Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T17:03:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: the keel new drill-down — language → adapters → framework → verticals (#115)\n\n`keel new` asked for the stack as one flat select over 33 preset ids.\nKnowing you want \"Kotlin, a CLI and an HTTP endpoint, on Spring\" is\neasy; knowing that is spelled `spring-cli-rest-kotlin` is not. It now\nnarrows to it three questions at a time — language → user-side adapters\n→ framework — plus a fourth step for extra verticals, in the terminal\nand in `keel ui` alike.\n\n**Multi-select on the `Prompt` port.** A `Question` may declare\n`kind: ''multi-select''`; the terminal adapter renders it as an inquirer\n`checkbox`. The answer stays a string — the chosen values comma-joined,\n`encodeSelection`/`decodeSelection` at both ends — so `Prompt.ask` still\nreturns `Promise<string>` and sticky memory, `--set`, the wizard''s\nreplay and `keel ui`''s form all keep working unchanged. A mechanism\noutside the Question flow would have put set answers beyond\n`WizardPrompt` (invisible to the review step) and beyond\n`keel.preview` (unrenderable by the UI).\n\n**The drill-down** (`domain/core/stack-wizard.ts`) derives every menu\nfrom the tags of the presets still reachable. Picking two adapters\nresolves to the composed preset — one project, one domain, both\nentrypoints — never a two-service product. Framework is asked only\nwhere a choice remains, which today means the JVM.\n\nThe language node is qualified by its `runtime.*` tag, and that is the\nload-bearing decision: a checkbox can express any subset of what it\nshows, so `{cli, server-http, spa}` under one TypeScript node would put\nthree unreachable pairings on the menu. Split into `typescript@node`\nand `typescript@browser`, every entry resolves. `entrypointStep`\nverifies that rather than assuming it, falling back to spelled-out\ncombinations where a language''s subsets are incomplete.\n\n**`--with`, and the extra-verticals step.** `extraVerticals` existed\nonly for a composite stack''s services; the single-service path now\nthreads it. The menu is pruned twice — the stack''s own verticals, and\nanything this project cannot cover, via the new `coversFor` (the\nresolver''s coverage check asked ahead of time and answered rather than\nthrown).\n\n**`keel ui` gets the same three controls as facets**, driven by a new\n`finder` on `keel.catalog`: a tree of language → combination →\nframework built by the same `stack-wizard.ts` functions. The page walks\nit and never sees a capability tag. `finder.defaultStack` reports the\ndefault preset whole rather than per facet — recomposing it picked\n`micronaut` over `quarkus`, since the framework facet is alphabetical.\n\nFlag-suppression is preserved: `--stack` skips the discovery questions,\n`--with` skips the fourth, `--yes` stays fully non-interactive, and\nevery default composes to `quarkus-cli` as before.\n\nCloses #109.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VjAE5D8bDNiC8wGx8ES6xY","tree":{"sha":"3dcfa87213acc46f2196c646c3cc701a35dd7647","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/3dcfa87213acc46f2196c646c3cc701a35dd7647"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3dcfa87213acc46f2196c646c3cc701a35dd7647\nparent ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787418209 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787418209 +0200\n\nfeat: the keel new drill-down — language → adapters → framework → verticals (#115)\n\n`keel new` asked for the stack as one flat select over 33 preset ids.\nKnowing you want \"Kotlin, a CLI and an HTTP endpoint, on Spring\" is\neasy; knowing that is spelled `spring-cli-rest-kotlin` is not. It now\nnarrows to it three questions at a time — language → user-side adapters\n→ framework — plus a fourth step for extra verticals, in the terminal\nand in `keel ui` alike.\n\n**Multi-select on the `Prompt` port.** A `Question` may declare\n`kind: ''multi-select''`; the terminal adapter renders it as an inquirer\n`checkbox`. The answer stays a string — the chosen values comma-joined,\n`encodeSelection`/`decodeSelection` at both ends — so `Prompt.ask` still\nreturns `Promise<string>` and sticky memory, `--set`, the wizard''s\nreplay and `keel ui`''s form all keep working unchanged. A mechanism\noutside the Question flow would have put set answers beyond\n`WizardPrompt` (invisible to the review step) and beyond\n`keel.preview` (unrenderable by the UI).\n\n**The drill-down** (`domain/core/stack-wizard.ts`) derives every menu\nfrom the tags of the presets still reachable. Picking two adapters\nresolves to the composed preset — one project, one domain, both\nentrypoints — never a two-service product. Framework is asked only\nwhere a choice remains, which today means the JVM.\n\nThe language node is qualified by its `runtime.*` tag, and that is the\nload-bearing decision: a checkbox can express any subset of what it\nshows, so `{cli, server-http, spa}` under one TypeScript node would put\nthree unreachable pairings on the menu. Split into `typescript@node`\nand `typescript@browser`, every entry resolves. `entrypointStep`\nverifies that rather than assuming it, falling back to spelled-out\ncombinations where a language''s subsets are incomplete.\n\n**`--with`, and the extra-verticals step.** `extraVerticals` existed\nonly for a composite stack''s services; the single-service path now\nthreads it. The menu is pruned twice — the stack''s own verticals, and\nanything this project cannot cover, via the new `coversFor` (the\nresolver''s coverage check asked ahead of time and answered rather than\nthrown).\n\n**`keel ui` gets the same three controls as facets**, driven by a new\n`finder` on `keel.catalog`: a tree of language → combination →\nframework built by the same `stack-wizard.ts` functions. The page walks\nit and never sees a capability tag. `finder.defaultStack` reports the\ndefault preset whole rather than per facet — recomposing it picked\n`micronaut` over `quarkus`, since the framework facet is alphabetical.\n\nFlag-suppression is preserved: `--stack` skips the discovery questions,\n`--with` skips the fourth, `--yes` stays fully non-interactive, and\nevery default composes to `quarkus-cli` as before.\n\nCloses #109.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VjAE5D8bDNiC8wGx8ES6xY","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqidZhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkNEQAG7azmEQg0JMC9d/vCmeYYye\nreRcY05YKeWDIqs5mdm8yO+KhBd6Ohx7Vobq9EMolgU5ex3fRneM/CX4l2ox5imB\nkf59zj+qsU10lFiOyW2Y8GLzRLq2cMbpaV2Ng6Bk2Dx1Xy7aLLY86W1pE6my/w+E\nvvuRNWd5OZR8zK36bmU8qil88CLDXLgbhsKYXUa8mdgl7fjr/ODxxfI7pNK1l+VD\n4igMC1Lmoy4ZsG+b+xHE2tSZuaIePICcGTEITFx5d3xZ9sIMqveqoiZTd6WfN8Yi\nJhDsdyxeMt0UChziEHSL8ccLNWt/UZsNpnpPQ8l9rEwLBOguNHqVXyvlqCz9jp69\n1VxZgDJRPSvA6+xEpkFED9RXTUfdbjYSbHsDM/8/sbdBs5WvP8To7fIoKLSdiXLQ\njC6R+8X981jwuit3e1c3nbEOM5mOjsjTJyH8yRSrwj/trF2QmFyNGl7TuK7Dk0fR\nDOYpYEnhOl3yVwgY5yA0m8gEN1KawkQbEpf+O9UgE8H4Q960xSGqzxQRPub0hEM6\nZuI5UW4Xme/Fe0c5LbbVS9ggA1GwK6Qz92QaiM6vcUXpI53Q6FRtFwlF8Xi0Dx5a\nYySONwp+XUzCmc9CM5I5T+s+QnbPEI0Bfi3jVSwMJWBNejHCcoBB3cX0IhrAt/Gl\nnREDoolYjeqBaaBkKPKI\n=dvA9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T17:03:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE2ZjgzYjE2MGU0OWJmZGM4NTAzODdjYjNhNzg4ZDI2NzE4YmRmM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d","sha":"ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d"}],"sha":"16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/16f83b160e49bfdc850387cb3a788d26718bdf3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T06:58:56Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T06:58:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): keel ui — the local scaffolder (#114)\n\nA Spring-Initializr-shaped front end for the engine the CLI already\ndrives, served on loopback and stopped with Ctrl-C. Point it at an\nempty directory and it is `keel new`; point it at a keel project and it\nbecomes `keel add` / `keel add module`, offering only what that project\ncan take. What it adds over the wizard is the plan while the choices\nare still moving: the file tree redraws on every change, before\nanything is written.\n\nkeel has no static form to render, and that is the composition model\nrather than an implementation detail — an adapter is asked its\nquestions only once its predicate matched, and a predicate reads tags\nan earlier answer folded in. So `keel.preview` runs the real install as\na dry run with a prompt that answers instead of blocking, and records\nwhat it was asked. It cannot drift from the engine because it is the\nengine.\n\n- A second primary adapter (`src/application/web/`), under the CLI\n  adapter''s dependency rule: `contract/` maps UiRequest → command/query\n  → UiResponse with no `node:http` in it; `executable/` owns the\n  socket. Two dependency-cruiser rules hold the seam.\n- Three queries (`domain/contract/queries.ts`): `keel.catalog`,\n  `keel.preview`, `keel.project-status`. Every field on the last\n  mirrors a refusal a brownfield handler would issue.\n- The page (`assets/web/`): framework-free custom elements on\n  `@rgoussu.dev/planks`, no bundler. `pnpm lint` grew to cover it.\n- Three guards on the loopback port — a per-run token in a custom\n  header, a `Host` allowlist against DNS rebinding, an `Origin`\n  allowlist. No CORS header is ever sent.\n- `Prompt.ask(question, asker)`: a question id is unique within its\n  asker and nowhere else, and the two kinds record answers in\n  different places, so a front end collecting answers cannot route one\n  back without attribution. The `control` kind marks the wizard''s\n  review step as flow control rather than part of the plan.\n- `InstallTarget` + `installCommandFor` name what to install\n  independently of which command carries it, so preview and commit\n  cannot disagree.\n\nDocs: `docs/ui.md`, README section, CLI reference entry, CHANGELOG,\nroadmap item P.","tree":{"sha":"4f6b2ec8a35baedb9206e1b59b983043928eb017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/4f6b2ec8a35baedb9206e1b59b983043928eb017"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/ff920c18820143607148bd19e5138343cff5707d","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f6b2ec8a35baedb9206e1b59b983043928eb017\nparent 8d29dc3e677e2755e476933be38a2e5a94e479e0\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787381936 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787381936 +0200\n\nfeat(ui): keel ui — the local scaffolder (#114)\n\nA Spring-Initializr-shaped front end for the engine the CLI already\ndrives, served on loopback and stopped with Ctrl-C. Point it at an\nempty directory and it is `keel new`; point it at a keel project and it\nbecomes `keel add` / `keel add module`, offering only what that project\ncan take. What it adds over the wizard is the plan while the choices\nare still moving: the file tree redraws on every change, before\nanything is written.\n\nkeel has no static form to render, and that is the composition model\nrather than an implementation detail — an adapter is asked its\nquestions only once its predicate matched, and a predicate reads tags\nan earlier answer folded in. So `keel.preview` runs the real install as\na dry run with a prompt that answers instead of blocking, and records\nwhat it was asked. It cannot drift from the engine because it is the\nengine.\n\n- A second primary adapter (`src/application/web/`), under the CLI\n  adapter''s dependency rule: `contract/` maps UiRequest → command/query\n  → UiResponse with no `node:http` in it; `executable/` owns the\n  socket. Two dependency-cruiser rules hold the seam.\n- Three queries (`domain/contract/queries.ts`): `keel.catalog`,\n  `keel.preview`, `keel.project-status`. Every field on the last\n  mirrors a refusal a brownfield handler would issue.\n- The page (`assets/web/`): framework-free custom elements on\n  `@rgoussu.dev/planks`, no bundler. `pnpm lint` grew to cover it.\n- Three guards on the loopback port — a per-run token in a custom\n  header, a `Host` allowlist against DNS rebinding, an `Origin`\n  allowlist. No CORS header is ever sent.\n- `Prompt.ask(question, asker)`: a question id is unique within its\n  asker and nowhere else, and the two kinds record answers in\n  different places, so a front end collecting answers cannot route one\n  back without attribution. The `control` kind marks the wizard''s\n  review step as flow control rather than part of the plan.\n- `InstallTarget` + `installCommandFor` name what to install\n  independently of which command carries it, so preview and commit\n  cannot disagree.\n\nDocs: `docs/ui.md`, README section, CLI reference entry, CHANGELOG,\nroadmap item P.","reason":"valid","sign