goussu-dev/Keel/commit/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628","sha":"1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628"}],"sha":"444b7f7fc27274111924b422d59a33424377d653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/444b7f7fc27274111924b422d59a33424377d653"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T06:06:15Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T06:06:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(code-style): the code-style vertical — one style model, every dialect (#103)\n\nAdds the `code-style` vertical: an editor layout contract plus each\nstack''s own formatter, all rendered from one style model at generation\ntime rather than through a runtime meta-formatter.\n\n`.editorconfig` reaches the actual formatter in only two of the five\nfamilies keel emits (Kotlin via ktlint, the web family via Prettier);\nJava''s mainstream formatters, gofmt and rustfmt ignore it. So keel\nholds one model and fans it out into each dialect — a real single\nsource of truth with no extra runtime dependency and no added CI time.\n\n- `editor-baseline`: `.editorconfig` + `.gitattributes`, per-language\n  and honest (Go gets hard tabs and no max_line_length).\n- `formatter`: Spotless with prince-of-space (Java) and ktlint\n  (Kotlin), rustfmt.toml, Prettier for the TypeScript stacks and the\n  SPA, nothing at all for Go.\n\nEnforcement is hook-fixes / CI-gates: `isEnforceCheck = false` on\nGradle and no lifecycle binding on Maven, so formatting never fails\nthe build; the pipelines gate on it, keyed on the `style.managed` tag.\n\nMachine-maintained regions that keel later rewrites are fenced with\n`spotless:off` / `spotless:on` plus a do-not-edit warning — without it\nthe formatter reflows the `@ComponentScan` and `@Import` lists and\n`keel add module` can no longer find them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0b59ee2ce284209d3e861275e546ca62e1ac7b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/e0b59ee2ce284209d3e861275e546ca62e1ac7b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628","verification":{"payload":"tree e0b59ee2ce284209d3e861275e546ca62e1ac7b7\nparent 82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787292375 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787292375 +0200\n\nfeat(code-style): the code-style vertical — one style model, every dialect (#103)\n\nAdds the `code-style` vertical: an editor layout contract plus each\nstack''s own formatter, all rendered from one style model at generation\ntime rather than through a runtime meta-formatter.\n\n`.editorconfig` reaches the actual formatter in only two of the five\nfamilies keel emits (Kotlin via ktlint, the web family via Prettier);\nJava''s mainstream formatters, gofmt and rustfmt ignore it. So keel\nholds one model and fans it out into each dialect — a real single\nsource of truth with no extra runtime dependency and no added CI time.\n\n- `editor-baseline`: `.editorconfig` + `.gitattributes`, per-language\n  and honest (Go gets hard tabs and no max_line_length).\n- `formatter`: Spotless with prince-of-space (Java) and ktlint\n  (Kotlin), rustfmt.toml, Prettier for the TypeScript stacks and the\n  SPA, nothing at all for Go.\n\nEnforcement is hook-fixes / CI-gates: `isEnforceCheck = false` on\nGradle and no lifecycle binding on Maven, so formatting never fails\nthe build; the pipelines gate on it, keyed on the `style.managed` tag.\n\nMachine-maintained regions that keel later rewrites are fenced with\n`spotless:off` / `spotless:on` plus a do-not-edit warning — without it\nthe formatter reflows the `@ComponentScan` and `@Import` lists and\n`keel add module` can no longer find them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh+rXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh+MQAAMOtPdIfoA5rZFKmGjoAx+1\nn3I25YswrBdnxmq0ehOXX8H4mAYadJYF1fl597ljYrztzC/Pc21cHETQ6Gtw0QJx\nuibTi0BJ7bfdcM9ChUrx0zzIn+RM5R0ip5p8VPC8MsoX4UQccgfQKrqzi1Wb4nzz\nzXhKrBpEya8zdzcyxOZtBCGuCnPe/yB7uyhH4Nx9Owc89rQ+uVUosNhSRd/+65gp\nJRPxB3f8dKrNB9YNCjjXyi6OtDHIiM6vkREFX9pPwQwUXikCc9vaWB454OveAtty\n+KBs4GGVy4LLxn8LZcMPJp+LvS3ntF7xSR0YvyNXJPXQXMpR/CfAQuez87RKKop7\nOuRj9ChDyYjbM1ZW4b0RIjtSdEi+CW81lbxx0HxAs81gpNAfTH5Z0zXdJ2hdXOFW\nOOti1hfjqeUnPEzdshYCXk2vJ81j/hF0boehlgpxeQ0tPyx2CVRQpOGpPGjx/nE/\nfeBJlWI4hKL/zS/IweXIx7/Ml3OeFZpy8c976Kfm6WU1JBmVaCFPdogfQfvm1SCk\nFsSA697ItAdDmTqpX9IReyVLe7wD64ZViPGsYUdNeJXF2oFgmoWgLoCFdyif3wIr\nJUKIsMLgW0HUzr9t8UUyIS06lsJpwfZdhQUOVjmrvTM1WY1b8HrewZL+rATfXxpm\nZeO9gWP66G+7ILbjfOpq\n=dWRL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T06:06:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDFlYzMxYjlmNTczYmVkMGRmNDdlODQxNjhmZjA1MzZhYjE1YTc2Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7","sha":"82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7"}],"sha":"1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1ec31b9f573bed0df47e84168ff0536ab15a7628"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T10:50:16Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T11:04:50Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"fix(hooks): pin the Gradle 9.7.0 checksum the pin bump left unverified\n\nThe pin sweep moved the emitted wrapper to 9.7.0, and the session-start\nhook reads `GRADLE_VERSION` from `gradle-wrapper.ts` precisely so the\nhost follows it — but its `GRADLE_SHA256` table still knew only 9.4.1.\nSo every web session since has taken the warn-and-continue path and\nunpacked bytes it did not verify. That path is deliberate (a routine\nversion bump must not brick every session) and it is loud, but it is\nmeant to be transient, and nothing was closing it.\n\nThe 9.7.0 digest comes from Gradle''s published checksums, read on an\nunrestricted network, and was confirmed against a download taken\nthrough the sandbox proxy: both paths give\n84fbba45…d873ae. That is the cross-check the docs now\ndescribe, and it is not the thing they warn against — hashing our own\ndownload and calling the result published proves only that two\ndownloads agree; an independently published value agreeing with our\ndownload rules out one of the two having been tampered with in\ntransit.\n\nExercised both ways against a cold `/opt`: with the real entry the\nhook downloads, verifies, installs and no longer warns; with one\ncharacter of the digest flipped it prints the mismatch, exits 1, and\nleaves nothing unpacked.","tree":{"sha":"b22d4d45f89b07ef3247ef2dfdc2b329940df032","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/b22d4d45f89b07ef3247ef2dfdc2b329940df032"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDgyZDcwNWYzMzFmYmE1Yjk5MDViYTkzNmY5MjdlZjUwYzMwNjZjYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d","sha":"0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d"}],"sha":"82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82d705f331fba5b9905ba936f927ef50c3066ca7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T14:42:58Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T10:36:03Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"chore(deps): bump the actions group with 3 updates\n\nBumps the actions group with 3 updates: [actions/checkout](https://github.com/actions/checkout), [pnpm/action-setup](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup) and [gradle/actions/setup-gradle](https://github.com/gradle/actions).\n\n\nUpdates `actions/checkout` from 7.0.0 to 7.0.1\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/checkout/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/checkout/compare/9c091bb21b7c1c1d1991bb908d89e4e9dddfe3e0...3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1)\n\nUpdates `pnpm/action-setup` from 6.0.9 to 6.0.10\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/pnpm/action-setup/compare/0ebf47130e4866e96fce0953f49152a61190b271...0977fd99725f1db4007ccb2928dbb4e90d06cc86)\n\nUpdates `gradle/actions/setup-gradle` from 67621b124fd2e251c5e8a0e6e3b91318f2287669 to 9c971963bec38e04b3d30dcc455b5382be2fdbfb\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/gradle/actions/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/gradle/actions/compare/67621b124fd2e251c5e8a0e6e3b91318f2287669...9c971963bec38e04b3d30dcc455b5382be2fdbfb)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: actions/checkout\n  dependency-version: 7.0.1\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: actions\n- dependency-name: pnpm/action-setup\n  dependency-version: 6.0.10\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: actions\n- dependency-name: gradle/actions/setup-gradle\n  dependency-version: 9c971963bec38e04b3d30dcc455b5382be2fdbfb\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  dependency-group: actions\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a746cefd56016a25592ce4bdb74f62404f81edd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/4a746cefd56016a25592ce4bdb74f62404f81edd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDBjN2U2MzIzOGVmNjY2M2UxOWUzODdmMzg5MzA5ZTg1YzM4NTc4OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38","sha":"17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38"}],"sha":"0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/0c7e63238ef6663e19e387f389309e85c385788d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T10:07:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T10:22:24Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"chore(composition): bump every emitted-template pin to latest stable\n\nThe version-currency loop run for real: every pin the registry tracks\ncompared against its upstream feed, every drifted one bumped —\ntemplates and registry together — and every bump proven on the full\ne2e grid.\n\nJVM: Quarkus platform 3.38.2 (the Gradle stacks'' `gradle.properties`\nfinally agrees with Maven''s pin), Micronaut platform 5.1.1 + Gradle\nplugin 5.0.2 + Data TX 5.1.1, Kotlin 2.4.10, JUnit Jupiter 6.1.3,\nFlyway 13.3.0 with the CLI image lifted to the same major, Shadow\n9.6.1, Gradle wrapper 9.7.0, Native Build Tools 1.1.9, protobuf-java\n4.35.1. Node/TS/web: node images and emitted CI node-version to the\n24 LTS, Vitest ^4.1.0, @testcontainers/postgresql ^12.1.0, Vite\n^8.2.0, @rgoussu.dev/planks ^0.3.1. Go: the `go.mod` directive to\n1.26. Plus the emitted workflows'' action majors and the monitoring\nimages.\n\nWhere \"latest\" broke the emitted projects the pin is held instead,\nwith the reason recorded on its registry entry so the weekly drift\nreport stays interpretable: TypeScript stays below 7 (dependency-\ncruiser, the tool holding the emitted seam wall, supports `>=2 <7`\nand cruises 0 modules under 7 while reporting success),\nTestcontainers stays on the latest 1.x (2.x renames the per-database\nmodule artifacts the templates use), `jakarta.inject-api` stays 2.0.1\n(the `.MR` upload is a maintenance re-tag), `@types/node` tracks the\nNode major the scaffolds run rather than npm''s latest.\n\nRebased onto main, where the toolchain work (#96–#100) landed after\nthis branch was cut. Four of the surfaces this bumped no longer carry\na version of their own: the `ci` pipelines and the Dev Container node\nfeature render theirs from the pin registry through\n`src/domain/core/adapters/version-pins.ts`. Conflicts are resolved in\nfavour of that rendering — the bumped values move into the registry\nentries (`node-active-lts` 24, `go-toolchain` 1.26) and the emitted\nsurfaces keep rendering, so one registry edit still moves all three.\nThe unit expectations follow, asserting through `pinValue` rather\nthan restating the number.\n\nAlso drops a stale claim from the changelog entry: it listed\nTestcontainers 2.0.5 among the bumps while the same entry records the\nhold at 1.x, a leftover from before the grid refused it.","tree":{"sha":"e697e881fdd7b68285130984a97d1d26b848ad97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/e697e881fdd7b68285130984a97d1d26b848ad97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE3YTA2NjQ3M2M2MjE3NzczNDU2Y2VkOGU3OGE1ZTI2NWM5YjRhMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81","sha":"3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81"}],"sha":"17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/17a066473c6217773456ced8e78a5e265c9b4a38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T09:27:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T09:41:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"message":"test(mutation): exclude the pin guard from the mutation run\n\nEvery push to `main` since the single-source pins landed has failed\n`.github/workflows/mutation.yml`, and none of them tested a mutant:\nthe run dies in the initial dry run, before instrumentation buys\nanything.\n\nStryker runs the suite against an instrumented copy of the tree, where\nevery mutable literal is wrapped in a mutation switch —\n`version: ''42.7.13''` reaches the sandbox as\n`version: stryMutAct_9fa48(\"4286\") ? \"\" : (stryCov_9fa48(\"4286\"), ''42.7.13'')`.\n`tests/version-pins.test.ts` is a text sweep over the sources, not a\nbehavioral test, and 47 of the registry''s locations point into\n`src/domain/`; 19 of their patterns anchor on syntax the switch\ndisplaces, so the guard reports dead locations against a file it was\nnever meant to read in that form. Green under `pnpm test`, red under\nStryker, and the whole run aborts on it.\n\nSo the guard joins `tests/e2e/` in the Stryker config''s exclusions,\nwhich it earns twice over. A text sweep sees the mutant in the source\nrather than in the behavior: left in, a mutant blanking a version\nliteral in `src/domain/core/adapters/` fails the guard and is scored\nkilled — coverage credited to an assertion nobody wrote. Its home is\n`verify`, against the real tree, on every push and PR, where it has\nbeen all along.\n\nThe workflow is report-only, so nothing was gated on the red. What was\nlost is the signal: no incremental report has been written since.","tree":{"sha":"7df123cffa6a6ab6c335cdd50c6fa23ffb7e6764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/7df123cffa6a6ab6c335cdd50c6fa23ffb7e6764"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDM3ODY0NzRlYjAyMjhjNTZjZGEwZjIyOTBlOWYxNWY2YzdmZTJjODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005","sha":"c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005"}],"sha":"3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/3786474eb0228c56cda0f2290e9f15f6c7fe2c81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:02:40Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T20:02:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): single-source pins — dev container and CI converge on the needs (#99)\n\nThe `toolchain` block, the `dev-container` features and the `ci` setup\nsteps each stated their own JDK / Node / Go version, kept honest only\nby the pin registry''s sweep happening to claim all three occurrences\nwith one entry. That holds for the shapes the sweep''s regexes\nrecognise; a surface that changes shape, or grows a second one, drifts\nsilently — and a dev container provisioning JDK 24 for a project whose\nblock declares 25 is a build that works on the runner and fails on the\nlaptop.\n\nAll three now resolve through one shared pin source,\n`src/domain/core/adapters/version-pins.ts`, whose\n`TOOLCHAIN_PIN_SOURCE` names the registry entry each tool''s version\ncomes from. The emitted CI templates render their versions rather than\nliteralizing them, and the Go dev container asks for the pinned minor\ninstead of `latest`, so the editor and `go.mod` agree.\n\n`tests/toolchain-pins.test.ts` is the wall, and it asserts over\nemitted projects rather than over the constants: comparing the\nadapters to the registry is a tautology once they read it, so the\nguard scaffolds every family and reads the versions back out of\n`devcontainer.json`, `ci.yml` and `.gitlab-ci.yml`. It also lists, per\nfamily, which `surface:tool` pairs state a version, so a surface\nquietly dropping one is as red as one stating the wrong one; the\ndeliberate absences (GitHub''s `go-version-file`, `rustup update\nstable`, corepack''s `packageManager`) are pinned down as absences.\nRust is the one floating pin: `latest` counts as agreement there and\nnowhere else, which is why its devcontainer feature stays versionless.\n\nEmitting `keel toolchain install` into pipelines is deliberately not\npart of this — the provider setup actions are faster and cached, and\nthe convergence is about the values, not the mechanism.\n\nCloses #92","tree":{"sha":"d6292497866bf3ea915fd213d5164fe030426174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/d6292497866bf3ea915fd213d5164fe030426174"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005","verification":{"payload":"tree d6292497866bf3ea915fd213d5164fe030426174\nparent 111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787169760 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787169760 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): single-source pins — dev container and CI converge on the needs (#99)\n\nThe `toolchain` block, the `dev-container` features and the `ci` setup\nsteps each stated their own JDK / Node / Go version, kept honest only\nby the pin registry''s sweep happening to claim all three occurrences\nwith one entry. That holds for the shapes the sweep''s regexes\nrecognise; a surface that changes shape, or grows a second one, drifts\nsilently — and a dev container provisioning JDK 24 for a project whose\nblock declares 25 is a build that works on the runner and fails on the\nlaptop.\n\nAll three now resolve through one shared pin source,\n`src/domain/core/adapters/version-pins.ts`, whose\n`TOOLCHAIN_PIN_SOURCE` names the registry entry each tool''s version\ncomes from. The emitted CI templates render their versions rather than\nliteralizing them, and the Go dev container asks for the pinned minor\ninstead of `latest`, so the editor and `go.mod` agree.\n\n`tests/toolchain-pins.test.ts` is the wall, and it asserts over\nemitted projects rather than over the constants: comparing the\nadapters to the registry is a tautology once they read it, so the\nguard scaffolds every family and reads the versions back out of\n`devcontainer.json`, `ci.yml` and `.gitlab-ci.yml`. It also lists, per\nfamily, which `surface:tool` pairs state a version, so a surface\nquietly dropping one is as red as one stating the wrong one; the\ndeliberate absences (GitHub''s `go-version-file`, `rustup update\nstable`, corepack''s `packageManager`) are pinned down as absences.\nRust is the one floating pin: `latest` counts as agreement there and\nnowhere else, which is why its devcontainer feature stays versionless.\n\nEmitting `keel toolchain install` into pipelines is deliberately not\npart of this — the provider setup actions are faster and cached, and\nthe convergence is about the values, not the mechanism.\n\nCloses #92","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgvgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+jkQAJTE/mxLAa686zDrSzTE0cjv\n02WgS4qfTw3w2UnsoczWU4LmAIkUrkvNllQ6ZCzKIqP/DNvBNIEJKJIYjUOp+iFJ\nD2aMRQF2ve7mKZSVHIDcAAOAfAitcJOstqA8/0p2atDk9MCA5XeK2QqtdrPN71G/\nmLnJBwDNZgtPOpgjO5xKeRd2aFlEwqy7ccJ/G5+gRCI6tC3Ky2U1JLvDjpZZJHK7\nuSQqx09mTqKJbMJV9QKxxrChXcwU2KsCqD3NNpAVij4vegdqA0rCWYSVm20VSelu\nQOYeJTh+IH/SU8u54tH2teoVdjA/MNobqxliIX0lt9wKeiXdTHaxu7I7/7FrB/Sc\na36oCPI2MAC4AeRcGHEeLALon2ZVfhfmO9T3w772hWP0Ggwy6lAdJwXDlLVe+UzI\nIZ22HuD3kb0RtBT1WJovzMd6Kgj7rPqDn7XR6Z8HPtR/mZ3v9WMlKYRRChZuQPcR\n5UedRhz9769gxFhnMbycz5+zFo//yRpvojDFaLAaE+koWAyW0G02ZdHC4dDJgkA8\niYmu4bJhoh0uDsRMNhqGp+elXyZkci/Vjo1fEKWpGP7sroLNf5i5joYjGY2OSxcd\niFB4zgDFQHbMDg3oKafgPJVcx0/bHVt7fuC+xUbsTV7F9cnVsXqClFGfW+T7k30N\nMbff4BnueyHmvkg3eeVp\n=u2lp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T20:02:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGM3NDIxOTkxOGJkMDg3OGVmMzEyY2M2ZDYzN2NkOGJkNDcyMGEwMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad","sha":"111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad"}],"sha":"c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c74219918bd0878ef312cc6d637cd8bd4720a005"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:21:10Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T19:21:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): resolve version prefixes through the manager (#100)\n\nRoadmap N.6, closing the gap N.3 opened and N.4 left standing. The\nblock pins a major for the JDK and for Node — a series, not a release\n— and two provider records cannot take one: asdf documents\n`.tool-versions` as a lockfile that forbids `latest`, and SDKMAN!\ncandidate identifiers always carry a patch, so `java=25-tem` names\nnothing installable. Both now declare a `resolve` on the record, and\none engine pass runs it before any render.\n\nThe order is lockfile order, and the obvious one is a bug: the config\non disk wins while it still answers the prefix, and only when nothing\nanswers is the manager asked its own way (`asdf latest`, `sdk list`).\nAsking upstream first would make every check call a good lockfile\nstale the day a patch shipped. So a resolved file stays put, a re-run\nwrites nothing, the steady state spawns no process, and an absent\nmanager can no longer overwrite a good file with the prefix it came\nfrom. A pin bump still moves it once, because the recorded value\nstops answering.\n\nkeel never invents the patch half. Where neither the file nor the\nmanager names a version, the prefix renders as before and both\nreports carry it as `unresolved` — counted against check''s verdict\nand printed as a warning.","tree":{"sha":"5efbbd7395238975829806928319c110fa0d7d12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/5efbbd7395238975829806928319c110fa0d7d12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 5efbbd7395238975829806928319c110fa0d7d12\nparent 7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787167270 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787167270 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): resolve version prefixes through the manager (#100)\n\nRoadmap N.6, closing the gap N.3 opened and N.4 left standing. The\nblock pins a major for the JDK and for Node — a series, not a release\n— and two provider records cannot take one: asdf documents\n`.tool-versions` as a lockfile that forbids `latest`, and SDKMAN!\ncandidate identifiers always carry a patch, so `java=25-tem` names\nnothing installable. Both now declare a `resolve` on the record, and\none engine pass runs it before any render.\n\nThe order is lockfile order, and the obvious one is a bug: the config\non disk wins while it still answers the prefix, and only when nothing\nanswers is the manager asked its own way (`asdf latest`, `sdk list`).\nAsking upstream first would make every check call a good lockfile\nstale the day a patch shipped. So a resolved file stays put, a re-run\nwrites nothing, the steady state spawns no process, and an absent\nmanager can no longer overwrite a good file with the prefix it came\nfrom. A pin bump still moves it once, because the recorded value\nstops answering.\n\nkeel never invents the patch half. Where neither the file nor the\nmanager names a version, the prefix renders as before and both\nreports carry it as `unresolved` — counted against check''s verdict\nand printed as a warning.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhgImCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdmIQADTBaUwryj2aNA0ckSptccYi\nmNfJ8vwG9V8Q4DI/o7tTJGs5i+/0PmB1BRp+322hoTGsrs6ftLb60xUY3nLvvvvc\nYUyJNoj8g6SNKiAGxWJ5FvivlNms4NDouqEbMFXJad8u9VvnpkHRMzjAYI3U4krd\nIwksc9N6FU71yucfyQNWGUwVTPDODeQIeCumbvap/SPSXaZlJGk1PxjWw29TS2k5\neRMGm7WiEwUGci15EiKI3FMtsa++P5jSe2Gzt+9xBwOePtOsoXmtOtXdYZoLGTfc\n1abfoH3FzrncnvHvBM44A5xt1XtEIDof51b/abncCQ7HkTrcBkUL+vRhelg3F4Ue\nPMqgHP4sHJ0yOePYaTtF1k1cHTN70m/dbC9/VARHHTVaDAb1qE/nhQGga1n+KsEy\nUk/FF+SdtrOhUu/yda2kM8DMVzNMSBGaJiMWTQeY04bX20A2jg8D0KTEHVohuYQ5\ncRkopVuGB2h7u1SpEBej6yxUeqI+FCL9oI6RpPuS/DWffTuvldWyRJonCg3LFDlp\nSzUX2O72vFwXILrojGsUC0AYNOfpUBl5INiYq/ZoCFD5/WQvzirRT9qP8JWou7Zh\n7kmymKxt3gsjhdhGr9+UxVDMrk8rWBIRy1JgwvTBC/6PDOjjI0goQtKUehIx3fZk\njgCMNV745VB0P/Sk5hih\n=O4iY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T19:21:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDExMWUwZWE2ZWE3Y2FhNjk5OGM4MjI4ZWU0MzYxNDBmNzY3YmI4YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c","sha":"7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c"}],"sha":"111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/111e0ea6ea7caa6998c8228ee436140f767bb8ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:50:23Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:50:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): sdkman, rustup, and Go''s native no-op complete the dial (#98)\n\nRoadmap N.4: three provider records join the manager dial, and none of\nthem widens it — each is offered only where its ecosystem is the whole\ndeclaration, which is the coverage invariant doing the work rather than\na rule of its own.\n\n- sdkman renders `.sdkmanrc` and installs with `sdk env install`,\n  reached through a login shell sourcing `sdkman-init.sh` because `sdk`\n  is a shell function, not a binary. Covers {jdk, gradle, maven}.\n- rustup renders `rust-toolchain.toml`, honored natively by cargo, and\n  installs the active toolchain. A bare Rust major spells `stable` —\n  rustup has no series channel, and the scaffolds track latest stable\n  by construction.\n- go-native is the explicit \"no manager needed\" answer: it merges\n  `go.mod`''s `toolchain` directive in place and runs no command at all.\n  The merge is the choice''s consistency check — check reports drift,\n  install writes the directive back. The directive is a floor, not a pin.\n\nThe two keel-chosen spellings (sdkman-java-distribution,\nrustup-stable-channel) join the pin registry.\n\nCloses #91","tree":{"sha":"35baa0408596fb67862dc871f81063d698a99565","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/35baa0408596fb67862dc871f81063d698a99565"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c","verification":{"payload":"tree 35baa0408596fb67862dc871f81063d698a99565\nparent d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787161823 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787161823 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): sdkman, rustup, and Go''s native no-op complete the dial (#98)\n\nRoadmap N.4: three provider records join the manager dial, and none of\nthem widens it — each is offered only where its ecosystem is the whole\ndeclaration, which is the coverage invariant doing the work rather than\na rule of its own.\n\n- sdkman renders `.sdkmanrc` and installs with `sdk env install`,\n  reached through a login shell sourcing `sdkman-init.sh` because `sdk`\n  is a shell function, not a binary. Covers {jdk, gradle, maven}.\n- rustup renders `rust-toolchain.toml`, honored natively by cargo, and\n  installs the active toolchain. A bare Rust major spells `stable` —\n  rustup has no series channel, and the scaffolds track latest stable\n  by construction.\n- go-native is the explicit \"no manager needed\" answer: it merges\n  `go.mod`''s `toolchain` directive in place and runs no command at all.\n  The merge is the choice''s consistency check — check reports drift,\n  install writes the directive back. The directive is a floor, not a pin.\n\nThe two keel-chosen spellings (sdkman-java-distribution,\nrustup-stable-channel) join the pin registry.\n\nCloses #91","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhezfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATJMQAHHsqN0xb1vqMDtXOTBEf1vt\nPQQEQ0Q2W8VCx4bcZVweNJgphMNJcmMpqy3XykD47SbUWsQ7CxvDykYusZ+eMuaV\n7Zv9BIPsAcZyFrphBgmzJwNRkT3MtalLDna/4noYQ7BNtOpY3MVpvmtr1QrDiTRp\nf9Knh0HlHdHP/97AlIFcVfvTF56WSieUNcXsVa2FN9iZch6zFMJSMrLCylZotGvs\n2RBX1YIqrB+wOOqnwSXXBvQ2EfdBzKXd2bxgv8/mY+VjtlzATtTiI3ioObeGvaPG\nIzEt8mgKAn6k2llDRD0X0fq41p6Ne31ua89Ftfof1k6vvPS5XIWZ1OyBA9WdOI9w\nFZiAWdcXqFQEvKoSppv8khzl+IneJbamQBYo+FnbGGq7HwGCC78tYBlcHJJgcTqH\nowsWzbBG2QHDdBdA10ltw+iHTy5pJriYfxfjacaA/WjKNiFrN1EiUJPS0aTMQQKT\nBvqnLR0LZPmTQISjnpihXGo1aPk5XmB5SRDYamgsRhTBd8d39p0xEcuGWh5uZgHg\nt8yMuUzCxMIgZ3ihZg+3qn/WirJt8GNZvO5n1LfZP0/CrSeZLJfRmrHZcqf+ZX+A\ngMniGPFNFCQeNfME6EDEYYT9sWdEKjYu9KGFOiuZlNIwQLK4m05Q80gg5NGnPF8p\nQTf8HKWvNj25pyH1r4vK\n=OWvk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T17:50:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDdiZWMwMGM5NDYwNDJhZWY0NDcyZmZmNjFjNjAwOTgyMzZhMTE5NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7","sha":"d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7"}],"sha":"7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/7bec00c946042aef4472fff61c60098236a1194c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:38:02Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:38:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): the manager dial — coverage resolution, singles vs combinations (#97)\n\nThe version manager `keel toolchain install` provisions with becomes a\nchoice, computed from the project''s declared needs: a provider covering\nthe whole needs set is offered as a single; where none does, a curated\ncombination is offered for the same coverage. A partial choice is never\noffered — the coverage invariant, now a unit test against the needs sets\nthe real family adapters produce.\n\nThree records join mise: asdf (.tool-versions), nvm (.nvmrc, reached\nthrough a login shell because nvm is a shell function; covers node and\nthe npm that ships with it) and corepack (the packageManager field in\nthe project''s own package.json, merged in place; covers pnpm).\nCombinations are compositions, not records, and are all-or-nothing.\n\nThe answer is sticky on the block''s new `provider` field, written by the\nengine so `keel add toolchain --reapply` leaves it alone, and\nre-validated against the needs on every run.\n\nCloses #90.","tree":{"sha":"a16aa6aeecb765fcddafe60c5ee8c2e2e574f2eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/a16aa6aeecb765fcddafe60c5ee8c2e2e574f2eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7","verification":{"payload":"tree a16aa6aeecb765fcddafe60c5ee8c2e2e574f2eb\nparent 1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787157482 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787157482 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): the manager dial — coverage resolution, singles vs combinations (#97)\n\nThe version manager `keel toolchain install` provisions with becomes a\nchoice, computed from the project''s declared needs: a provider covering\nthe whole needs set is offered as a single; where none does, a curated\ncombination is offered for the same coverage. A partial choice is never\noffered — the coverage invariant, now a unit test against the needs sets\nthe real family adapters produce.\n\nThree records join mise: asdf (.tool-versions), nvm (.nvmrc, reached\nthrough a login shell because nvm is a shell function; covers node and\nthe npm that ships with it) and corepack (the packageManager field in\nthe project''s own package.json, merged in place; covers pnpm).\nCombinations are compositions, not records, and are all-or-nothing.\n\nThe answer is sticky on the block''s new `provider` field, written by the\nengine so `keel add toolchain --reapply` leaves it alone, and\nre-validated against the needs on every run.\n\nCloses #90.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhdvqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPWkQAKTKSIzRWMvZ3QpAxLhGgPbp\nbQS7PJnO7NJLHbKnyw3rXAoN2v0191wtZ0TAmKKZb4+8Ue5FW4qRlCooD8ImTu5s\nfelRUiy4ztUF60Y+wQr4K8eHChj+MX9kpeHmIlTT+Z/CVAAzI1h18Ee1OEpZgD4R\n8lb7qNFr3WFHMoEiq59eQMMngarcAjtZHH1J2tr2Ei5lV7SsT1/YEjRgjxSsUsot\njO26GYbtL5Gx6oLJkGWsGmdvxx0AHt22mbMM5r/iJuamf0lqIAeJ/u6oB/moHeti\n19ljHLjvUU4ffa3QDPaSe0GmeXjFIhy/upBORWSdtzubEGPD3LaDqeFUh4P/OjZ1\nU9PQKlr3UtsphnL+QICxGEthFt8rgSgIAsfti9+FttXfCyGQnvOmCthQmo8m3+DV\nlXdzirrxnScLN5VIobanaJdYkcnbduaZTnYfDUpV6wEOfjXK83aFRInMhP4YBtGg\nqo6aEeUq+PCHV0j1oy6xnvN3xgCIaBrkeR9hRfJ0q7XOHJPn5OnOphSrvUXw5eM1\nt8syl2KcCWP4RYwX+CDo3KBsdxbQDtH5k4omcfUBaTAxpr4KsiRYUT5jxD1CbCLz\nqRw/GGf4TIVUyh3BatbySqAPMrTZ09gT8BdvUxLsaU9uERlEuKi6rhnGIIckLf+x\nTsx0XMJ3lGcnuSi4nkij\n=o+r1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T16:38:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKGQwMThiZjA3YjFlNTRiMGM3MWRlMDYxOTkzNGUyZjE1MmI1ODBjZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a","sha":"1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a"}],"sha":"d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d018bf07b1e54b0c71de0619934e2f152b580cd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:22:55Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T12:22:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): the provisioning context + keel toolchain install, mise walking skeleton (#96)\n\nThird slice of roadmap item N (closes #89): a new bounded context\ninside keel (src/domain/toolchain/, its own hexagon) that reads the\ntoolchain block and satisfies it through exactly one provider —\nmise — end to end. The context meets the rest of keel only at\ndomain/contract; new dependency-cruiser rules hold the seam both\nways, per the \"modulith first, extraction later\" decision.\n\nThe provider record model (id, covers, config renderer, install\nsequence, per-tool version spelling) is domain content like the\nadapter tables; the mise record spells jdk@25 as java =\n\"temurin-25\", everything else verbatim. Orchestrator, never\ninstaller: keel toolchain install renders mise.toml — the\nprovider''s native file — then delegates to mise trust + mise\ninstall, idempotent at any point in the project''s life; mise\nabsent stays loud (bootstrap one-liner + manual tool list), never\na silent skip. keel toolchain check reports satisfied/missing per\nneed — counting mise.toml drift against the block as unsatisfied —\nwithout touching anything, and exits 1 when unsatisfied.\n\nThe keel-chosen half of the JDK spelling registers in the pin\nregistry (mise-java-distribution) and the sweep now scans the new\ncontext. Engine tests run in verify over the shipped fakes; a real\nmise install suite (tests/toolchain/) is opt-in via\nKEEL_RUN_TOOLCHAIN=1 — the tests/currency/ pattern, never in the\nPR matrix. Documented in docs/cli.md, docs/verticals/toolchain.md,\ndocs/composition.md, and docs/development.md.","tree":{"sha":"3719bf6c9bcb415a9c74b2048c313638b6aef41c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/3719bf6c9bcb415a9c74b2048c313638b6aef41c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a","verification":{"payload":"tree 3719bf6c9bcb415a9c74b2048c313638b6aef41c\nparent 82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787142175 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787142175 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): the provisioning context + keel toolchain install, mise walking skeleton (#96)\n\nThird slice of roadmap item N (closes #89): a new bounded context\ninside keel (src/domain/toolchain/, its own hexagon) that reads the\ntoolchain block and satisfies it through exactly one provider —\nmise — end to end. The context meets the rest of keel only at\ndomain/contract; new dependency-cruiser rules hold the seam both\nways, per the \"modulith first, extraction later\" decision.\n\nThe provider record model (id, covers, config renderer, install\nsequence, per-tool version spelling) is domain content like the\nadapter tables; the mise record spells jdk@25 as java =\n\"temurin-25\", everything else verbatim. Orchestrator, never\ninstaller: keel toolchain install renders mise.toml — the\nprovider''s native file — then delegates to mise trust + mise\ninstall, idempotent at any point in the project''s life; mise\nabsent stays loud (bootstrap one-liner + manual tool list), never\na silent skip. keel toolchain check reports satisfied/missing per\nneed — counting mise.toml drift against the block as unsatisfied —\nwithout touching anything, and exits 1 when unsatisfied.\n\nThe keel-chosen half of the JDK spelling registers in the pin\nregistry (mise-java-distribution) and the sweep now scans the new\ncontext. Engine tests run in verify over the shipped fakes; a real\nmise install suite (tests/toolchain/) is opt-in via\nKEEL_RUN_TOOLCHAIN=1 — the tests/currency/ pattern, never in the\nPR matrix. Documented in docs/cli.md, docs/verticals/toolchain.md,\ndocs/composition.md, and docs/development.md.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhaAfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMFcQAAkVqzpT3zmaoTy43aMMtsL8\nyOjK/r/nNNkkYlEsJLDfvv5Cq+qy8WsLEsp9Z+W+dKa3I0CkrfK+lDgV8TCxM7gz\nfKw81LPzFVNeRVLtiCwEcQvug/TnQhB+xXuljb2udbpoaK1CaK3n6G4v+UXO65xm\nk0cAjQDui76o4gMLVfMd4Lhsegkff73tAj5c8wNzZ5/sILHaujuBi2Qx48aY0p+P\nrWoTpfv6pdddK8uqMElDk3R+agKYOuPtHD1GrcpzcJX5sYf3mfwRP/yFugpUuMz3\nPyDPNug8Z/U3Aoy5eF81AyQ8xaydpqt3Z/A5AGsU0zHvO+qrNQsuAb0uLL4LPjnn\nFkpBDbJ91j2hJUllvEqY4nMIRsWeeAwB3TJDc7OYRqzZ5Ze2RJ00d8UsEJM7ojSW\nrjRH4OVxKQWs4ol9Hzr9mwr+uoaBEDOSua3p/9fZM8fqm6zhleFcTvDUb0E8hN24\n+tVznBpnM1KoyToXD/GfJaHf3kENyng8WvxnjwzjhHwWiQeo1Zwa5DDIHxHq/32w\nFbGHjHRscCkdZ9YL1JlWPZkS80EG8yFArXRuxJN+TaRVwkw/UuhpZH9HT8xeVWuj\n9imgkA59ugSTM49oZZYdBAmZUt+dJ8iBMQQgF4eOrcI5RkUgejj5gdBmH+xfbsop\namqux6QoPfQJwDf0nDqE\n=zZBZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T12:22:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a","node_id":"C_kwDOSGEt5toAKDE0NTY5NTJjNmI5Zjg4MWQ1NTQ3YmQ2ZTFiNjQ4ZGYxMGQ3YWE0N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409","sha":"82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409"}],"sha":"1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/1456952c6b9f881d5547bd6e1b648df10d7aa47a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:34:10Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T11:34:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(toolchain): keel add toolchain — the vertical that records needs (#95)\n\nSecond slice of roadmap item N (closes #88): an opt-in toolchain\nvertical that derives the project''s toolchain needs from the\nmanifest''s tags and records them in the N.0 toolchain block — one\npredicate-selected adapter per family, the dev-container pattern:\nruntime.jvm → jdk + the build system the pkg.* tag names, lang.go →\ngo, lang.rust → rust, lang.typescript → node + pnpm when tagged\n(npm rides with node). A short \"Toolchain\" runbook note lands in\nthe README.\n\nVersions are read from assets/composition/version-pins.json through\nthe TemplateSource port at contribute time and each need cites its\nentry id as source — the block is one more consumer of the registry,\nnever a second place versions are stated. The registry gains a\nts-pnpm entry claiming the packageManager pins the TS/web templates\nalready carried unregistered. Contribution grows a toolchain field;\nthe installer folds declared needs into the manifest upserting by\ntool, so keel add toolchain --reapply refreshes the block after a\npin bump without duplicating entries.\n\nDeliberately in no stack''s default vertical set until the\nprovisioning engine (N.2+) settles the end-to-end story; on a\nfullstack composite each service records its own block via its own\nmanifest. Unit tests assert the block per family and per pkg.*/\nlayout combination against the registry itself; docs in\ndocs/verticals/toolchain.md, the catalogs, and composition.md.","tree":{"sha":"d7e28b53605f41f70effe52ea288b3c9c3372076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/d7e28b53605f41f70effe52ea288b3c9c3372076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409","verification":{"payload":"tree d7e28b53605f41f70effe52ea288b3c9c3372076\nparent 8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787139250 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787139250 +0200\n\nfeat(toolchain): keel add toolchain — the vertical that records needs (#95)\n\nSecond slice of roadmap item N (closes #88): an opt-in toolchain\nvertical that derives the project''s toolchain needs from the\nmanifest''s tags and records them in the N.0 toolchain block — one\npredicate-selected adapter per family, the dev-container pattern:\nruntime.jvm → jdk + the build system the pkg.* tag names, lang.go →\ngo, lang.rust → rust, lang.typescript → node + pnpm when tagged\n(npm rides with node). A short \"Toolchain\" runbook note lands in\nthe README.\n\nVersions are read from assets/composition/version-pins.json through\nthe TemplateSource port at contribute time and each need cites its\nentry id as source — the block is one more consumer of the registry,\nnever a second place versions are stated. The registry gains a\nts-pnpm entry claiming the packageManager pins the TS/web templates\nalready carried unregistered. Contribution grows a toolchain field;\nthe installer folds declared needs into the manifest upserting by\ntool, so keel add toolchain --reapply refreshes the block after a\npin bump without duplicating entries.\n\nDeliberately in no stack''s default vertical set until the\nprovisioning engine (N.2+) settles the end-to-end story; on a\nfullstack composite each service records its own block via its own\nmanifest. Unit tests assert the block per family and per pkg.*/\nlayout combination against the registry itself; docs in\ndocs/verticals/toolchain.md, the catalogs, and composition.md.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BE