":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commit/8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d","sha":"8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d"}],"sha":"82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/82dadbc234df6561179a01cacf07f341098f0409"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:01:52Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:01:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(contract): the versioned toolchain manifest block (#94)\n\nFirst slice of roadmap item N (closes #87): the contract between keel,\nwhich records what a project''s toolchain needs, and the provisioning\nengine, which will decide how to satisfy them. No writer, no consumer.\n\nThe manifest may now carry an optional toolchain block — schemaVersion\nplus needs as { tool, version, source? } over a closed tool vocabulary\n(jdk, gradle, maven, go, node, npm, pnpm, rust). The block versions\nindependently of the manifest; an unknown schemaVersion is rejected\nloudly. Absence means nothing declared, distinct from an empty block.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing duplicate MODULITH_LAYOUT_TAG import that\nfailed the persistence vertical suite under vitest.","tree":{"sha":"2067b834903c006a95ca1da33b197b6367eb593c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/2067b834903c006a95ca1da33b197b6367eb593c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/8ab346b8098f512281f8e61129eb9df3b1a4c82d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2067b834903c006a95ca1da33b197b6367eb593c\nparent 6aa071a6242477721f846221308cd5d0037ecc0a\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787122912 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787122912 +0200\n\nfeat(contract): the versioned toolchain manifest block (#94)\n\nFirst slice of roadmap item N (closes #87): the contract between keel,\nwhich records what a project''s toolchain needs, and the provisioning\nengine, which will decide how to satisfy them. No writer, no consumer.\n\nThe manifest may now carry an optional toolchain block — schemaVersion\nplus needs as { tool, version, source? } over a closed tool vocabulary\n(jdk, gradle, maven, go, node, npm, pnpm, rust). The block versions\nindependently of the manifest; an unknown schemaVersion is rejected\nloudly. Absence means nothing declared, distinct from an empty block.\n\nAlso fixes a pre-existing duplicate MODULITH_LAYOUT_TAG import that\nfailed the persistence vertical suite under vitest.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhVTgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsuAQAExKXbMe73WQ3JiajvxQSU/x\nkulW348UT+C4zc1quIoT5o4HsNXu3A4UOcB4hZ4nI16glU5bJ4V8D0UHYPselI2G\nxPevugKVEDJpvfjjk6JrQIRARg9mSWPRu3gdgLPGbNXcu8QxEo