om/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/d8ef3f58da10febba4d7651fe3d5b4b625e2243f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:50:32Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:50:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(walking-skeleton): ts-cli stack — the CLI twin of ts-http (#84)\n\nCloses #71. `keel new --stack=ts-cli` scaffolds the same\nno-build-step TypeScript workspace as ts-http (Node 22.18+ runs the\nsources directly, the `exports` maps hold the walls) with the\ndeployment unit swapped: application/cli maps flags to commands and\nResults to streams + exit code — 0 for a greeting, 2 when the domain\nsays no, 1 for a defect. Both module layouts and both package\nmanagers from day one; the entrypoint-neutral half of the bootstrap\nnow lives in a shared walking-skeleton/ts-domain template tree both\nstacks render. --with-peer-context and `keel add module` became\nentrypoint-agnostic on TypeScript (tsAssemblies, the Rust/Go\npattern), so the modulith story carries over whole. Two new e2e cells\n(modulith-ts-cli-{npm,pnpm}) and a basic walking-skeleton suite ride\nthe web shard. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap updated.","tree":{"sha":"413def1fa4d2825ef6f8dab4d09bb18f4aea83e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/413def1fa4d2825ef6f8dab4d09bb18f4aea83e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/d8ef3f58da10febba4d7651fe3d5b4b625e2243f","verification":{"payload":"tree 413def1fa4d2825ef6f8dab4d09bb18f4aea83e3\nparent 2a2c86462c2497f81d794071e974a91691e9ad58\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787064632 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787064632 +0200\n\nfeat(walking-skeleton): ts-cli stack — the CLI twin of ts-http (#84)\n\nCloses #71. `keel new --stack=ts-cli` scaffolds the same\nno-build-step TypeScript workspace as ts-http (Node 22.18+ runs the\nsources directly, the `exports` maps hold the walls) with the\ndeployment unit swapped: application/cli maps flags to commands and\nResults to streams + exit code — 0 for a greeting, 2 when the domain\nsays no, 1 for a defect. Both module layouts and both package\nmanagers from day one; the entrypoint-neutral half of the bootstrap\nnow lives in a shared walking-skeleton/ts-domain template tree both\nstacks render. --with-peer-context and `keel add module` became\nentrypoint-agnostic on TypeScript (tsAssemblies, the Rust/Go\npattern), so the modulith story carries over whole. Two new e2e cells\n(modulith-ts-cli-{npm,pnpm}) and a basic walking-skeleton suite ride\nthe web shard. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap updated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhHE4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5LgQAG2+vjvBpDkvr8xTYRNuGWMD\n8ythE3sCqBIMiUZh6xrG1K3lkdsSKHfOmzArie4u3t1WuQlo9kgbSTNkboKdolDZ\nzZUEEcbuSpQDPmIACSZyL/MLJUsPevuBcx7IptIofFTujO8VQC6e91arngjMHWa2\nr5mjmoytW55gLtHd4hmB/qyNN58NcMnbmeCXhDjfWhK64dK7KhrEztR/iyGfjn+h\ntzuBYV7yIygZVcJ/5MZE5VB2inhCK+9ksPJhoAaFsB5++mM3nLSBk8