 wired via\n.claude/settings.json, auto-formatting where the toolchain ships a\nformatter then running the family''s CI gate), and a `run` skill\n(.claude/skills/run/SKILL.md) with the launch-and-probe loop for the\nscaffolded shape. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap updated.","tree":{"sha":"46d410e5f9fe3f1e4a2f91b26a0fe7cac9dcf523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/46d410e5f9fe3f1e4a2f91b26a0fe7cac9dcf523"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/2a2c86462c2497f81d794071e974a91691e9ad58","verification":{"payload":"tree 46d410e5f9fe3f1e4a2f91b26a0fe7cac9dcf523\nparent b62bb4069aa044726571db254f07b777399a0528\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787063480 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787063480 +0200\n\nfeat(walking-skeleton): the Claude kit — stack runbook addenda + emitted .claude content (#80)\n\nRoadmap item G (closes #70). The walking skeleton gains an\n`agentic-kit` dimension covered by one adapter per stack family\n(jvm-, go-, rust-, ts-, wc-claude-kit), each resolving its commands\nfrom the manifest tags rather than minting adapters per pkg.* tag.\nEvery scaffold now ships: a stack runbook appended to the emitted\nAGENTS.md under sentinel markers (self-replacing on re-apply, never\ntouching the user''s edits around it), the pre-commit format hook keel\nitself uses (.claude/hooks/pre-commit-format.sh wired via\n.claude/settings.json, auto-formatting where the toolchain ships a\nformatter then running the family''s CI gate), and a `run` skill\n(.claude/skills/run/SKILL.md) with the launch-and-probe loop for the\nscaffolded shape. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap updated.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhGy4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOhsQAIdeFUAcnqQ8k1vL6s5y2wlw\nMxPTP8aUB8cI+2YZ4FP/zuWRf33Nz4hYg8MhrWEVOhbbeBpNROrxHF1ziVxvjwSu\nqC0yiQbgm5mJFutLHcP963iFfWPTmzeNrww84c7kdZT2fVluF2L6BGR2YP6VsQ9g\nFO3RSOq8V3Cmw50Z01VvPT8y/d12BmYDtnio4Cng7l9TjSeaK/C3lJQ6So7BwwMl\nG7