 without writing); a patch that would change\nan already-patched shared file refuses the run with\nkeel.reapply-conflict before anything commits. Answers are frozen\n(--set with --reapply errors), re-promoted tags never double, and the\nvertical keeps its original installedAt. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap\nupdated; item L marked shipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LLJzWZ8tVJ2WjAqRntD8D","tree":{"sha":"be04d052288988536af2a9e099589fc328dae941","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/be04d052288988536af2a9e099589fc328dae941"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/e25830d6f7a239da1300dd8e6418086404c0e3f9","verification":{"payload":"tree be04d052288988536af2a9e099589fc328dae941\nparent c3b55e6eaa08c88ae2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787055940 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787055940 +0200\n\nfeat(cli): `keel add --reapply` — the update path for scaffolded projects (#78)\n\nThe conservative v1 of roadmap item L (closes #68): re-render an\ninstalled vertical from the manifest''s recorded answers, show a\nunified diff against the working tree, refuse on conflict.\n\nTemplate-owned files are rewritten to the pristine re-render\n(byte-identical renders skipped, every rewrite reported as a unified\ndiff; --dry-run shows it without writing); a patch that would change\nan already-patched shared file refuses the run with\nkeel.reapply-conflict before anything commits. Answers are frozen\n(--set with --reapply errors), re-promoted tags never double, and the\nvertical keeps its original installedAt. Docs, CHANGELOG, and roadmap\nupdated; item L marked shipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019LLJzWZ8tVJ2WjAqRntD8D","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhE9ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkxsQAD5TL6BPtE