2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad","sha":"c3b55e6eaa08c88ae2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c3b55e6eaa08c88ae2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad"}],"sha":"e25830d6f7a239da1300dd8e6418086404c0e3f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/e25830d6f7a239da1300dd8e6418086404c0e3f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14975619?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rgoussu-dev","id":14975619,"login":"rgoussu-dev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTc1NjE5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rgoussu-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/commits/c3b55e6eaa08c88ae2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T11:44:16Z","email":"rgoussu@gmail.com","name":"Romain Goussu"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T11:44:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build: build-from-sources loop — pnpm keel playground + tarball recipe (#77)\n\nRoadmap item K (#67). The e2e harness proves the emitted projects but\nnot the package; this gives the working tree a documented path to\nbeing consumed the way a user consumes it.\n\n- `pnpm keel …` builds and runs bin/keel.js inside a scratch\n  playground (scripts/keel-local.mjs): KEEL_PLAYGROUND pins the\n  directory across invocations, a playground inside the repo is\n  refused.\n- docs/development.md → \"Trying keel locally\" documents that fast\n  inner loop and the packaging-fidelity loop (pnpm build && npm pack,\n  install the tarball into a scratch prefix, keel new from there),\n  with which to use when.\n- AGENTS.md §5, CHANGELOG, and roadmap item K updated in the same\n  change.\n\nAcceptance run as specified: the packed tarball, installed into a\nscratch prefix, scaffolded a ts-http project whose own npm test and\ntypecheck pass, with no reference back to the checkout inside it.","tree":{"sha":"b3bd8815fd8d5dce8a79ece49258e14429258268","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/trees/b3bd8815fd8d5dce8a79ece49258e14429258268"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rgoussu-dev/Keel/git/commits/c3b55e6eaa08c88ae2e20eb3720aaa03cb7315ad","verification":{"payload":"tree b3bd8815fd8d5dce8a79ece49258e14429258268\nparent 763eec8cc4e4d27caab113f4af1345011c269d73\nauthor Romain Goussu <rgoussu@gmail.com> 1787053456 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787053456 +0200\n\nbuild: build-from-sources loop — pnpm keel playground + tarball recipe (#77)\n\nRoadmap item K (#67). The e2e harness proves the emitted projects but\nnot the package; this gives the working tree a documented path to\nbeing consumed the way a user consumes it.\n\n- `pnpm keel …` builds and runs bin/keel.js inside a scratch\n  playground (scripts/keel-local.mjs): KEEL_PLAYGROUND pins the\n  directory across invocations, a playground inside the repo is\n  refused.\n- docs/development.md → \"Trying keel locally\" documents that fast\n  inner loop and the packaging-fidelity loop (pnpm build && npm pack,\n  install the tarball into a scratch prefix, keel new from there),\n  with which to use when.\n- AGENTS.md §5, CHANGELOG, and roadmap item K updated in the same\n  change.\n\nAcceptance run as specified: the packed tarball, installed into a\ns