sh-sangawar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahesh-sangawar","id":12147465,"login":"mahesh-sangawar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTQ3NDY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/9e753982e19341b6c295a5a19adc9eac6669ae04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:44:35Z","email":"mayu.b14@gmail.com","name":"Mahesh Sangawar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:44:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mark8ly): grant the artwork sweeper Postgres access (#960) (#1316)\n\nThe abandoned buyer-artwork reaper has failed EVERY run since it shipped\non 2026-10-03 — six consecutive failures over 35 hours.\n\nmark8ly-postgres-ingress allow-lists callers by\napp.kubernetes.io/name, and #1293 added the CronJob without adding it\nhere. The policy accepts the TCP connection and drops it mid-TLS, so the\nbinary reported\n\n  tls error: ... read: connection reset by peer\n\nretried ten times inside db.Open, and the Job died on\nactiveDeadlineSeconds. Nothing about the CronJob looked wrong: correct\nimage, correct command, correct DATABASE_URL, identical pod spec to the\nsweepers that work.\n\nThe values.yaml comment directly above this list warns about exactly\nthis — \"Adding a marketplace-api CronJob? It needs an entry HERE as well\nas its own manifest\" — and names two prior instances. This is the\nfourth, and it was shipped anyway.\n\nDiagnosed by running the failing CronJob and a working one back to back\nin the same minute: identical spec, one succeeded, one was reset. That\nruled out the database, the credentials and the image, and left the\ncaller identity.\n\nThis sweeper is load-bearing in a way the other three are not. It\ndestroys photographs shoppers uploaded and never bought, so a silent\nfailure is a retention breach that accumulates — \"we kept pictures of\nyour children because a CronJob was broken\" — rather than dead rows\nnobody misses.","tree":{"sha":"435ecbc7bd2faac89810ca148d7d16a06d5d6755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/trees/435ecbc7bd2faac89810ca148d7d16a06d5d6755"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/commits/9e753982e19341b6c295a5a19adc9eac6669ae04","verification":{"payload":"tree 435ecbc7bd2faac89810ca148d7d16a06d5d6755\nparent 24788a08c25e3ea45f97f5b4273639a27bb6ec5a\nauthor Mahesh Sangawar <mayu.b14@gmail.com> 1791182675 +1100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791182675 +1100\n\nfix(mark8ly): grant the artwork sweeper Postgres access (#960) (#1316)\n\nThe abandoned buyer-artwork reaper has failed EVERY run since it shipped\non 2026-10-03 — six consecutive failures over 35 hours.\n\nmark8ly-postgres-ingress allow-lists callers by\napp.kubernetes.io/name, and #1293 added the CronJob without adding it\nhere. The policy accepts the TCP connection and drops it mid-TLS, so the\nbinary reported\n\n  tls error: ... read: connection reset by peer\n\nretried ten times inside db.Open, and the Job died on\nactiveDeadlineSeconds. Nothing about the CronJob looked wrong: correct\nimage, correct command, correct DATABASE_URL, identical pod spec to the\nsweepers that work.\n\nThe values.yaml comment directly above this list warns about exactly\nthis — \"Adding a marketplace-api CronJob? It needs an entry HERE as well\nas its own manifest\" — and names two prior instances. This is the\nfourth, and it was shipped anyway.\n\nDiagnosed by running the failing CronJob and a working one back to back\nin the same minute: identical spec, one succeeded, one was reset. That\nruled out the database, the credentials and the image, and left the\ncaller identity.\n\nThis sweeper is load-bearing in a way the other three are not. It\ndestroys photographs shoppers uploaded and never bought, so a silent\nfailure is a retention breach that accumulates — \"we kept pictures of\nyour children because a CronJob was broken\" — rather than dead rows\nnobody misses.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0dTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARrwQAFHYOaUX0RuTkzAjRmTsjAHY\n5AJvji1EtvUAsBEXMSMSujGCrQBHiOY3LnNB0odGmi2fz+N2pdGNeDRB9cVLq/sP\niaBCXhZRRkPquI/upWoMtx4wKNccelnPeTOhLD3l3hjTFQDOboxK+wDYMQ3boADj\nClhwLBOg7QkyUyGS7zXp/eLgJNxP+8O4BWlrq3hSd2Ei9axl1nG7EH6S+RGGjkTV\nRjIBzVzLbNAcCPwQwF+E4HSBWOlgzoN7N24th0Kd0tRqaxwSGmTXmOrj+lgWsjcd\n5FZqg3z9d516ai4v+OdrTCs8G+maxTM7i6M26ezbduKncuUG4mQSXjLVpz8KLIzU\nyoTRtjGrQot8QztpF3N68Y2CZAYZnbtEnWfFntPM+GQc7UcSsj4Tf5KBmS6hbl4D\nDpLe1sIEmko1cpBsCdb0Cy7/qcMA3zQJbSRIg/OxmtNmLUoVZ+pp9Qn57pqEo8sh\nzh4XGucFoG/XO9GBZA82kNXhoEmEDhGMQEakqAJ3A5FfFJPjzVDRYrnJYLDStwJn\nngRWBuIUgRrRP4+RjR0UwDpnryaHSeYclkghBMYidR1GhEy9iK7TyoFNVRCl9g+o\n86iKB0QMyEf+ujOj2yACgG2VCLgv0eKih8/h/nikPQAlzf9YW3dLYWAZm8hxasEN\nVLPZ3d3AysEqKeAzIntB\n=26Qc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T06:44:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-