s://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahesh-sangawar","id":12147465,"login":"mahesh-sangawar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTQ3NDY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/76fabc9fca08045cb3d6b8aeb181eed1d79b2314/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:02:22Z","email":"mayu.b14@gmail.com","name":"Mahesh Sangawar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T13:02:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mark8ly): wire the private artwork bucket and deploy its reaper (#960) (#1293)\n\n* feat(mark8ly): wire the private artwork bucket and deploy its reaper (#960)\n\nBuyer artwork needs a bucket that is not world-readable, and the one piece\nof it that was already written has never been deployed.\n\nThree changes.\n\n**Both marketplace-api charts get MARKETPLACE_PRIVATE_GCS_BUCKET.** The\nstorefront pod writes buyer uploads (#963); the admin pod reads them back\nso a merchant can download the original (#968). Neither may fall back to\nthe public media bucket, which carries\n`roles/storage.objectViewer -> allUsers` — correct for a product shot,\ncatastrophic for a photograph of someone''s child. marketplace-api has no\nfallback by design: empty means the feature stays off rather than quietly\nlanding artwork somewhere world-readable.\n\n**The storefront chart gets MARKETPLACE_GCS_SIGNER_SA_EMAIL, which it was\nmissing entirely.** This is the one that would have burned us. Under GKE\nWorkload Identity ADC has no private key, so `bucket.SignedURL` cannot\nsign locally — marketplace-api only takes the IAM SignBlob path when this\nvariable is set. Without it every buyer upload fails at signing time with\nthe bucket correctly created, the KSA correctly bound and the env var for\nthe bucket correctly present: configured, correct-looking, emitting\nnothing. The admin chart has always set it; the storefront chart never\ndid, because until #963 it had no reason to sign anything.\n\n**The abandoned-artwork reaper gets a CronJob.** Shipped in the image by\nmark8ly#986. Every 6h against a 72h upload TTL, so worst-case retention is\n~78h rather than the ~96h a daily run would give; the cost of lateness\nhere is holding a person''s photograph longer than we said we would.\n\nThis CronJob is deliberately NOT a GCS lifecycle rule, and the template\nrecords why. Checkout snapshots the storage key into\norder_item_personalisations and copies no object, so a claimed order''s\nartwork is the same object under the same buyer-uploads/ key as the cart\nupload. An age-based bucket rule would delete the artwork of PAID orders\nonce it aged past the TTL, silently, long after the merchant stopped\nlooking. Only the database knows which objects are claimed.\n\nThe bucket itself and its IAM are not in this repo (no terraform here) and\nremain manual infra work.\n\n* chore(mark8ly): bump both marketplace-api chart versions\n\nct lint requires a version bump for any changed chart.","tree":{"sha":"82e71de916b295e26ef8a27adc6a7285bafbf5a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/trees/82e71de916b295e26ef8a27adc6a7285bafbf5a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/commits/76fabc9fca08045cb3d6b8aeb181eed1d79b2314","verification":{"payload":"tree 82e71de916b295e26ef8a27adc6a7285bafbf5a4\nparent c92dbe1ba75acc30e31151e8f150fece9dd0d16d\nauthor Mahesh Sangawar <mayu.b14@gmail.com> 1791032542 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791032542 +1000\n\nfeat(mark8ly): wire the private artwork bucket and deploy its reaper (#960) (#1293)\n\n* feat(mark8ly): wire the private artwork bucket and deploy its reaper (#960)\n\nBuyer artwork needs a bucket that is not world-readable, and the one piece\nof it that was already written has never been deployed.\n\nThree changes.\n\n**Both marketplace-api charts get MARKETPLACE_PRIVATE_GCS_BUCKET.** The\nstorefront pod writes buyer uploads (#963); the admin pod reads them back\nso a merchant can download the original (#968). Neither may fall back to\nthe public media bucket, which carries\n`roles/storage.objectViewer -> allUsers` — correct for a product shot,\ncatastrophic for a photograph of someone''s child. marketplace-api has no\nfallback by design: empty means the feature stays off rather than quietly\nlanding artwork somewhere world-readable.\n\n**The storefront chart gets MARKETPLACE_GCS_SIGNER_SA_EMAIL, which it was\nmissing entirely.** This is the one that would have burned us. Under GKE\nWorkload Identity ADC has no private key, so `bucket.SignedURL` cannot\nsign locally — marketplace-api only takes the IAM SignBlob path when this\nvariable is set. Without it every buyer upload fails at signing time with\nthe bucket correctly created, the KSA correctly bound and the env var for\nthe bucket correctly present: configured, correct-looking, emitting\nnothing. The admin chart has always set it; the storefront chart never\ndid, because until #963 it had no reason to sign anything.\n\n**The abandoned-artwork reaper gets a CronJob.** Shipped in the image by\nmark8ly#986. Every 6h against a 72h upload TTL, so worst-case retention is\n~78h rather than the ~96h a daily run would give; the cost of lateness\nhere is holding a person''s photograph longer than we said we would.\n\nThis CronJob is deliberately NOT a GCS lifecycle rule, and the template\nrecords why. Checkout snapshots the storage key into\norder_item_personalisations and copies no object, so a claimed order''s\nartwork is the same object under the same buyer-uploads/ key as the cart\nupload. An age-based bucket rule would delete the artwork of PAID orders\nonce it aged past the TTL, silently, long after the merchant stopped\nlooking. Only the database knows which objects are claimed.\n\nThe bucket itself and its IAM are not in this repo (no terraform here) and\nremain manual infra work.\n\n* chore(mark8ly): bump both marketplace-api chart versions\n\nct lint requires a version bump for any changed chart.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwPzeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARjYQAAcFaAxppepStvzx3itOtuxf\neNlAeCTaWli7wi5HyleNMTVlFeJJ6kYSzDvXRCGENB/CdBMxlMLYfxuqkRrkA7Sp\n94KzVe/XEmJYP97Tq8xfcZuJ1HrvOAzcipu30gLV+rMm/KnN9MEzOZ0lITWGo1eu\nbe/BvCz2RccGjOkJnQmP4FJyw1eNLAI57Nx9mfk9J2EekDLnA6QysT2RW6yCs4yV\nXktFKexqYxQDLQY74730j+bQSBtiQHElODRK2fMul/tMe6MAa0G+BxMeUHcBGfqj\nVInFh3clhdBfUBBYS8FtW3a65elCDcIr0MIerDB7HS/dPpZzdlycQXR+3l3bSmbm\nJFjgQAs6cp2+RjOh98EvVpaCx8uKXIBVIk0ViDDmWHBSrxotVPD6EdpZJ3tVfcV4\nVObpdscqs3MYHqaIA8d3VAvd/Z85r5a0DUcjyl6LEgkbrsO88k6UKs5WrSx3PORA\nFJeOR5lxXzmBjYgMns8+Nax9U0ROqAIgZV/6HVDePxPt1MGFHHkbskd5sPWz9HHV\n4c3z0AaXYh5PdEj3fIkyXn74lDjHuYsBVdwFmUUp4a6/NSeTrVhNPNvTbowAXx4M\nHfc2M6M37zOlRo6KkiwAG9VFYMnNg7XXA389Oun0+NCh5+5c6YGe2dB3iyL16B5L\naX5eS9BAghljH1Ve4aBl\n=3Whf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T13:02:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gi