,"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/3f9ac976f582f65dc9c6b1c849be1a2d45084791","node_id":"C_kwDOSGd6e9oAKDNmOWFjOTc2ZjU4MmY2NWRjOWM2YjFjODQ5YmUxYTJkNDUwODQ3OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/ce108a9c1abcaef4866597461d83cb829a9e00e5","sha":"ce108a9c1abcaef4866597461d83cb829a9e00e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/ce108a9c1abcaef4866597461d83cb829a9e00e5"}],"sha":"3f9ac976f582f65dc9c6b1c849be1a2d45084791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/3f9ac976f582f65dc9c6b1c849be1a2d45084791"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12147465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahesh-sangawar","id":12147465,"login":"mahesh-sangawar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTQ3NDY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/ce108a9c1abcaef4866597461d83cb829a9e00e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:57:30Z","email":"mayu.b14@gmail.com","name":"Mahesh Sangawar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:57:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(postiz): record the LinkedIn product combination that works (#1262)\n\n* docs(postiz): record the LinkedIn product combination that works\n\nThe comment said connect works once LinkedIn approves the Community\nManagement API request. It does not, and that sentence cost an afternoon\nof chasing an approval that was never the blocker.\n\nPostiz asks for seven scopes in a single authorization request and fails\nthe whole request if any is refused. CM API grants the four organization\nscopes but LinkedIn forces it to be the only product on an app, which\nexcludes OpenID Connect sign-in and so openid/profile. Advertising API\ncarries the same organization scopes without that rule, so it can sit\nalongside OIDC — approved for postiz-app on 2026-10-01, and all seven\nscopes now verify as accepted on both callbacks.\n\nRecord the three products that must stay on the app, why the CM-only app\nis a dead end, and how to re-test by replaying the generated auth URL,\nsince a failure here leaves nothing in the backend log at all.\n\n* chore(postiz): bump chart to 0.1.7\n\nchart_version_policy.py requires an increment for any change under\ncharts/apps/<chart>/ that is not a top-level values file, comments\nincluded.","tree":{"sha":"7292814b905425f60ae2773335aef74f8a1fd6e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/trees/7292814b905425f60ae2773335aef74f8a1fd6e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/commits/ce108a9c1abcaef4866597461d83cb829a9e00e5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7292814b905425f60ae2773335aef74f8a1fd6e5\nparent 5940cf7e2b9f720c169c342b9e461a7afe8d5578\nauthor Mahesh Sangawar <mayu.b14@gmail.com> 1790855850 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790855850 +1000\n\ndocs(postiz): record the LinkedIn product combination that works (#1262)\n\n* docs(postiz): record the LinkedIn product combination that works\n\nThe comment said connect works once LinkedIn approves the Community\nManagement API request. It does not, and that sentence cost an afternoon\nof chasing an approval that was never the blocker.\n\nPostiz asks for seven scopes in a single authorization request and fails\nthe whole request if any is refused. CM API grants the four organization\nscopes but LinkedIn forces it to be the only product on an app, which\nexcludes OpenID Connect sign-in and so openid/profile. Advertising API\ncarries the same organization scopes without that rule, so it can sit\nalongside OIDC — approved for postiz-app on 2026-10-01, and all seven\nscopes now verify as accepted on both callbacks.\n\nRecord the three products that must stay on the app, why the CM-only app\nis a dead end, and how to re-test by replaying the generated auth URL,\nsince a failure here leaves nothing in the backend log at all.\n\n* chore(postiz): bump chart to 0.1.7\n\nchart_version_policy.py requires an increment for any change under\ncharts/apps/<chart>/ that is not a top-level values file, comments\nincluded.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkqqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARIMQAFB+TZQkAb63XR9XGj7LlHED\nV4qN+MR0OQhoqB1MttBAfKs7Ut90/TUadL7j9WZ76U/kl2IXQnLoi0fKi8tSMPNO\nQKFqprRiWtV+eei6O8PPBOCGNATKht1UtIyYdW+/dsfyosn51hP4EacMSZ09aE8H\n19B5TXAaRrywWbRXIOVwf1aUNkptaLk2f+nlxBf+A+qXa5Ut5VR1WQkMriBHmKGQ\nLKyESuwekXIPVvSXww+dtG9n7CznER5HZi6E0p10NDXMO6R1qzVXa3Er/2Z21vcq\nRNQ+KYfxtTKsO5iwnub8Ve+q+GW52f+9OVLki6m+0ojaAtMFNvs3mhma6SPj2ulp\n0AeV+vBJrV5AAxAaf4x/0FM73DRPynhjVCmoyQnBOaegpuNnMRfxJ2hZ4HSVayfr\nNqsn58WVnPflWIGEPXFgg3aIDl+j7jEC2exTD1+9TT/kxbC5sCXrBSDJNjIoMaPM\nodEdctTIjwk5E00lwDWeWpnmNcUrAUNHwPgu+pvE0jKPxFEr81Cr9HpboZpsB4YY\nJZmbnbs0uGBEcFYajVGA6ilBXYbZ/3RodL1pkryzrzFXgmhU2nDK50YT90ik4wmo\nrpRYLWoUwm60qBCSwr+JFkDuox9vO/kOQ4gdYxZUzxFNxH5yz4