admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/e61033a04b645ebbb9486b41a6681e5ccf99794f","node_id":"C_kwDOSGd6e9oAKGU2MTAzM2EwNGI2NDVlYmJiOTQ4NmI0MWE2NjgxZTVjY2Y5OTc5NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4","sha":"4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4"}],"sha":"e61033a04b645ebbb9486b41a6681e5ccf99794f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/e61033a04b645ebbb9486b41a6681e5ccf99794f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12147465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahesh-sangawar","id":12147465,"login":"mahesh-sangawar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTQ3NDY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:13:38Z","email":"mayu.b14@gmail.com","name":"Mahesh Sangawar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:13:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Drop the beautyandcruor staging host now the cutover is confirmed (#1232)\n\nbeautyandcruor.com has been serving the new site since the address records\nmoved and the user has confirmed it working, so the\nbeautyandcruor.tesserix.app entry in the frontendApps allow list has nothing\nleft to protect.\n\nIt was already inert: the chart''s VirtualService lists only the two real\nhosts, so the staging hostname stopped routing when tls.enabled went true and\nhas been answering 404 since. This removes the allow-list entry that outlived\nit.\n\nThe noindex rule needs no action. nginx keys X-Robots-Tag off a `map $host`\nwhose default is \"noindex, nofollow\" with empty values for the two production\nhosts, so it stopped applying to the live site by itself and still covers any\nother hostname that reaches the pod. Verified: no X-Robots-Tag on\nbeautyandcruor.com or www.\n\nAlso records, next to `gateways`, that restoring the staging host means\nrestoring the frontendApps entry too. That coupling is not visible from the\nchart and is what produced the 403 during this cutover.","tree":{"sha":"38019f52d6cd21708ff4d2448e4daf191da3a5db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/trees/38019f52d6cd21708ff4d2448e4daf191da3a5db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/commits/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4","verification":{"payload":"tree 38019f52d6cd21708ff4d2448e4daf191da3a5db\nparent aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8\nauthor Mahesh Sangawar <mayu.b14@gmail.com> 1790572418 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790572418 +1000\n\nDrop the beautyandcruor staging host now the cutover is confirmed (#1232)\n\nbeautyandcruor.com has been serving the new site since the address records\nmoved and the user has confirmed it working, so the\nbeautyandcruor.tesserix.app entry in the frontendApps allow list has nothing\nleft to protect.\n\nIt was already inert: the chart''s VirtualService lists only the two real\nhosts, so the staging hostname stopped routing when tls.enabled went true and\nhas been answering 404 since. This removes the allow-list entry that outlived\nit.\n\nThe noindex rule needs no action. nginx keys X-Robots-Tag off a `map $host`\nwhose default is \"noindex, nofollow\" with empty values for the two production\nhosts, so it stopped applying to the live site by itself and still covers any\nother hostname that reaches the pod. Verified: no X-Robots-Tag on\nbeautyandcruor.com or www.\n\nAlso records, next to `gateways`, that restoring the staging host means\nrestoring the frontendApps entry too. That coupling is not visible from the\nchart and is what produced the 403 during this cutover.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufeCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsccQAIMkMoLU0aETuRULK5ZGrSGs\n+22V3ree4zDSusfhSLH/dQbQ7lbW77MoCPx8WxUGl8Oj/sb/QoYsgzjG+RjeBSxV\nF9sV8gZ5y5YEy0JBuSQQ8MQzqhIiAwYlH5HxlhVtF3yRIdOkMbYHiNfGzI/cNju2\nmFlf+eraJQO3NhgT6ag/2Zz/tRtSf3TN8zWGnhV87ditEg6tN25l6qmUwduHZ5t8\n59Wyo0tayIAPEJ79chZmg97/OjAL7Jc+Pg7YEegz0FdQoax4K68K9EPhZ9LNCPCo\n37JSpRK1zh4HU54CuS+vsLf7ffZ6jcIIPDJHBSnF3LqzFc+GlqunFi8S7BHPDHnL\n1aS7Aqh2eSneqPnkFsyWZdQYiymF8ZyuRD9GXr3J3R0idSJP9HPsO3aClwbNw+Sl\n8l/pmPUFffLWDVFwRZQ8yx5IutRyFQJs02a2Y2eBNz5zIt29CRJ8zVDxRnQnUutY\n6BeMeoOzFFxXIkY457eOa9AMhymkofIJUt8Wur53C9GZX0gfBaWErDRdhLXCkBUr\nMOaRngcduO6Ne/jmHjDLpiB1I/YmNVEb6XRs9Nbd/3jeRjNYkw5gn6J5UaWCUEBa\nuSgosOCowddc822WU85Dwc2yDsNjlqMdm3gNJEl6xix4ZI3xRepjg+SqNbqXtE6O\nqgwxQwiafzu+/tNXv4dM\n=oBrS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T05:13:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4","node_id":"C_kwDOSGd6e9oAKDRlZGRiYzE4OWE1MjBmMDIxYTM0YjY5ZDEwMDMyMGVlOGMzMDFkYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commit/aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8","sha":"aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8"}],"sha":"4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/4eddbc189a520f021a34b69d100320ee8c301db4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12147465?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mahesh-sangawar","id":12147465,"login":"mahesh-sangawar","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTQ3NDY1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mahesh-sangawar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/commits/aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:47:11Z","email":"mayu.b14@gmail.com","name":"Mahesh Sangawar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:47:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Quote the custom-domain HSTS max-age so browsers accept it (#1231)\n\nThe gateway emitted `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=3.1536e+07;\nincludeSubDomains; preload`. RFC 6797 requires max-age to be digits, so\nevery browser rejected the directive outright. HSTS has been doing nothing\non every domain served by this gateway.\n\nsecurityHeaders.hsts.maxAge was an unquoted 31536000, and Helm renders a\nlarge integer in scientific notation. The value is interpolated directly\ninto the Lua that builds the header, so what shipped was 3.1536e+07.\n\nThe two EnvoyFilters in charts/thirdparty/istio-config were unaffected\nbecause they hardcode the string rather than templating a number, which is\nwhy only the custom-domain filter carried the broken value and the fault\nnever showed up on tesserix.app or mark8ly.com.\n\nThis is the same trap already documented on\n`enquiry.admin.uploads.maxBytes` in charts/apps/beautyandcruor — a string,\nnot a number. Quoting is the entire fix.\n\nFound while verifying the beautyandcruor.com cutover. Confirmed present on\nyahvismartfarm.com too, so this restores HSTS for every custom domain, not\njust the new one.","tree":{"sha":"ffef1fcae2d53bfd237ce74ed5236a956095ea09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/trees/ffef1fcae2d53bfd237ce74ed5236a956095ea09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tesserix/tesserix-k8s/git/commits/aa6a1f4ec1deac53aee8996c6d200e53c0ef6da8","verification":{"payload":"tree ffef1fcae2d53bfd237ce74ed5236a956095ea09\nparent c72609b59a2cb0b2b4dd9972cb72a54afa3eba1d\nauthor Mahesh Sangawar <mayu.b14@gmail.com> 1790570831 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790570831 +1000\n\nQuote the custom-domain HSTS max-age so browsers accept it (#1231)\n\nThe gateway emitted `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=3.1536e+07;\nincludeSubDomains; preload`. RFC 6797 requires max-age to be digits, so\nevery browser rejected the directive outright. HSTS has been doing nothing\non every domain served by this gateway.\n\nsecurityHeaders.hsts.maxAge was an unquoted 31536000, and Helm renders a\nlarge integer in scientific notation. The value is interpolated directly\ninto the Lua that builds the header, so what shipped was 3.1536e+07.\n\nThe two EnvoyFilters in charts/thirdparty/istio-config were unaffected\nbecause they hardcode the string rather than templating a number, which is\nwhy only the custom-domain filter carried the broken value and the fault\nnever showed up on tesserix.app or mark8ly.com.\n\nThis is the same trap already documented on\n`enquiry.admin.uploads.maxBytes` in charts/apps/beautyandcruor — a string,\nnot a number. Quoting is the entire fix.\n\nFound while verifying the beautyandcruor.com cutover. Confirmed present on\nyahvismartfarm.com too, so this restores HSTS for every custom domain, not\njust the new one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufFPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMKAQAKiLSPGonhejU4jkTIrmGcKM\nI+3c9vexx5p7OyDGwcyL/QdhtH7Mn8cO/RS2Gmdr62y26FJw6Z+t3h568l8mW39r\nlTYsC0Q18upJBhBawL8ue0TST2DfaexiFhysLtl54aEus1tziB5qF/WOtrLp4FOZ\nH4C82ReTvNFzD9MqrWy9/I12qwGVy0r6O80UcabcPtEMvSFZColaZ2KNHt8+ZNYx\nL1WwqbwG4s4blwxYyLKNpb38VkgMQ6u4ypoLaovGGWFs3NPH6G41