wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73","id":181457780,"login":"Stoff73","node_id":"U_kgDOCtDTdA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/a962fe238dd2517bfc07eb60e8f1a3f312db3f3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T12:31:03Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T12:31:03Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"message":"docs(session): context-clear handover 2026-05-13-session-3 + slice 3 deploy note update\n\nG-4-b slice 3 PASS — handover snapshots all 3 HIGH closed (H-1 admin\nwrite MFA, H-2 legacy GDPR erasure removed, H-3 spouse consent refactor),\n60 new pinning tests, 0 regressions, both commits pushed. Deploy note\nextended to include the slice 3 files in the still-pending combined\nupload manifest (slices 1+2+3 now 4 consecutive sessions pending on\ncsjones.co/fynla_inter).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bdb7d765d35727406c489f942cd1317ce607d6ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/trees/bdb7d765d35727406c489f942cd1317ce607d6ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/commits/a962fe238dd2517bfc07eb60e8f1a3f312db3f3b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181457780?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73","id":181457780,"login":"Stoff73","node_id":"U_kgDOCtDTdA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commit/a962fe238dd2517bfc07eb60e8f1a3f312db3f3b","node_id":"C_kwDOSGm9vdoAKGE5NjJmZTIzOGRkMjUxN2JmYzA3ZWI2MGU4ZjFhM2YzMTJkYjNmM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commit/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429","sha":"711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429"}],"sha":"a962fe238dd2517bfc07eb60e8f1a3f312db3f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/a962fe238dd2517bfc07eb60e8f1a3f312db3f3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181457780?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73","id":181457780,"login":"Stoff73","node_id":"U_kgDOCtDTdA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T10:35:06Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T10:35:06Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"message":"fix(security): G-4-b slice 3 HIGH H-3 — spouse consent refactor + slice 3 close\n\nH-3 — `FamilyMembersController::handleSpouseCreation` (existing-account\nbranch) auto-linked accounts AND mutated the invitee''s own fields\nWITHOUT consent. An attacker who knew their target''s email could in a\nsingle POST:\n\n  - set the victim''s `spouse_id` to the attacker\n  - flip the victim''s `marital_status` to ''married''\n  - OVERWRITE the victim''s `annual_employment_income` with an\n    attacker-supplied value\n  - OVERWRITE the victim''s address (line 1/2, city, county, postcode)\n    if blank\n  - auto-accept bidirectional `SpousePermission` rows so the attacker\n    immediately gained data-sharing read access to every endpoint that\n    checks `hasAcceptedSpousePermission()` (Estate IHT, gifting, trusts,\n    joint accounts, most module roll-ups)\n\nThe victim received only an after-the-fact \"your account has been\nlinked\" email — never given the chance to refuse.\n\nFix shape (consent-first):\n\n1. `handleSpouseCreation` existing-account branch now creates ONLY a\n   pending `SpousePermission` row + a `FamilyMember` record on the\n   inviter''s side (so their UI reflects \"spouse: <name> (pending)\").\n   It NEVER mutates any field on the invitee, and NEVER sets\n   `spouse_id` / `marital_status` on either user. Idempotent — a\n   duplicate invite reuses the existing pending permission.\n\n2. `SpousePermissionController::accept` extended to be the single\n   source of truth for finalising a spouse link. If the current user\n   has no `spouse_id` yet and a pending invitation targets them,\n   `accept` atomically sets `spouse_id` + `marital_status` on both\n   users, creates the reciprocal accepted `SpousePermission` and the\n   reciprocal `FamilyMember` on the invitee''s side, and cache-\n   invalidates both. Race-safe via `lockForUpdate()` on the inviter.\n\n3. `SpousePermissionController::reject` mirrors accept — pre-link\n   pending invitations can be rejected without any field mutation\n   anywhere.\n\n4. New mailable `SpouseDataSharingRequest` + template replaces the\n   misleading \"your account has been linked\" email for the\n   pre-acceptance state. `SpouseAccountLinked` is still used after the\n   invitee accepts.\n\n13 new pinning tests in `FamilyMembersControllerSpouseConsentTest.php`\ncover every H-3 invariant: no auto-link, no field mutation, pending\npermission created, no reciprocal direction created at invite time, no\nreciprocal `FamilyMember` on invitee side at invite time, correct mail\nclass sent, response payload shape, idempotency, and the full\naccept-finalises-link / reject-leaves-state-untouched flows.\n\nArch test exception added for `SpousePermissionController` (uses\n`DB::transaction` for the atomic accept; same allowance shape as the\nexisting exceptions for `FamilyMembersController`, `PaymentController`).\n\nDocs:\n\n- `Plans/test-gauntlet-plan-v1.md` — slice 3 marked PASS.\n- `May/May13Updates/g-4-b-slice-3-controllers-audit.md` — status →\n  PASS, all 3 HIGHs documented as closed with file references.\n- `May/May12Updates/triage-backlog.md` — M-1 + L-1..L-5 + M-2 candidate\n  + cosmetic copy review logged as E-16..E-23.\n\nPest serial baseline post-slice-3: 2975 passing, 0 regressions,\n1 skipped (pre-existing). New tests in this slice: 60 (39 admin MFA\nacross H-1, 8 legacy GDPR route pins across H-2, 13 spouse consent\ninvariants across H-3).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e32e2e33f69a581506db92af5fd83fda89bc1e02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/trees/e32e2e33f69a581506db92af5fd83fda89bc1e02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/commits/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181457780?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73","id":181457780,"login":"Stoff73","node_id":"U_kgDOCtDTdA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commit/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429","node_id":"C_kwDOSGm9vdoAKDcxMWIwZDdmMGUzNWE2YWVkNzAzZmY3ZjQ4ZTQ2OWJmNTQwYjE0Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commit/09302e95c205f708f197bf731f1616b18541988c","sha":"09302e95c205f708f197bf731f1616b18541988c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/09302e95c205f708f197bf731f1616b18541988c"}],"sha":"711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/711b0d7f0e35a6aed703ff7f48e469bf540b1429"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181457780?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Stoff73","id":181457780,"login":"Stoff73","node_id":"U_kgDOCtDTdA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/commits/09302e95c205f708f197bf731f1616b18541988c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-13T10:34:36Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-13T10:34:36Z","email":"c.jones@csjones.co","name":"Stoff73"},"message":"fix(security): G-4-b slice 3 HIGH H-1 + H-2 — admin write MFA + legacy GDPR erasure removed\n\nH-1 — Admin write endpoints lacked `mfa.verified`. Split the\n`routes/api.php` admin route group into a read-only group (dashboard,\nlistings, AI provider GET, ai-audit, backup/list, user-metrics,\ndiscount-codes GET) and a write group wrapped with `mfa.verified` (user\nCRUD, AI-provider switch, backup create/restore/delete, discount-code\nCRUD). 17 admin write endpoints are now MFA-gated; reads remain reachable\nwithout an MFA-claimed token so half-authenticated admins can still\ninspect state. 39 new pinning tests in\n`AdminWriteEndpointsRequireMfaTest.php` cover the three states (MFA\nadmin without MFA token → 403; MFA admin with `mfa_verified` token →\nnot 403; legacy non-MFA admin → not 403).\n\nH-2 — 4 legacy single-step GDPR erasure routes (`POST /erasure`,\n`GET /erasure/status`, `POST /erasure/{id}/confirm`,\n`POST /erasure/{id}/cancel`) bypassed the new 3-step verify+execute\nflow (no MFA, no email code, no confirmation phrase). Frontend never\nused them (privacyService.js only calls /initiate, /verify, /execute,\n/resend-code). Routes deleted; controller methods retained with\n`@deprecated` docblocks for inert admin-tooling use only. 8 new\npinning tests in `LegacyGdprErasureRoutesAreUnroutableTest.php` assert\nthe legacy paths are unroutable via the route table (which is exact —\nHTTP status would be 405 because `routes/web.php` has an SPA\ncatch-all GET).\n\nPre-existing `Tests\\Feature\\Auth\\GDPRApiTest > Data Erasure` describe\nblock exercised the deleted legacy flow; replaced with a single\npreview-user-blocked-from-initiating-erasure invariant against the new\n`/erasure/initiate` route. The legacy CRUD behaviour is now durably\ncovered by `LegacyGdprErasureRoutesAreUnroutableTest`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"75927d4171668209face17f79c9a2031511c9a6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/trees/75927d4171668209face17f79c9a2031511c9a6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Stoff73/fynlainternational/git/commits/09302e95c205f708f197bf731f1616b18541988c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181457780?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Stoff73/e