owing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c5e2ee9ddc778836da03437604d9be7eac055dd3","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGM1ZTJlZTlkZGM3Nzg4MzZkYTAzNDM3NjA0ZDliZTdlYWMwNTVkZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","sha":"bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071","sha":"9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071"}],"sha":"c5e2ee9ddc778836da03437604d9be7eac055dd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c5e2ee9ddc778836da03437604d9be7eac055dd3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:59:27Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:45Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Record the sweep honestly, and repoint the design doc at the plugin layout\n\nThe CHANGELOG entry for the em dash sweep claimed that column-aligned blocks\nkept their widths, \"verified by comparing column positions across 241 blocks\nbefore and after\". That was false, and the check behind it was too weak to\nnotice: it compared column positions only within blocks where every line shared\na single column, which is exactly the shape the damaged blocks did not have.\nReview caught what the check could not. The entry now states what broke, what\nrepaired it, and what the diff-aware check measures instead.\n\nA second review pass is recorded alongside it: the fence gate that counted\ninstead of matching, the retired-path lookbehind that excluded the characters a\npath is written after, the live broken instruction in present.sh that two gates\nmissed, the two gates that disagreed about the same string, three wrong Gemini\nfacts that sat under a heading saying \"verified\", and five of eight wave exits\nin the twin plan that could not fail. It also records that\nsecurity.allowedExtensions gates Gemini CLI extension loading as well as\ninstalling, for local paths as much as git URLs, which inverts a risk in that\nplan.\n\ndocs/language-agnostic-design.md had nine paths into the claude-catalog tree\nremoved in the marketplace migration, and two live plugin files link to it for\na stack list and a schema, so it could not simply be archived. The paths are\nrewritten and the header says so. Whether the design still describes the target\nwas not re-assessed, and the status stays draft.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2540203b301905740252ca1a617936664f214575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/2540203b301905740252ca1a617936664f214575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDljOTRlNTEwMzIxMmE3MTQxZGZjNWY4MmU3ZWIzZGNmMjM5ZGQwNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33","sha":"40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33"}],"sha":"9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9c94e5103212a7141dfc5f82e7eb3dcf239dd071"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:21Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:45Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Make the fence gate match fences, and stop two gates disagreeing\n\nvalidate_code_fences() asserted that each file held an even number of fence\nlines. A file carrying one stray closer and one unclosed opener holds an even\nnumber, so the gate passed precisely the combination it exists to catch. It is\nnow built on scan_fences(), a CommonMark state machine shared with\nvalidate_plugin_root_refs() so the two cannot disagree about which lines are\ncode: a closer must be bare and at least as long as its opener, a fence with an\ninfo string can never close anything, and blocks do not nest.\n\nThe retired-path lookbehind was (?<![\\w/.-]), which refuses a match after /, .\nor -, and those are the characters a path is written after. ./claude-catalog/x,\n../claude-catalog/x, ~/dev/claude-registry/claude-catalog/x and\n$ROOT/claude-catalog/x all passed: four of the six forms that occur here. It is\n(?<![\\w-]) now, and the scan follows scripts/ and hooks/ over every file rather\nthan two extensions, which is what it took to see scripts/present.sh.\n\nThe bare plugin-root check rejected the variable used as a cwd value in a\ndocumented MCP snippet, which is correct usage, and its rationale was half\nfalse: install-local.sh rewrites the variable only inside the loop over\nagents/, while skills and references are copied with cp -R and never rewritten.\ntest-clean-install.sh had not been tightened at all, so material could satisfy\none gate and fail the other. Both now apply one rule: a bare reference is an\nerror in agent prose outside a code fence, and legal everywhere else.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02c241e2c831219aa33929f9c66db330fd2ff99b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/02c241e2c831219aa33929f9c66db330fd2ff99b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDQwZTQ3OTQ2Yjc5YTIwYWE2Mzc5NzRiMTVhMTU3MzI3MDI3MDlkMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4","sha":"fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4"}],"sha":"40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/40e47946b79a20aa637974b15a15732702709d33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:56Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Drop category from the six plugin manifests\n\nclaude plugin validate warned on every one: the field belongs in the\nmarketplace entry and Claude Code ignores it at load time. The marketplace\nentries already carry the same value, asserted before removal. The whole\nmarketplace now validates with no warnings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"830b10ae957ee47bd933d4baf4bfd84ea0fac7e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/830b10ae957ee47bd933d4baf4bfd84ea0fac7e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGZjZjM4NDBiMGQ3Y2FjY2M4ZTJhMzFmOGZlMTU2MmVhZmI4NDBhZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00","sha":"fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00"}],"sha":"fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcf3840b0d7caccc8e2a31f8fe1562eafb840ad4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:31Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Fix present.sh, which named a deleted file and could not run on macOS\n\nLine 125 told the model to follow a brand standard at\nclaude-catalog/policies/accenture-branding.md, removed in the marketplace\nmigration. It points at the accenture-branding skill now, which the agent\npreloads. This was the only live broken instruction in the repository, and the\nretired-path scan missed it twice over: scripts/ was out of scope, and the glob\ncovered .md and .json only.\n\nTwo lines below it, realpath -m is a GNU extension. BSD realpath rejects the\nflag, and under set -e that ended the script before it ever built a prompt, so\non a Mac nobody got far enough to follow the dead reference. Replaced with\nmkdir -p and cd \"$dir\" && pwd -P, which is portable and creates the output\ndirectory the old line assumed already existed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0c5f2e748bf6d208cbea5624c21c7906cd8af7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/b0c5f2e748bf6d208cbea5624c21c7906cd8af7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGZjNzBlYzQ4MzU1NGVkZWM5YmQ2YjlhZWUwODQ2Zjk2OTM0ZDZkMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb","sha":"6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb"}],"sha":"fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fc70ec483554edec9bd6b9aee0846f96934d6d00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:59:13Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:00:43Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Repair six stray fences and finish the em dash sweep without breaking columns\n\nSix files carried a stray closing fence left over from an earlier edit. A lone\nfence opens a block rather than erroring, so everything after it renders as\ncode: in python-to-java-migration-expert that was the quality checklist and\nboth reference links, and in analysis-architecture/functional-analyst 54 lines\nincluding both reference links. Four files whose templates quote a\nthree-backtick fence were promoted to four-backtick outer fences, uniformly per\nconstruct rather than only where the damage showed.\n\n492 em dashes removed. The 311 sites a line-for-line diff can classify are not\n311 commas: 211 commas, 69 colons, 8 parenthetical and 23 rewritten into a new\nsentence, because a dash carrying \"namely\" turns into a list the moment a comma\nreplaces it. 245 remain in plugins, every one inside a language-tagged fence\nwhere the character is part of a comment being illustrated.\n\nThree column-aligned blocks did not survive the first pass. schematics.md:76\nand :167 were left 59 characters wide against a diagram whose other rules are\n60, bootstrap-protocol.md:78 and :79 lost a column against the five rows they\nalign with, and tanstack/SKILL.md:30 took a comma where its nine siblings take\na colon and padding. All repaired: the 27 box rules in schematics.md measure\n60, the seven bootstrap-protocol.md rows place their pipes at columns 6, 38 and\n87, and no closed box in the changed set moved. 11 further em dashes had become\npipes rather than a sanctioned separator, all in === === status banners, one of\nthem directly above a pipe table where a reader would take it for a column.\n\nAlso: the deliberation eval told a human to copy agents out of a directory that\nhas not existed since the plugin migration, and bmad/workflows.json carried the\nsame dead path in its _comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"32b00181550420bc5586c2215cab3e6258801860","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/32b00181550420bc5586c2215cab3e6258801860"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDZkMGNhZGQzNGI0ODFiZGExYzllNjkzODlhZjE1ZmQ4YzhjZWQ3ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420","sha":"d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420"}],"sha":"6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6d0cadd34b481bda1c9e69389af15fd8c8ced7eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:06Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:06Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Add gemini-interop, and plan the twin registry it exists to serve\n\nA seventh plugin holding the Gemini CLI knowledge needed to plan, and later\nbuild, a registry that runs on Google''s Gemini CLI instead of Claude Code.\nFour skills and one agent: gemini-cli-expert for the CLI itself,\ngemini-extension-authoring for the distribution unit, cross-host-parity for\nthe mapping in both directions and the four structures that have no\ncounterpart, capability-parity-sync for the mirroring procedure and its\nledger, and gemini-porter, which performs the translation and refuses the\ncases that need restructuring first.\n\nEvery claim about Gemini CLI is checked against the released v0.57.0 tag\nrather than main, and the load-bearing ones against the installed bundle.\nThe skill is cross-host-parity rather than claude-gemini-parity because\nvalidate_skills() forbids \"claude\" and \"anthropic\" in a skill name.\n\ndocs/gemini-twin/twin-registry-plan.md plans the twin as one source repo\ncarrying a committed twin tree, with eight waves and one exit criterion\neach, stated as a command that exits non-zero while the wave is incomplete.\nMeasured readiness: 45 of 46 skills port with no edits, 77 of 86 agents are\nmechanical, 9 agents lose their dispatch mechanism because Gemini sub-agents\ncannot dispatch other sub-agents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"657585ec959a2b62d1ba3eb21ed9dff2006429bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/657585ec959a2b62d1ba3eb21ed9dff2006429bf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGQ4OThiNmRlMGNmOGM5NTllMWE2YjkwOWEyOTRkNjU2OTc3YmM0MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","sha":"bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067"}],"sha":"d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d898b6de0cf8c959e1a6b909a294d656977bc420"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T06:15:00Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T06:15:00Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Record the three commits on main that do not build, and drop the colliding commands\n\ndcf474f, a2cdfc3 and 961e76d each fail the validator with 94 errors, because\nthey were staged with a pathspec meant to leave a concurrent job''s files alone.\n'':(exclude)plugins/*/references/*'' also matches a skill''s own references\ndirectory, so 21 new reference files were held back while the SKILL.md files\nlinking them went in. The links resolved one commit later.\n\nThe history stays as it is: main is shared, and a force push would hand anyone\nwho had already pulled a diverging history to untangle by hand. The changelog\nnow says so, so a bisect through that range is not a mystery.\n\nSix slash commands in the user''s ~/.claude/commands collided by name with\nregistry capabilities (codebase-mapper, functional-analyst, technical-analyst\nand the three python-to-*-migration-expert), which made routing between the two\nnon-deterministic. Removed, with the seven memory commands left untouched. They\nremain recoverable from the claude-config repository.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4744194be9e10ea4a45816e457bf5721dfb39ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/e4744194be9e10ea4a45816e457bf5721dfb39ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGJkODIyZmRhYzg3YTJlMWJlMmRlMGM5Nzk3NGJlYjQzMWRmYzIwNjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e","sha":"fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e"}],"sha":"bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/bd822fdac87a2e1be2de0c97974beb431dfc2067"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T00:00:21Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T00:00:21Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Fix the installer for example links, and align the docs with the gates as coded\n\nThe repaired clean-install assertion earned its keep on its first real run. The\nseven new example links use ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/examples/, and install-local.sh\ncopied only references/ while rewriting only that one prefix, so all seven\nresolved to a directory that had never been created. The installer now mirrors\nthe plugin root, copying references/ and examples/ under it, which leaves a\nsingle prefix to rewrite instead of two rules where one was missing.\n\nThat check had been dead code until an hour ago: it matched absolute paths\nagainst /Users/, while the harness installs into mktemp -d.\n\nDocs: evals-guide.md said nothing in CI validates the eval schema and that every\nnegative names the sibling it routes to. The first was false one commit after it\nwas written, and the second is now the opposite of the rule, so a contributor\nfollowing it gets a red build. Both of its worked examples would have failed CI\nthemselves, and one cited a fixture that does not exist. how-to-write-a-capability\ncarried the same two defects plus four more: a retired-name row describing a\nbacktick match the gate no longer uses, a gate table missing five entries, a\nbudget figure that did not separate warn from fail, and a reference-path rule\nthat told authors to use ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} everywhere, which is right for\nagent bodies and wrong for all 15 skills that correctly use a relative link.\n\nThe changelog claimed the 10000-character body ceiling is a hard error with no\nlegacy exception. It is a warning that never sets a non-zero exit. Five gates\nhad reached main with no entry at all.\n\nWiki: the pipeline output contract table had lost the owner column and five live\nID prefixes, and a sweep found ten more conventions it never listed. Neither the\nCI section nor the architecture flow mentioned the clean-install gate, which\nlanded one commit before the wiki was written. Volatile counts are now\nmeasurement commands, since the corpus moved twice while this was being written.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9adf15e148f4de4bf59ebb7b69faa06cbc5214c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/9adf15e148f4de4bf59ebb7b69faa06cbc5214c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGZjYjI1Zjg2YjI5YzAyY2NjYjY0OTQ5ZjdmNDYzNWYxYzE2NzQ2OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974","sha":"d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974"}],"sha":"fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fcb25f86b29c02cccb64949f7f4635f1c167468e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:56:55Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:56:55Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Clear the em dash out of the output templates, and give the narrative evals a home\n\nThe prose sweep skipped everything inside code fences. Right for code, wrong for\none category: 255 em dashes sat on heading, bullet, table and ID lines inside\nmarkdown-fenced output templates across 51 files. Those are the literal strings\nthe agents write into challenger reports, risk registers and client\ndeliverables, so every artefact this registry produced still came out full of\nthem. 255 down to 3, and the 3 are inside an ASCII box where the character is\ndrawing, not punctuation. Aligned blocks keep their columns: the colon moves\nonto the label and the padding follows.\n\nA comma introduced by the earlier sweep had changed an instruction.\n\"do NOT touch other UC''s methods, those will be filled by other invocations\"\nadmits a restrictive reading, that only the methods due to be filled are off\nlimits. It is two sentences now, and a three-detector sweep found no others.\n\n18 table cells reading `n/a` meant \"none\" or \"always\", not \"not applicable\", in\ncolumns where every other row states a real condition. They say what they mean.\n\nThe seven developer output sections ended with \"if you could not run them, say\nso\", which made the only falsifiable claim in each unfailable: an agent that\nsays it could not run cargo test satisfied it. Each now states what the\ndelivered code must satisfy as written, readable from the code. actor-feature-\nmapper said five files and required six. developer-rust told the agent to emit\nfile content next to a non-negotiable rule to write with the Write tool; the two\nare ordered now, not offered as alternatives.\n\nSeven example files had existed since before the migration with nothing\nreferencing them, so Claude never learned they were there. Each is linked from\nits agent, with content verified rather than assumed. functional-analyst had no\nroom, so its three least-used templates moved to a reference file.\n\nThe eight narrative eval files were orphans of the pre-migration format, sitting\nbeside the JSON directories that superseded them, except they were not\nsuperseded: they carry the input context, the exact prompt and the\nmust-not-contain list that neither JSON shape has room for. Seven moved into\ntheir capability''s eval directory as scenarios.md, with a header saying how the\nthree files relate. The eighth covers the pipeline rather than a capability and\nstays where it is, now saying so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3718f759ae1d5af80cbbed37e82e87ecb5dfec54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/3718f759ae1d5af80cbbed37e82e87ecb5dfec54"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGQyZWMyOTY2YThjMDhmMTRlNmJiOWVhZTE0MTRlMTRlZTU0NWY5NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa","sha":"961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa"}],"sha":"d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d2ec2966a8c08f14e6bb9eae1414e14ee545f974"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:45:03Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:45:03Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Give the brand skill actual assets instead of constants to re-derive\n\nThe audit''s rubric names this case verbatim: assets/ is for brand material, and\naccenture-branding was a 196-line prose file with nothing beside it, so every\nconsumer re-derived 51 colour and typography constants by reading tables.\n\nThree assets now carry the values: brand-tokens.json (palette in hex and RGB,\nthe typography scale, slide dimensions), pptx_constants.py (importable rather\nthan pasted at the top of each generation script), and accenture.css (linked\nfrom generated HTML rather than inlined). The JSON is the source; the other two\nfollow it. The body keeps the tables a human reads and drops the two verbatim\nblocks a machine should read instead, 196 lines down to 133.\n\nVerified they reach a real install: install-local.sh copies the skill directory\nwhole, so assets/ arrives alongside SKILL.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e334da7052ffd2ddc920c12f83c0f4840d03657","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/4e334da7052ffd2ddc920c12f83c0f4840d03657"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDk2MWU3NmRhMzI2MjliMzRkNWM5OWY1MTQ3MDk2MTkzMGZkZGVmZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4","sha":"fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4"}],"sha":"961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/961e76da32629b34d5c99f51470961930fddeffa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:42:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:42:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Stop the eval scaffold shipping three descriptions its own gate rejects\n\ntemplates/new-use-case/evals/triggers.json had \"Direct primary invocation\",\n\"should route to `SIBLING-AGENT` instead\" and \"should not activate any\nsupervisor\". validate_evals() rejects all three, so a contributor copying the\nscaffold started with a red build and no idea why. The placeholders now show\nthe rule instead of breaking it, and the gate scans templates/ as well, since a\nscaffold that cannot pass CI is worse than no scaffold.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d432aaabe92a26d2be2c444cb507fbab3024d1b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/d432aaabe92a26d2be2c444cb507fbab3024d1b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGZiMWFkZmYyZGE3ZGEzYzUzNzY0YzQzZDM5ZDgyODViMTUzYjYwYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278","sha":"a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278"}],"sha":"fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/fb1adff2da7da3c53764c43d39d8285b153b60b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:41:56Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:41:56Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Give every capability a trigger eval, and stop the fixtures answering for the agent\n\n59 of 132 capabilities had no eval at all, so a description edit that quietly\nbroke their routing had nothing to catch it, which is the specific thing\nCLAUDE.md says trigger evals are for. All 132 have one now: 811 cases across 132\nfiles, three positives and three negatives each for the new ones. Behaviour\nscenarios were written only for the three capabilities a person invokes by\nintent; the other 56 state in their own frontmatter that a supervisor is their\nonly caller, and scoring a worker on a prompt no user sends measures the\nsupervisor instead.\n\nAn adversarial review found the fixtures were doing the agent''s work. 24\ncomments across 16 files named the defect in the expectation''s own vocabulary:\n`// Panic in library code instead of returning an error` sitting above the\nexpectation \"flags the panic in MustLoad as panic in library code\". Those are\ngone. The standard was already in the batch: OrderController.java and\napplication.yml carry no such comments and their defects are findable only by\nanalysis. Three fixtures written in this pass failed the same test and were\nfixed too.\n\nThe 27 cross-capability negatives asserted a routing decision no file claimed,\nso a router that declined everything scored 27 of 27. Each is now a positive in\nthe capability whose description claims it, with 19 balancing negatives added\nthere. Developer negatives are two-sided, 53 of 53, verified.\n\n19 expectations asserted `tool_used: Skill`, a field nothing reads: not the\nvalidator, not the guide, not the templates. Each keeps the observable effect\nand names the skill, without the ungradeable half.\n\nA classifier reading only the case description scores 49.4 percent on the added\nset against a 50 percent base rate, so the description carries no signal about\nthe verdict. One negative contradicted its target''s own description and was\nreplaced.\n\nCLAUDE.md: the reference-path rule said `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` and never a\nrepo-relative path, which is right for the 55 agents that use it and would have\nled a contributor to break all 9 skills that correctly use a relative link, as\nthe Agent Skills standard specifies. Scoped per file type now. The model-pin\nrule is restated as it is actually gated, and the section claiming CI has no\neval gate is corrected, since it now has one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"028d1b72f51a62c198e3fff291d65db4f38d36d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/028d1b72f51a62c198e3fff291d65db4f38d36d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGEyY2RmYzM2ZDU1NzEyMzQ0ZGVlODNlNmI0MGYwOWQwYmYwMzkyNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e","sha":"dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e"}],"sha":"a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a2cdfc36d55712344dee83e6b40f09d0bf039278"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:31:14Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:31:14Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Repair four gates that could not fail, and rewrite the skills as skills\n\nAn adversarial review took the new gates apart and found four of them were\ntheatre. Each is fixed and each fix is proved by reintroducing the defect.\n\nscripts/test-clean-install.sh checked absolute reference paths with a regex\nanchored on /Users/, while the harness installs into mktemp -d, which is\n/var/folders on macOS and /tmp in CI. That assertion had never run, anywhere.\nIt now anchors on $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, which the script already had in scope.\nThe same script passed green on an empty install, because it checked properties\nof whatever it found and asserted nothing about what it should find. It now\ncompares installed counts against the tree, with floors, so a tree that is\nitself empty fails rather than agreeing with itself.\n\nvalidate_cross_plugin_references() accepted any line saying \"the `x` plugin''s\"\nwithout checking that x exists or that the file is in it, so naming `banana` as\nthe owner passed. It resolves the path inside the named plugin now.\n\nvalidate_workflow_dag() returned quietly when its own subject was missing, so\ndeleting the DAG silenced it.\n\nThe retired-name gate matched only backticked and quoted spellings, which left\neight live references to code-reviewer, including a dispatch instruction in\nper-phase-protocol.md telling an agent to run something this registry does not\nhave. Word boundaries now, with a lookbehind so the official\npr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer replacement is not flagged as the thing it\nreplaces.\n\nThe eval verdict gate listed six phrasings rather than describing the property,\nso \"a job for developer-csharp, obviously not this one\" passed. It rejects a\ndescription naming any capability the query does not itself mention, which\nleaves a description free to name its own subject.\n\nIn the workflow the two shell tests ran before the comment step without\ncontinue-on-error, so a failure aborted the job and the contributor saw a red\ncheck and no findings. Both are gated at the end of the job now.\n\nSkills: 41 of 46 opened as agent personas (\"You are a senior JPA expert\"), which\noverwrites the calling agent''s persona at load time and contradicts this repo''s\nown line that a skill is knowledge loaded into context, not a subagent. All 46\nread as instructions now, with five second-person survivors that are quoted\nspecimens of banned output. 21 body sections restating trigger conditions are\ngone, 11 descriptions widened first to keep what was only stated there. Six\nbodies over 400 lines became 21 reference files. That split introduced an\noff-by-one leaving an unclosed fence that swallowed a heading in angular-expert,\nand the same bug had silently dropped a checklist item in two more files. All\nthree are repaired and every file in the corpus now has even fence parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dafc2322d6fd2313e41e91ed2dcb2b4b5b952dad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/dafc2322d6fd2313e41e91ed2dcb2b4b5b952dad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGRjZjQ3NGZmOWM2MTUwOWYzNmM5NDY1OGVjOTkwNzk5YWMwYjdlOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc","sha":"c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc"}],"sha":"dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/dcf474ff9c61509f36c94658ec990799ac0b7e8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:04:24Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:04:24Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Gate the six substance rules the structural checks never covered\n\nAn audit against Anthropic''s agent-development, skill-development, skill-creator\nand claude-md-improver rubrics found that everything the repo gates is clean and\neverything it does not gate has drifted. 132 capabilities, zero structural\ndefects, and 153 substance ones.\n\nThese start as warnings because the backlog is real: 98 reference files over 100\nlines with no ## Contents, so Claude previews them head-first and acts on a\npartial read; 23 of 24 opus agents pinning the most expensive model with no\nrecorded reason, which the authoring guide has required all along; 21 SKILL.md\nbodies restating their trigger conditions in a section that only loads after\nrouting has already happened; 6 skill bodies above 400 lines with no\nreferences/, treating the 500-line ceiling as a target; 5 agent bodies over the\n10000-character limit, three of which crossed it in the previous commit when\noutput-format sections were added.\n\nThe opus rule is deliberately narrower than the repo''s own wording. Requiring a\ncomment on every pin would mean 66 of them, 43 for a sonnet worker default that\nis a class policy, better stated once per plugin than repeated per file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"480a86c136bc8850d2774f50d15f901683b38ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/480a86c136bc8850d2774f50d15f901683b38ba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGM2Yzc4MGE2YWQ1NDkyOWIzNTk1ZmQ0YWYxNDc2MzIyNDYwMjgzZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac","sha":"c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac"}],"sha":"c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c6c780a6ad54929b3595fd4af1476322460283fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:49:29Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:49:29Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Gate the workflow DAG against the tree\n\nThe template told contributors to edit workflow-dag-draft.json by hand, which\nis now the only way to update it, with nothing checking the result. It had\nalready drifted: two entries named capabilities removed months earlier and the\ntwo superseded supervisors were missing, and because those cancelled out, the\nagent count matched the tree exactly. A count check would have passed.\n\nvalidate_workflow_dag() compares the names, not the total.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"084f5f8e90b4e5816bd7665b2e23f1d485e4b365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/084f5f8e90b4e5816bd7665b2e23f1d485e4b365"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGM4MDQ2MWJjY2Q1YjMxYWJiOTgxZWVjNjU1NzA1Y2Y3ZDk4Yzk0YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3","sha":"0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3"}],"sha":"c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c80461bccd5b31abb981eec655705cf7d98c94ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:48:00Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:48:21Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Refresh the normative docs, fix the scaffolding, and clear bmad of dead names\n\nThe docs still taught the pre-migration model. CONTRIBUTING, GOVERNANCE and the\nreview checklist required model: haiku and tools: Read on skills, which the\nvalidator now rejects outright. evals-guide.md documented Markdown eval files\nthat exist nowhere. The 12000-token budget survived in three places after\nCLAUDE.md was corrected. The README skill roster was wrong: analysis-architecture\nlisted 2 skills and omitted graphify-code-graph entirely; all six tables were\nregenerated from the frontmatter.\n\nnew-capability.sh scaffolded both eval files in shapes the corpus does not use:\n\"skills\" where all 79 scenarios use \"agent\", and a should_trigger /\nshould_not_trigger object where all 73 trigger files use a flat list. Every\ncapability created with it started out of schema.\n\nshared-settings-example.json pointed its hooks at claude-catalog/hooks/, granted\nAgent(code-reviewer), and set hook timeouts of 5000 and 3000. Those are seconds,\nso it was asking for 83 and 50 minutes. It also relied on the permission pattern\nBash(rm -rf *), which does not match rm -fr or rm -r -f; the file now says so and\npoints at the hook that actually parses the command.\n\nbmad/ named capabilities that no longer exist. workflows.json listed both\ndeveloper-java and developer-java-spring in shared_agents, plus code-reviewer;\nworkflow-dag-draft.json carried the same two ghosts while missing the two\nsuperseded supervisors that do exist, so the DAG and the tree now agree at 86.\nmapping.md''s ten claude-catalog/ paths were rewritten. backfill-dag.py is\ndeleted: its only output was claude-marketplace/catalog.json, so it has crashed\non import since the migration.\n\nThe retired-capability gate looked for backticks only, which is how\nbmad/workflows.json kept two retired names through every previous pass. It now\nmatches the JSON spelling too and scans bmad/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e06a4f4f99a64fbf3ed1f41fb054524bcce96ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/7e06a4f4f99a64fbf3ed1f41fb054524bcce96ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDBmNTk5YmI1NDAzNWY5ZDg3ZTgwMzY3NzA3ZjM4ZjVmYWExMGI4YzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27","sha":"00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27"}],"sha":"0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0f599bb54035f9d87e80367707f38f5faa10b8c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:47:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:47:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Make the eval suites able to fail, and gate the two ways they stopped failing\n\nThe trigger suites graded themselves. 364 of 365 descriptions named the routing\nwinner (\"Primary invocation\", \"Should not activate this capability\"), so a\nnine-line keyword table with no semantics scored 99.7%. All 411 descriptions now\ndescribe the query and never the verdict; the same query used as a positive in\none file and a negative in another carries the same description. That table now\nscores 53.0% against a 52.8% base rate.\n\nThe developer negatives were all cross-language flips, which any keyword matcher\ncatches. 27 same-language negatives were added that belong to a different\ncapability instead, and pair coverage went from 2 of 36 to 36 of 36, each pair\nsharing one verbatim query labelled positive on one side and negative on the\nother. Measured independently here: 61 of 91, under the 69.2% base rate.\n\n57 expectations could not be marked pass or fail from the artefact. \"Keeps the\nflow readable\" became a statement about block length and receiver mutation;\n\"states that cargo fmt was run\" became the clippy conditions the code must\nsatisfy as written. 23 fixtures were added for the 24 scenarios whose\nexpectations demand file:line evidence, each containing the defect its\nexpectation asks the agent to cite. Scenarios that target the repository the\nagent runs in were left with no fixture, deliberately.\n\n19 expectations now check that an agent loads the skills it declares, which\nnothing tested before. Two negatives contradicted their own capability''s\ndescription and were replaced, including a Flyway question filed as a negative\nfor the skill whose description says it redirects Flyway to Liquibase.\n\nvalidate_evals() locks both schemas and rejects a description that states the\nverdict, so neither regression can come back quietly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4c019c1efa742dbbdfd42f74356c89f23e40fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/e4c019c1efa742dbbdfd42f74356c89f23e40fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDAwNjY4ZjI3YjUwMjRmM2NiNWQxMzQ1YjY3OTgyZTdlNmU2YzJkMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11","sha":"d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11"}],"sha":"00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/00668f27b5024f3cb5d1345b67982e7e6e6c2d27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:47:30Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:47:30Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Rewrite the wiki against the current tree and clear the em dash from the prose\n\nThe wiki had not been touched since 2026-04-30 and still described the\npre-migration layout: claude-catalog/ as the source directory,\nclaude-marketplace/ as the published one, a hand-maintained catalog.json, a\nstable/ directory of agent files, setup-capabilities.sh as the installer. None\nof that exists. All 14 pages were rewritten from the tree, with every count\nrecounted rather than carried over, and both installation paths documented,\nsince the plugin marketplace is not reachable under an enterprise policy that\nallowlists its sources. 100 internal links resolve, 0 broken.\n\nThe em dash reads as machine-written, so it is not punctuation we ship. 2132 of\nthem are gone from the plugin prose (replatforming 1659 to 9, the other five\n1659 to 0). The 9 that remain sit inside inline code spans that agents emit\nverbatim; rewriting those would change strings the agents write. Two more of\nthat kind were converted anyway, in wiki-writer and the UniCredit component\ncatalogue, because those literals end up in produced artefacts.\n\nReplacement was not mechanical. Under a prohibition an em dash never becomes a\ncolon: \"never use Thread.sleep to wait for async: use CompletableFuture\" reads\nas forbidding CompletableFuture, so those became separate sentences. Table\ncells that meant nothing became n/a, ASCII blocks kept their alignment\nincluding continuation lines, and headings that changed took their inbound\nanchors and cross-references with them.\n\n18 agents that specified no output shape anywhere got one checkable\n## Output format or ## Quality section: the files they own, the toolchain whose\nresult they must report, the self-check that can actually fail. The 49\nreplatforming agents that already specify their output under another heading\nwere left alone rather than given a duplicate.\n\nNo frontmatter field drifted on any of the 86 agents, and the description\nbudget went down, not up: 11949 to 11927.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"543c3915d768b720da1c8ccda9ccdab98233da7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/543c3915d768b720da1c8ccda9ccdab98233da7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGQ1NDQ1ZTNmMTk3Y2IwNWY3NjExYmNiZmRiMWMyYzE3ODFiYWNiMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1","sha":"d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1"}],"sha":"d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d5445e3f197cb05f7611bcbfdb1c2c1781bacb11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:24:08Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:24:08Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Add a clean-machine install check and a gate for cross-plugin references\n\nThe plan''s W7 called for an end-to-end test from a machine that has never seen\nthis registry. scripts/test-clean-install.sh installs all six plugins into a\nthrowaway CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and asserts the result is usable rather than merely\npresent: frontmatter parses, no ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} survives (it does not\nexpand outside a real plugin), every absolute and relative reference path\nresolves, an agent whose body invokes skills carries the Skill tool, and\n--uninstall removes exactly what it created. Passing run: 86 agents, 46 skills,\n158 reference files, 312 files installed and 0 left behind.\n\nWriting it surfaced a case no review had: four replatforming supervisors cite a\nreference owned by the deliberation plugin. Plugins install independently, so a\nrelative path can never reach another plugin''s tree. Here the lines say \"the\n`deliberation` plugin''s ...\", which is what makes them findable, so the new\ngate accepts a cross-plugin reference only when the line names its owner and\nrejects the bare path it could otherwise decay into.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"210230190390b8d888f7ea626620fbdd6827544a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/210230190390b8d888f7ea626620fbdd6827544a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGQwZGM4MjMzNWY3MDRhMDgyOWY4MjY1ZTIxMmE3NTU1OTFiMjM2ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58","sha":"8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58"}],"sha":"d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d0dc82335f704a0829f8265e212a755591b236d1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:05:39Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T22:05:39Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Retire stale names in the docs, unify the eval schemas, pin the root MCP config\n\nThe retired-capability gate globbed only plugins/, so the pages a teammate\nreads first were the ones still advertising capabilities that no longer exist:\nthe wiki catalog listed `developer-java-spring` and `code-reviewer` as\navailable, and docs/quick-start.md and the pitch repeated the latter. 19 names\nupdated; `code-reviewer` now points at `pr-review-toolkit:code-reviewer`, which\nis where that capability actually lives. The gate now covers wiki/, docs/,\nREADME.md and CLAUDE.md, exempting the changelog and archive, where naming a\nremoved capability is the point.\n\nevals.json carried two incompatible shapes: 16 scenarios as\n{id, prompt, expectations, timeout} and 63 as {agent, query, files,\nexpected_behavior}. All 79 now use the latter. Separately, the negative case\n\"What are the security risks in this codebase?\" was marked as not triggering\nsoftware-architect, whose own description lists security among the\nnon-functional requirements it assesses; it is now a dependency-CVE query,\nwhich genuinely belongs to technical-analyst.\n\nThe root .mcp.json ran `@playwright/mcp@latest` and `uvx --from git+...` with\nno ref, executing whatever upstream publishes at launch, while the two\nplugin-level configs for the same servers were already pinned. Root pinned to\nmatch, with a gate so the three cannot drift apart again.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4817d4d6c7988d7fe9bd920fd61569ea29a78d51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/4817d4d6c7988d7fe9bd920fd61569ea29a78d51"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDg2NzBhNjNlNTUyMThjNjJjYmIyYmQ2MTVhYjUwYmMzNTlhODNkNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7","sha":"d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7"}],"sha":"8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/8670a63e55218c62cbb2bd615ab50bc359a83d58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:59:31Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:59:31Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Resolve 52 capability paths left pointing at the old catalog categories\n\nThe migration flattened skills and agents out of category directories, but 52\nin-body references still addressed them as backend/, frontend/, react/, api/,\ntesting/ and friends. None of those directories exist any more, so an agent\ntold to invoke api/rest-api-standards, or a reference block routing to\nfrontend/angular/angular-expert, named something the runtime cannot resolve.\napi-designer had one of these as Quality self-check item 1.\n\nSome were nested two levels deep, so the substitution needed a second pass to\nreach a fixpoint; the sweep now reports zero.\n\nASCII decision blocks were realigned after the prefixes came off, including\nthe continuation lines under the em dash entries, which had stayed indented\nto the width of the old longer names.\n\nAlso, under negative headings (\"What you never do\"), four bullets had an em\ndash replaced by a colon, which lets the recommended alternative parse as part\nof the prohibition: \"never use Thread.sleep to wait for async operations: use\nCompletableFuture\" can be read as forbidding CompletableFuture. Those now put\nthe alternative in its own sentence. And doc-expert''s description had lost the\nbackend-documentation half of a \"backend/frontend-documentation\" shorthand;\nboth skills are named explicitly now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"af80fefc1f52c9cb137a293977fc9b4c94523aeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/af80fefc1f52c9cb137a293977fc9b4c94523aeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGQ5YTkwM2Y0YWU2OGVjMjRkZDY3OWFlM2I4NzFjYjZiZGMxNTFjZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8","sha":"82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8"}],"sha":"d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d9a903f4ae68ec24dd679ae3b871cb6bdc151ce7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:54:32Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:54:32Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"Fix frontmatter regression, inverted safety hook and two non-gating CI gates\n\nThe trigger-restoration pass in 15f4749 left an unescaped quote in the\ndescription of technical-analyst and wiki-writer, so their frontmatter no\nlonger parsed as YAML. Claude Code loads such an agent with its name taken\nfrom the filename and silently drops every other field, which cost both\nagents their description, model, colour and their whole tools list including\nthe Skill entry the same commit had just added. Nothing caught it: the\nvalidator''s split_frontmatter returns raw text and field() reads it line by\nline, so broken quoting still yields a plausible value.\n\n- Repair both descriptions; all five fields parse again on both agents, and\n  all six plugins pass `claude plugin validate`.\n- Add validate_frontmatter_yaml(), which runs a real yaml.safe_load over\n  every plugin markdown file. Verified against a reintroduced break.\n- Widen the Skill-tool gate: it keyed on a literal \"## Skills\" heading and so\n  missed developer-frontend, whose body says \"Invoke the framework skill set\"\n  while its tools list had no Skill entry. Both the gate and the file fixed.\n- Make `claude plugin validate` able to fail. It was wrapped in `|| echo` with\n  continue-on-error, and the failure step keyed only on the Python validator,\n  so a plugin Claude Code itself rejects still went green. A CLI that cannot\n  run is still reported rather than enforced.\n- Rewrite the rm check in the safety hook. Substring-matching \"rm -rf /\" had\n  an inverted profile, measured: `rm -fr /`, `rm -r -f /` and\n  `rm --no-preserve-root -rf /` all passed, while `rm -rf /tmp/scratch` was\n  blocked. It now parses flags and targets per command segment. New 24-case\n  regression matrix in hooks/tests, wired into CI.\n- CLAUDE.md documented a 12000-token description gate; the gate is 13000.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8c7d00701246d571d0c93004e9c1accf272039aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/8c7d00701246d571d0c93004e9c1accf272039aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDgyZDU4MmNiYThhODA2MjFiZDk5MWE1NDhjMzhiOTYxZGVhNjk1Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d","sha":"a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d"}],"sha":"82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/82d582cba8a80621bd991a548c38b961dea695f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:32:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:32:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"feat(scripts): add install-local.sh for policy-blocked environments\n\nEnterprise strictKnownMarketplaces can block this marketplace as a plugin\nsource, as it does on the Accenture deployment: the allowlist names nine\nGitHub repositories and admits nothing else, local paths included.\n\ninstall-local.sh installs the same tree without the plugin system. Agents go\nto ~/.claude/agents/, skills to ~/.claude/skills/ where the Skill tool finds\nthem, and bundled reference material to ~/.claude/registry-references/<plugin>/.\nEvery ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} is rewritten to that absolute path, because the\nvariable only expands inside an installed plugin and would otherwise sit in\nthe agent body as a literal string that silently opens nothing.\n\nDefaults to dev-standards, analysis-architecture and docs-branding rather than\neverything, since the combined subagent descriptions of all six plugins come to\nroughly 12000 tokens against a 15000 ceiling. Tracks what it wrote in a manifest\nso --uninstall is exact, and is idempotent for re-running after a git pull.\n\nCannot wire MCP servers; it prints the two plugins that ship one and says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb0c71d713cebcb6d56855cdb41352e52b0d30cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/eb0c71d713cebcb6d56855cdb41352e52b0d30cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGEwMDVlZTVkODJjOGM3ZDU1ZWJkYjc1MzZmZWFlNzkwYmU3NjM2OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43","sha":"15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43"}],"sha":"a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/a005ee5d82c8c7d55ebdb7536feae790be76368d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:21:07Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:21:07Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"fix(registry): repair defects the swarm and its critics found after the migration\n\nFive findings, four of them regressions introduced by the migration itself.\n\n1. No agent could invoke the Skill tool. All 86 agents carry an explicit `tools:`\n   allowlist and none included `Skill`, so the \"## Skills\" sections rewritten during\n   the migration to say \"load with the Skill tool\" were inert: the agent silently\n   substituted its own priors for the team standard, with no error anywhere. Added\n   `Skill` to the 19 agents that reference skills, and a CI gate that fails when an\n   agent has a \"## Skills\" section without the tool.\n\n2. 84 dangling read instructions. Agent bodies and reference files carried links of\n   the form [`x.md`](../../docs/x.md), a shape that predates the plugin layout and\n   contains no ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}, so neither the migration rewrite nor the\n   validator saw them. Every pipeline supervisor opened with a reference table whose\n   rows were all dead. Repaired 74 in-plugin and 10 cross-plugin, and added a CI gate\n   that resolves every relative markdown link inside plugins/.\n\n3. Description content loss. The regex that stripped the trailing trigger enumeration\n   was greedy between \"Typical triggers include\" and \"See When to invoke\", swallowing\n   the sentences in between. registry-auditor lost its output description and its\n   read-only boundary; six deliberation personas lost their schema reference and their\n   \"not for standalone use\" boundary. Two agents (technical-analyst, wiki-writer) ended\n   with a literal `\", and \"` fragment where phrases should have been, and\n   developer-ruby lost its phrasings entirely. Restored from the pre-migration\n   descriptions.\n\n4. The description budget was measured with a word-count heuristic that underestimates\n   these strings by 17%, because they are dense with backticks, escaped quotes and\n   technical terms. Real counts (tiktoken cl100k_base): the pre-migration registry was\n   at 17018 tokens, already 2018 OVER the documented 15000 ceiling rather than at 95%\n   of it as previously reported; the current registry is at 12011. The validator now\n   uses a real tokenizer when available and a calibrated character ratio otherwise.\n\n5. Trigger evals leaked their answer. Every should_not_trigger query ended with a\n   parenthetical naming the skill that should win, and no should_trigger query had one,\n   so a classifier testing for \"(\" scored 232/232 without understanding anything. All\n   67 triggers.json files converted to the array schema the repo''s own template already\n   defines, moving the rationale into the description field. The trivial classifier\n   now scores at the base rate.\n\nAlso: references to retired capabilities (`code-reviewer`, `test-data-design-standards`,\n`database-migration-patterns`, `developer-java-spring`) now fail CI through a RETIRED\ntable, rather than becoming dangling dispatch instructions at runtime; 589 em dashes\nreplaced across 60 skill files, with the 4 remaining \"not applicable\" table cells\nrewritten as n/a; 26 old-style catalog paths (`frontend/angular/angular-expert`)\nnormalised to bare skill names.\n\nAdds 46 skill trigger suites and 21 agent eval suites (evals.json + triggers.json).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51590a587a0e40541b6016f0b08528390f5097d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/51590a587a0e40541b6016f0b08528390f5097d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDE1ZjQ3NDk0ODBiZTExYWM5OTQwNDg1MjQyMWUxNzA1NTUwOTBhNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005","sha":"f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005"}],"sha":"15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/15f4749480be11ac99404852421e170555090a43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:00:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T21:00:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"ci: split validation into the two contexts the main ruleset requires\n\nThe ''Protect main branch'' ruleset requires the status-check contexts\n''Validate marketplace'' and ''Validate catalog''. The migration replaced both\njobs with a single ''Validate registry'', so every future pull request would\nhave sat pending on two contexts that never report.\n\nRather than change the shared ruleset, split the validator along a boundary\nit already had: validate_registry.py gains --only manifests (marketplace.json\nand every plugin.json) and --only capabilities (agents, skills, references\nand the description budget). The two workflow jobs map onto those halves and\ncarry the required names.\n\nAdded a comment in the workflow marking the job names as load-bearing, since\nrenaming one silently blocks every pull request.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"563bed3ea5b5fdb501d4012b4e85e2e9411478cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/563bed3ea5b5fdb501d4012b4e85e2e9411478cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGY1OGQ1MmRlYmMwZTQwNzM3M2VmYTNmNWI3NTkzZDRjODdmMTAwMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86","sha":"756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86"}],"sha":"f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/f58d52debc0e407373efa3f5b7593d4c87f10005"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:55:15Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T20:55:15Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"feat(registry)!: migrate to official Claude Code plugin marketplace\n\nCollapse claude-catalog/ and claude-marketplace/ into plugins/, with\n.claude-plugin/marketplace.json at the root and a plugin.json per plugin.\nSix plugins: replatforming, dev-standards, analysis-architecture,\ndeliberation, docs-branding, caveman.\n\nFixes three blocking defects found by an audit against the current Anthropic\nguidance (Agent Skills best practices, Claude Code subagents, plugin\nmarketplaces):\n\n- 123 references to claude-catalog/docs/** across 62 files did not resolve at\n  runtime, because setup-capabilities.sh installed only agent files. Rewritten\n  to ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/references/**; all 114 now resolve.\n- Combined subagent descriptions sat at ~14200 tokens against a 15000-token\n  platform ceiling. Now ~10200 with every plugin enabled, and ~2500 for a\n  typical development session, because plugins are enabled per project.\n- All 42 skills were haiku subagents invoked through the Agent tool, so\n  ~/.claude/skills/ was empty and the Skill tool never saw them. Converted to\n  Agent Skills at plugins/<plugin>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md.\n\nAlso:\n\n- Six oversized skills split into references/ with tables of contents; every\n  SKILL.md body is now under the 500-line guidance.\n- model: inherit for user-facing agents, opus + effort: high for supervisors,\n  challengers, auditors and deliberation personas, sonnet retained for fan-out\n  workers. Supervisors gain experimental.cacheTtl: 1h.\n- Deliberation personas moved to opus, matching what the engine already\n  documented but did not configure.\n- Removed model_justification, a non-standard field whose multi-line value\n  corrupted the model key above it in orchestrator.md.\n- Merged python-to-{java,angular,react}-migration-expert from the retired\n  skill-registry; its other 20 skills are covered by more mature capabilities\n  here.\n- Carried graphify-code-graph (#44) forward as an Agent Skill in\n  analysis-architecture.\n- Removed code-reviewer, superseded by pr-review-toolkit.\n- Retired per-capability beta/stable tiers in favour of plugin semver.\n- validate_registry.py replaces validate_catalog.py and\n  validate_marketplace.py, gating the description budget, SKILL.md length,\n  frontmatter correctness, reference-link resolution and CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\n  path resolution.\n- Pinned @playwright/mcp and uml-mcp; wired both via plugin.json mcpServers.\n\nThis commit also lands the work that sat unmerged on\nfeature/test-data-seeder-agent: the Step G workflow retrospective,\ncross-phase iteration, and a batch of capability releases. PR #43 had\nsquashed an earlier form of that branch, so the two lines had diverged with\nonly two files differing in content; both were reconciled before this commit.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: setup-capabilities.sh and the SessionStart git-diff sync hook\nare retired. Install with /plugin marketplace add and /plugin install.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35f3e971278da0c47f032dfac79a92578a3e5305","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/35f3e971278da0c47f032dfac79a92578a3e5305"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDc1NmY4ODM2NDE1NWJlOGRjOTM3MzBmMGY2NTNkYWM0YTg2MWJiODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc","sha":"2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc"}],"sha":"756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/756f88364155be8dc93730f0f653dac4a861bb86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T19:23:20Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T19:23:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skill): add graphify-code-graph — code knowledge-graph usage skill (#44)\n\n* feat(skill): add graphify-code-graph — code knowledge-graph usage skill\n\nNew analysis skill documenting the graphify CLI for code use cases:\nlocal, deterministic tree-sitter AST extraction into a GraphRAG-ready\ngraph.json; query/path/explain/affected/god-nodes playbook; compliance-safe\nlocal-first workflow (code = no LLM/no upload; non-code gated on model\nbackend); limitations (no SQL/PL-SQL grammar) and integration with\ntech-analyst + Neo4j export.\n\nMirrored to claude-marketplace/skills/analysis/ and registered in\ncatalog.json (graphify-code-graph@1.0.0). CHANGELOG updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(skill): conform graphify-code-graph to skill policy (haiku, Read-only)\n\nCatalog validator requires skills to be knowledge providers: model: haiku\nand tools: Read. Reframe as a knowledge/playbook provider (caller executes\ngraphify via Bash) and align catalog.json (tools: [Read], model: haiku).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fae509f9685b792bd8dbd12f7a356a45edcd291a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/fae509f9685b792bd8dbd12f7a356a45edcd291a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc","verification":{"payload":"tree fae509f9685b792bd8dbd12f7a356a45edcd291a\nparent 67ce411ba406edc143d790ab17dbb3042fa946ca\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1784834600 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784834600 +0200\n\nfeat(skill): add graphify-code-graph — code knowledge-graph usage skill (#44)\n\n* feat(skill): add graphify-code-graph — code knowledge-graph usage skill\n\nNew analysis skill documenting the graphify CLI for code use cases:\nlocal, deterministic tree-sitter AST extraction into a GraphRAG-ready\ngraph.json; query/path/explain/affected/god-nodes playbook; compliance-safe\nlocal-first workflow (code = no LLM/no upload; non-code gated on model\nbackend); limitations (no SQL/PL-SQL grammar) and integration with\ntech-analyst + Neo4j export.\n\nMirrored to claude-marketplace/skills/analysis/ and registered in\ncatalog.json (graphify-code-graph@1.0.0). CHANGELOG updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(skill): conform graphify-code-graph to skill policy (haiku, Read-only)\n\nCatalog validator requires skills to be knowledge providers: model: haiku\nand tools: Read. Reframe as a knowledge/playbook provider (caller executes\ngraphify via Bash) and align catalog.json (tools: [Read], model: haiku).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYmooCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZGkQAHYhiZ+cycFrjKssd5M2TOOT\npUv127DxbWq5h7r+R1wGXLTq7IS7liPtoeiCAvfKQnuSP0AxndBTqd6GXQY/A5LS\nWa0HLWknGqOu79mC47VLRSP