tps://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/67ce411ba406edc143d790ab17dbb3042fa946ca"}],"sha":"2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/2a7721a86a14b89c80d20da97b2fbb24cf38decc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69315983?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/MarcoMoscariello","id":69315983,"login":"MarcoMoscariello","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzE1OTgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarcoMoscariello","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/67ce411ba406edc143d790ab17dbb3042fa946ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T07:10:42Z","email":"69315983+MarcoMoscariello@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marco Moscariello"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T07:10:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"New step to create mock data after refactoring  (#43)\n\n* feat(refactoring-tobe): test-data-seeder agent + Phase 4 Step 5.5 post-testing seeding\n\nAdd a new sub-agent that seeds a coherent cross-module test dataset into a\nfreshly-built TO-BE application so the Step 6 UI smoke gate can judge the\napp visually. An empty UI is indistinguishable from a broken UI, so without\nthis step the human-visual gate is meaningless.\n\nNew agent (beta):\n- test-data-seeder — auto-detects the project''s migration tool (Liquibase,\n  Flyway, Django fixtures, Rails seeds, EF Core HasData, Knex, TypeORM,\n  Prisma, sqlx, Diesel, goose, Alembic, raw SQL), designs a 5-pivot\n  dataset with lifecycle coverage and login-user spread, writes seeds\n  gated to a non-production profile, optionally extends an in-memory\n  dev/test auth store, restarts the backend and verifies via API smoke\n  calls. Strictly generic across stacks. Body 8 370 chars (under 10k cap);\n  detailed 7-step Method extracted to docs/refactoring-tobe/.\n\nNew skills:\n- test-data-design-standards — pivot taxonomy, lifecycle coverage, FK\n  consistency, login spread, column-length safety checklist\n- database-migration-patterns — per-stack idempotent insert templates,\n  non-prod gating, FK lookup patterns\n\nWorkflow integration (Phase 4 Step 5.5):\n- new doc phase-4-step-5-5-test-data-seeding.md (hard gate, pre/post-step\n  messages, manifest schema)\n- phase-4-replatforming.md: Step 5.5 section, gate-table row, sub-agents\n- phase-4-step-6-ui-smoke-gate.md: explicit Step 5.5 precondition\n- constraints.md: Step 5.5 non-skippable invariant\n- refactoring-supervisor.md: reference-docs table row\n\nMarketplace: +1 agent (beta), +2 skills; catalog count 127 → 130.\nValidators: catalog WARNINGS only (pre-existing legacy agents; new agent\nNOT listed); marketplace ✅ all checks passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(skills): merge test-data-design-standards + database-migration-patterns into test-data-seeding-standards\n\nThe two skills were always co-invoked by test-data-seeder with no path\nwhere one was needed without the other. Split context increases\nintegration risk; a single skill removes the overhead and eliminates\nthe database-migration-patterns name mismatch (which covered only seed\ninjection, not schema DDL, despite the generic name).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: indexing-supervisor@2.0.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''indexing-supervisor'' version 2.0.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: module-documenter@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''module-documenter'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: synthesizer@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''synthesizer'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: functional-analysis-supervisor@3.0.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''functional-analysis-supervisor'' version 3.0.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: actor-feature-mapper@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''actor-feature-mapper'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: user-flow-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''user-flow-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: technical-analysis-supervisor@2.1.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''technical-analysis-supervisor'' version 2.1.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: code-quality-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''code-quality-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: dependency-security-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''dependency-security-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: integration-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''integration-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: resilience-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''resilience-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: state-runtime-analyst@2.0.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''state-runtime-analyst'' version 2.0.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: baseline-testing-supervisor@0.3.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''baseline-testing-supervisor'' version 0.3.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: deliberative-decision-engine@0.1.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''deliberative-decision-engine'' version 0.1.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: refactoring-tobe-supervisor@0.3.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''refactoring-tobe-supervisor'' version 0.3.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: tobe-testing-supervisor@0.1.2 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''tobe-testing-supervisor'' version 0.1.2 to beta tier.\n\n* release: decomposition-architect@0.2.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''decomposition-architect'' version 0.2.1 to beta tier.\n\n* release: logic-translator@0.2.1 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''logic-translator'' version 0.2.1 to beta tier.\n\n* feat(bmad): BMAD methodology migration — progressive disclosure + workflow DAG + evals\n\n## Infrastructure\n- bmad/workflows.json — machine-readable workflow registry (use-case modules)\n- bmad/design/mapping.md — canonical BMAD→Anthropic pattern decisions\n- bmad/design/workflow-dag-draft.json — full dependency graph (87 pipeline agents)\n- bmad/scripts/backfill-dag.py — syncs DAG into catalog.json bmad blocks\n- catalog.json: 85 pipeline agents now carry bmad.{preceded_by, followed_by, workflow, phase, wave}\n- claude-catalog/templates/new-use-case/ — 8-step scaffold for adding a new workflow use case\n\n## Progressive disclosure (all supervisors ≤ 10k chars)\n- legacy-body-baseline.json: cleared — zero exceptions remain\n- 18 agents body-reduced; operational content moved to supervisor-protocol.md reference docs\n- 7 new supervisor-protocol.md files (one per phase + deliberation + 2 legacy)\n\n## Document-as-cache\n- All 7 supervisor-protocol.md files now include ## Pipeline state with full YAML schema,\n  bootstrap protocol, and update-after-wave instructions\n\n## Eval suites\n- claude-catalog/evals/: trigger.json + evals.json for all 6 supervisors,\n  orchestrator, code-reviewer, software-architect\n\n## Quality pass (Phase D)\n- 32 agent files improved: concrete When-to-invoke scenarios, realistic description\n  trigger phrases, named Do-NOT-use alternatives\n- 14 worker agents: explicit \"not for standalone use\" Do-NOT-use lines\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(bmad): address 12 review findings — DAG accuracy, Phase 5 refs, progressive disclosure\n\nMUST FIX (5):\n- refactoring-supervisor.md: strip 6 inline sections violating progressive\n  disclosure rule; extract to new supervisor-protocol.md; body now Role +\n  When to invoke + Reference docs only\n- refactoring-supervisor/evals.json eval-002: fix wrong state file path\n  (.refactoring-kb/ → docs/refactoring/workflow-manifest.json)\n- baseline-testing-supervisor.md: replace 3 stale Phase 5 references with\n  Phase 4 Step 6; update Do-NOT-use to remove tobe-testing-supervisor\n- baseline-testing-supervisor/evals.json: fix 2 stale Phase 5 references\n- workflow-dag-draft.json: baseline-runner.preceded_by adds service-collection-builder;\n  functional-traceability-auditor.preceded_by adds W2 workers (W3b runs even\n  when challenger is skipped); re-run backfill-dag.py to sync catalog.json\n\nSHOULD FIX (7):\n- indexing/supervisor-protocol.md: add ## Inputs + ## Manifest update sections;\n  replace duplicated Sub-agents table with compact pointer to sub-agents-catalog.md\n- new-use-case template: add evals/evals.json stub; README Step 7 clarifies\n  backfill-dag.py vs manual approach; checklist adds evals.json item\n- functional-analysis-supervisor/evals.json: add eval-002 (exports-only resume)\n  and eval-003 (missing .indexing-kb/ guard)\n- quick-start.md: update refactoring-supervisor row to Phases 0–4; mark\n  refactoring-tobe-supervisor and tobe-testing-supervisor as LEGACY (v2 only)\n- refactoring-tobe + tobe-testing supervisor-protocol.md: add prominent LEGACY\n  callout block at the top of both files with redirect to refactoring-supervisor\n- functional-analysis-supervisor/triggers.json: add negative \"Run Phase 1\"\n  entry disambiguating direct vs workflow-supervisor routing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update README, regenerate PDF/PPTX, complete supervisor-protocol\n\n- README.md: add BMAD methodology section, fix structure block (bmad/,\n  evals/, templates/), agent count 83→87, mark legacy supervisors,\n  fix Phase 5 refs in supervisor descriptions\n- refactoring-workflow/supervisor-protocol.md: add ## Pipeline state\n  (workflow-manifest.json bootstrap protocol + note on phase-level\n  pipeline-state.yaml); completes the 7/7 supervisor-protocol coverage\n- guida-operativa.pdf: regenerated v3.0 — 4 parts (usage, contributing,\n  BMAD methodology, appendices); 87 agents/42 skills; Step 5.5 and\n  LEGACY supervisors documented\n- pitch-claude-registry.pptx: regenerated — 12 slides including BMAD\n  architecture slide and platform scalability slide\n- CHANGELOG.md: entries for this round of fixes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: marco.moscariello <marco.moscariello@accenture.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: luke <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d7860cae6e7b99a0fca973966662d99f41e8511","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/9d7860cae6e7b99a0fca973966662d99f41e8511"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/67ce411ba406edc143d790ab17dbb3042fa946ca","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d7860cae6e7b99a0fca973966662d99f41e8511\nparent 9d33068aa8c600df01d42bfd2312d1b5e157bddb\nauthor Marco Moscariello <69315983+MarcoMoscariello@users.noreply.github.com> 1780211442 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780211442 +0200\n\nNew step to create mock data after refactoring  (#43)\n\n* feat(refactoring-tobe): test-data-seeder agent + Phase 4 Step 5.5 post-testing seeding\n\nAdd a new sub-agent that seeds a coherent cross-module test dataset into a\nfreshly-built TO-BE application so the Step 6 UI smoke gate can judge the\napp visually. An empty UI is indistinguishable from a broken UI, so without\nthis step the human-visual gate is meaningless.\n\nNew agent (beta):\n- test-data-seeder — auto