ng_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9e73bec18c218db95b220dd2e3f30a835c6afe79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-19T08:19:19Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-19T08:19:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(refactoring): close shell+nav+405+CORS gaps surfaced by InfoSync retro (#40)\n\nAnchored to the InfoSync 2026-05 retrospective\n(INFOSYNC-REFACTORING-AGENT-GAP-REPORT.md, new top-level file): the\npipeline declared green (177/177 + 200/200 + 204/204) while the FE was\nunusable. Patches close every gap-class at the layer that should have\ncaught it.\n\nFrontend scaffolder (agents + reference docs):\n- app-shell.md: mandate full overwrite of app.component.html; provide\n  the canonical `<app-layout><router-outlet/></app-layout>` template;\n  document the placeholder-string self-check.\n- code-skeletons.md: add `core/layout` section with sidenav-per-BC\n  pattern, conditional shell, permission-gated entries, trackBy.\n- frontend-scaffolder.md: add Step 10 self-check (6 greps the agent\n  MUST run before reporting status: ok — no CLI placeholders survive,\n  app-layout referenced, layout exists with routerLinks, interceptors\n  file(s) emitted, no per-service Authorization header).\n\nBackend scaffolder (agents + reference docs):\n- error-and-security.md: add explicit overrides for\n  handleHttpRequestMethodNotSupported (405),\n  handleHttpMediaTypeNotSupported (415),\n  handleHttpMediaTypeNotAcceptable (406). Document that without these\n  overrides the framework exceptions fall through to the generic\n  Exception handler and the FE sees HTTP 500. CORS:\n  setAllowedOriginPatterns with localhost+127.0.0.1 default.\n- backend-scaffolder.md: forbid @CrossOrigin on controllers; the\n  CorsConfigurationSource bean is the single source of truth.\n\nChallengers (always-on adversarial reviewers):\n- phase4-challenger.md: add Check 10 (navigation reachability) — no\n  CLI placeholder, layout shell exists, every protected route in\n  app.routes.ts is reachable via routerLink/router.navigate in the UI\n  tree; orphan route generates one FINDING-NAV-ORPHAN-ROUTE-* per\n  route. Update description and \"Method — N checks\" wording.\n- tobe-testing-challenger.md: add Check 9 (shell coverage) — smoke\n  spec MUST exist, cover ≥ 80% of protected routes, assert placeholder\n  strings are gone, run against a real backend.\n\nFrontend test writer:\n- frontend-test-writer.md: declare `smoke.spec.ts` as a MANDATORY spec\n  independent of user flows. It iterates app.routes.ts, asserts no CLI\n  placeholder, asserts feature h1/h2 is visible, asserts a nav link\n  exists for each route, asserts no console/network errors.\n\nRefactoring supervisor (orchestrator):\n- refactoring-supervisor.md: add the `Phase 4 Step 6 — UI smoke gate`\n  section. Before PO sign-off the supervisor MUST bring backend +\n  frontend up, run smoke.spec.ts, capture screenshots of /home + 3\n  bounded-context samples, and ask the user a *visual* confirmation\n  question — sign-off cannot proceed until the user confirms layout is\n  coherent. Adds the matching decision-rule row to the table.\n\nTop-level:\n- INFOSYNC-REFACTORING-AGENT-GAP-REPORT.md: new file documenting the\n  8 gap classes (G1-G8), root-cause analysis of why each automated\n  check missed them, the exact file→change mapping, and the strategic\n  recommendation to add a `ui-smoke-validator` agent in a future wave.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4478c110cb1b54ce9b6065583e8531feea3f57e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/f4478c110cb1b54ce9b6065583e8531feea3f57e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/9e73bec18c218db95b220dd2e3f30a835c6afe79","verification":{"payload":"tree f4478c110cb1b54ce9b6065583e8531feea3f57e\nparent cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1779178759 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779178759 +0200\n\ndocs(refactoring): close shell+nav+405+CORS gaps surfaced by InfoSync retro (#40)\n\nAnchored to the InfoSync 2026-05 retrospective\n(INFOSYNC-REFACTORING-AGENT-GAP-REPORT.md, new top-level file): the\npipeline declared green (177/177 + 200/200 + 204/204) while the FE was\nunusable. Patches close every gap-class at the layer that should have\ncaught it.\n\nFrontend scaffolder (agents + reference docs):\n- app-shell.md: mandate full overwrite of app.component.html; provide\n  the canonical `<app-layout><router-outlet/></app-layout>` template;\n  document the placeholder-string self-check.\n- code-skeletons.md: add `core/layout` section with sidenav-per-BC\n  pattern, conditional shell, permission-gated entries, trackBy.\n- frontend-scaffolder.md: add Step 10 self-check (6 greps the agent\n  MUST run before reporting status: ok — no CLI placeholders survive,\n  app-layout referenced, layout exists with routerLinks, interceptors\n  file(s) emitted, no per-service Authorization header).\n\nBackend scaffolder (agents + reference docs):\n- error-and-security.md: add explicit overrides for\n  handleHttpRequestMethodNotSupported (405),\n  handleHttpMediaTypeNotSupported (415),\n  handleHttpMediaTypeNotAcceptable (406). Document that without these\n  overrides the framework exceptions fall through to the generic\n  Exception handler and the FE sees HTTP 500. CORS:\n  setAllowedOriginPatterns with localhost+127.0.0.1 default.\n- backend-scaffolder.md: forbid @CrossOrigin on controllers; the\n  CorsConfigurationSource bean is the single source of truth.\n\nChallengers (always-on adversarial reviewers):\n- phase4-challenger.md: add Check 10 (navigation reachability) — no\n  CLI placeholder, layout shell exists, every protected route in\n  app.routes.ts is reachable via routerLink/router.navigate in the UI\n  tree; orphan route generates one FINDING-NAV-ORPHAN-ROUTE-* per\n  route. Update description and \"Method — N checks\" wording.\n- tobe-testing-challenger.md: add Check 9 (shell coverage) — smoke\n  spec MUST exist, cover ≥ 80% of protected routes, assert placeholder\n  strings are gone, run against a real backend.\n\nFrontend test writer:\n- frontend-test-writer.md: declare `smoke.spec.ts` as a MANDATORY spec\n  independent of user flows. It iterates app.routes.ts, asserts no CLI\n  placeholder, asserts feature h1/h2 is visible, asserts a nav link\n  exists for each route, asserts no console/network errors.\n\nRefactoring supervisor (orchestrator):\n- refactoring-supervisor.md: add the `Phase 4 Step 6 — UI smoke gate`\n  section. Before PO sign-off the supervisor MUST bring backend +\n  frontend up, run smoke.spec.ts, capture screenshots of /home + 3\n  bounded-context samples, and ask the user a *visual* confirmation\n  question — sign-off cannot proceed until the user confirms layout is\n  coherent. Adds the matching decision-rule row to the table.\n\nTop-level:\n- INFOSYNC-REFACTORING-AGENT-GAP-REPORT.md: new file documenting the\n  8 gap classes (G1-G8), root-cause analysis of why each automated\n  check missed them, the exact file→change mapping, and the strategic\n  recommendation to add a `ui-smoke-validator` agent in a future wave.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDB0HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQpMQAAUqdbYFCEsBRsqjCYZ30nMt\nQ+tKZ1AKHvWGv8K5fBjASjGmbwGs4IJEKbPbM+lcOmzVqXCqEsi52MUsGxaAV1fz\nH7EEdRKuEO023/CTX9xiL08zyyOOEG+ShSrdw1W3DMwJo9vQYX6QhXjiTOrxf2GB\nTh/9N43nHGOF6Qw6V4lnPCgHVGHXznMNeiQEV9zUBVbyYSPX/r5X+n0cFfsnCvxk\nKJZetfC+aTSLpGC2AOeFpBxsKk0HQdk2PNLYRszn2bF4Oyghiqkfg9IkcWbu0AUg\nJpQJhrORXGNJEqtslEYUWtfx3EP0WbwFNgaio7Nk029iZwAhJrdnYwGjuKHr/tC1\ng27dCSMo37XQPY+4DUPSEkM6Vw/TN5jDVuE6vd4aCvpsoq1X2YEfc8Q6aAbqB1b0\nJ19MDFq7uHwx1rcKqQHIhAp0lqznQA6k8b+8tWINJcGtFsRHxFoSDh/K/udqqiGm\nD/AN9f5eRo6vio4qW3geEQNLRbccSVS016DGXaz9zOJITu6FwgumebmgEpvTpyXJ\ndQpP8HRF7VgHkDS3ogPBdKyh73x+4EZaF6Wn2OTQu982Yz+HSS2Ozdo4opqPPvmK\ncy4fi9L89Ovq8Peqo/JL3vPAyTUVe0P6ZcSiP13hg77KB2+Z7vhGdeHcmUaobQ14\np4hyQBGwAfJE7iTRux86\n=bfNy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-19T08:19:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/9e73bec18c218db95b220dd2e3f30a835c6afe79","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDllNzNiZWMxOGMyMThkYjk1YjIyMGRkMmUzZjMwYTgzNWM2YWZlNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc","sha":"cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc"}],"sha":"9e73bec18c218db95b220dd2e3f30a835c6afe79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9e73bec18c218db95b220dd2e3f30a835c6afe79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T07:43:43Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T07:43:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(cost): switch 14 agents from opus to sonnet, bump patch versions (#39)\n\nCost optimisation: switch every catalog agent currently on `model: opus`\nto `model: sonnet`, except the meta-orchestrator `orchestrator` which\nthe validator hard-requires to remain opus.\n\nAffected (catalog + marketplace mirror + catalog.json model field):\n- refactoring-supervisor          3.2.0 -> 3.2.1\n- functional-analysis-supervisor  3.0.0 -> 3.0.1\n- technical-analysis-supervisor   2.1.0 -> 2.1.1\n- baseline-testing-supervisor     0.3.0 -> 0.3.1\n- indexing-supervisor             2.0.0 -> 2.0.1\n- refactoring-tobe-supervisor     0.3.0 -> 0.3.1\n- tobe-testing-supervisor         0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n- deliberative-decision-engine    0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n- debate-proposer / -critic / -judge / -risk-reviewer /\n  -operations-reviewer / -replatforming-specialist   each 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n\nAlso strips the now-stale `model_justification:` frontmatter blocks on\nthe converted agents (each block argued for opus; keeping them on a\nsonnet agent would be misleading). The blocks remain on `orchestrator`\nwhere opus is still in use.\n\nValidator: catalog WARNINGS only (pre-existing body-length on same 19\nsupervisors), marketplace PASS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f97327e9b79bf3c27e341987f61fa68b65e88a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/9f97327e9b79bf3c27e341987f61fa68b65e88a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f97327e9b79bf3c27e341987f61fa68b65e88a4\nparent 0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1778917423 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778917423 +0200\n\nchore(cost): switch 14 agents from opus to sonnet, bump patch versions (#39)\n\nCost optimisation: switch every catalog agent currently on `model: opus`\nto `model: sonnet`, except the meta-orchestrator `orchestrator` which\nthe validator hard-requires to remain opus.\n\nAffected (catalog + marketplace mirror + catalog.json model field):\n- refactoring-supervisor          3.2.0 -> 3.2.1\n- functional-analysis-supervisor  3.0.0 -> 3.0.1\n- technical-analysis-supervisor   2.1.0 -> 2.1.1\n- baseline-testing-supervisor     0.3.0 -> 0.3.1\n- indexing-supervisor             2.0.0 -> 2.0.1\n- refactoring-tobe-supervisor     0.3.0 -> 0.3.1\n- tobe-testing-supervisor         0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n- deliberative-decision-engine    0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n- debate-proposer / -critic / -judge / -risk-reviewer /\n  -operations-reviewer / -replatforming-specialist   each 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1\n\nAlso strips the now-stale `model_justification:` frontmatter blocks on\nthe converted agents (each block argued for opus; keeping them on a\nsonnet agent would be misleading). The blocks remain on `orchestrator`\nwhere opus is still in use.\n\nValidator: catalog WARNINGS only (pre-existing body-length on same 19\nsupervisors), marketplace PASS.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCCAvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVM0QAHSXsygs7NsThTmsMNuwSoPH\nUqmk8pCOiLG1ejUBTKlnHUvKssdNGCbCMtB4CO8BSa42kKD86Nnomp4VuO2NQVg7\nZNkPUANUb3zo+LX/D/LoZ4PvGbHGgsbGdmp2E432sRJ2/hlDtJOQ8wmV/X/YmMqQ\n0u2DaBOzmFLhsUfblonhPswPkU0whsGkH222DTgnL5Qgw5GM722KOE+9hAJocpwx\neneFtDxRNLWzJhKFA7/lxxTte5gt2rYzdcRlQG1d3ANRrI//vR/3/wg8BhqDl4Sv\nzy+gy5+CZtJrSWMXRbwqb0DOUbwRwgFupaqGIHohGc/TwbLKB7HPJGdTw8CPSfSV\nBUvHHNE9URcPfc+zVAe8Q0ZNqHXE38xEVJUmwJNBpXMP+1EQpl19TN/inAExTCjU\nv+OblSiFOCg2eafLd8eXDbPVwnKMia7SQO/uD1ypE3OTFVgTV8u1ji4p2wf5X3Kt\nw2MeKolj+rxjWJ9R8X+NGB5nbQG3jpVtCa4qw8nGQCweABXdTKtVigDlYPF/AT4B\naHeBUb2gZbB7mKOcGKDLTXpSb8q+qjgNAw+9Gicc4uKwFgzRVJP1g2TmXwZMtqce\nMoL0pYEgV5udRStIhe7ZeE05zaASS1aiSv6VlBi6oAAiGHdb4yWpYNBHaP9qGLiU\n8ZfxXptvKTYDTtwzwcjF\n=5EqV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T07:43:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGNkYjA2NjkwMmZlM2Q3YTRlYzU3Y2EyMGQwZWFlNDEyNDBiOWI3YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463","sha":"0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463"}],"sha":"cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/cdb066902fe3d7a4ec57ca20d0eae41240b9b7bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-16T07:26:01Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-16T07:26:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(analysis): iterative HITL loop + feature narrative + deliberation for Phases 1-3 (#38)\n\n* release: refactoring-supervisor@3.2.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''refactoring-supervisor'' version 3.2.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: functional-analysis-supervisor@3.0.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''functional-analysis-supervisor'' version 3.0.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: technical-analysis-supervisor@2.1.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''technical-analysis-supervisor'' version 2.1.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: baseline-testing-supervisor@0.3.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''baseline-testing-supervisor'' version 0.3.0 to beta tier.\n\n* feat(analysis): iterative HITL loop + feature narrative + deliberation for Phases 1-3\n\nThe analysis phases (Phase 1 functional, Phase 2 technical, Phase 3\nbaseline testing) now run inside a structured HITL iteration loop\ninstead of a one-shot proceed/revise prompt. After each phase the user\npicks approve / iterate / stop; on iterate the user provides specific\nadjustments and the phase supervisor re-dispatches only the affected\nsub-agents, then produces a new verification report.\n\nWhy: functional analysis in particular is the most delicate part of the\nworkflow — a misunderstanding there propagates everywhere downstream\nand is expensive to undo. The iteration loop lets the human verify and\nadjust the analysis before locking it.\n\nCanonical specs:\n- claude-catalog/docs/refactoring-workflow/iteration-loop.md\n- claude-catalog/docs/refactoring-workflow/phase-verification-report.md\n\nPhase 1 specifics:\n- New 00b-feature-narrative.md written by the supervisor in Wave 3c —\n  plain-prose feature-by-feature chapters, the human-readable entry\n  point. Inserted at slot 00b- so existing numbering is preserved.\n- Wave 3d writes _meta/phase-verification-report.md.\n- Exports gated on approve (no longer regenerated every iteration).\n\nPhase 2 + Phase 3:\n- Lighter changes: verification report + iteration handling + delibera-\n  tion routing on contested findings. Phase 3 explicitly guards the\n  oracle snapshot from silent regeneration.\n\nDeliberation extended to Phases 1-3 (debate triggers + self-escalation\non subjective conflicts).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"045e68c32f1e1c3a8b7b0c10c7a9f298037fe48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/045e68c32f1e1c3a8b7b0c10c7a9f298037fe48c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/0a06d9d776068b2cec142c62f11867324dc4b463","verification":{"payload":"tree 045e68c32f1e1c3a8b7b0c10c7a9f298037fe48c\nparent 3eea4d701edc0bdd684e6b3c892c3bfb5fd4ea3b\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1778916361 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778916361 +0200\n\nfeat(analysis): iterative HITL loop + feature narrative + deliberation for Phases 1-3 (#38)\n\n* release: refactoring-supervisor@3.2.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''refactoring-supervisor'' version 3.2.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: functional-analysis-supervisor@3.0.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''functional-analysis-supervisor'' version 3.0.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: technical-analysis-supervisor@2.1.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''technical-analysis-supervisor'' version 2.1.0 to beta tier.\n\n* release: baseline-testing-supervisor@0.3.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''baseline-testing-supervisor'' version 0.3.0 to beta tier.\n\n* feat(analysis): iterative HITL loop + feature narrative + deliberation for Phases 1-3\n\nThe analysis phases (Phase 1 functional, Phase 2 technical, Phase 3\nbaseline testing) now run inside a structured HITL iteration loop\ninstead of a one-shot proceed/revise prompt. After each phase the user\npicks approve / iterate / stop; on iterate the user provides specific\nadjustments and the phase supervisor re-dispatches only the affected\nsub-agents, then produces a new verification report.\n\nWhy: functional analysis in particular is the most delicate part of the\nworkflow — a misunderstanding there propagates everywhere downstream\nand is expensive to undo. The iteration loop lets the human verify and\nadjust the analysis before locking it.\n\nCanonical specs:\n- claude-catalog/docs/refactoring-workflow/iteration-loop.md\n- claude-catalog/docs/refactoring-workflow/phase-verification-report.md\n\nPhase 1 specifics:\n- New 00b-feature-narrative.md written by the supervisor in Wave 3c —\n  plain-prose feature-by-feature chapters, the human-readable entry\n  point. Inserted at slot 00b- so existing numbering is preserved.\n- Wave 3d writes _meta/phase-verification-report.md.\n- Exports gated on approve (no longer regenerated every iteration).\n\nPhase 2 + Phase 3:\n- Lighter changes: verification report + iteration handling + delibera-\n  tion routing on contested findings. Phase 3 explicitly guards the\n  oracle snapshot from silent regeneration.\n\nDeliberation extended to Phases 1-3 (debate triggers + self-escalation\non subjective conflicts).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqCBwJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlFoQAKXCTm6eBQiWDxdZzbYTbKte\nRSeoEmG7tqToCOsxqfkecFSlOXFJo4OIGILMPtIugqQcWFNjRk1mai2/Th8LVd8J\nP0qd/khYWZrC0mQ78bM4zCvZLdRvZLBPOHdkB3JvV/pojnW9oIS4UnM0hIxXY12C\ncorarRiPibfFxXM5cDrH2s+pbNYCdy2n3es8ZMnqk41BSirsuqK1YZRA9g6p3aiQ\ng2XJtlou0W3Y/hNc5PGmSM5AVi6dqkxzaqHP0AMrH8zvZQZvTWcC+iP96CpkNua8\nSAAlKxpKPnVfAx+wS0nZMhrz8EmKlVgjHzCF4qFLpVg97p0KH0zRwNihFEyQbAEp\nZyDqb3w5OOJ/SmQb2tixlH9WlTH0aVEWcKVlY8jFmQRkix3jm+731lUD1fQtJsBR\nD2pKyxrftjXfnbUCKPQyihibu/cuDZIN6PPQzvYrOcyR0irkaS7z3wCdWFbYYmDP\nLjNiq+2Ux4NHfPPiGh/e25icx3SK2J3jOh58dMYvogQ0b1G6Y0jS1ArMyEGQwIU1\nGjuVXIRb1OlG0GF7s/NTYdZGvW76FMojvvdb+RXLrI4fKZQDYbagfpiUtCJwEhhn\ndTYVOPHV4/x1XaMUxrCx0oEjHXP2PbTAct3fPwE5cQLOY95RokWznNUqelFdrk+h\ntr4H+NKKGN6zQvEws/t7\n=MJ/E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-16T07:26:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscr