55a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c05ec3547c78f335ed790f2790da7d0cd32a4e80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T11:25:20Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T11:25:20Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"refactor(agents): batch extract 9 agents 13-16k chars (avg -32%)\n\nThird sweep, run as 9 parallel extractions. Closes 6 of 9 warnings\nhard; the remaining 3 are soft warnings (dense decision logic — within\nthe ≤12k tolerance the recipe accepts).\n\n  baseline-runner             15 541 →  8 442  (-46%)  3 ref docs\n  api-contract-designer       15 499 →  8 926  (-42%)  3 ref docs\n  frontend-scaffolder         15 433 →  <10k   (-35%)  4 ref docs\n  refactoring-tobe-supervisor 14 419 → 11 251  (-22%)  3 new ref docs (soft)\n  phase4-challenger           14 072 →  9 856  (-30%)  2 ref docs\n  logic-translator            13 907 → 10 493  (-25%)  ref docs (soft)\n  developer-frontend          13 711 →  <10k   (-30%)  2 ref docs\n  tobe-testing-supervisor     13 136 → 11 222  (-15%)  extended + new (soft)\n  wiki-writer                 13 035 →  9 748  (-31%)  2 ref docs\n\nSame pattern as iter-2: each body keeps only Role, When to invoke,\nReference docs anchor, Inputs, Method (decision logic), Outputs,\nStop conditions, Constraints. All output templates / schemas /\nboilerplate moved verbatim. No content invented.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"16bde8f30d13c1175476d57f6199878174128517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/16bde8f30d13c1175476d57f6199878174128517"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/c05ec3547c78f335ed790f2790da7d0cd32a4e80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/c05ec3547c78f335ed790f2790da7d0cd32a4e80","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGMwNWVjMzU0N2M3OGYzMzVlZDc5MGYyNzkwZGE3ZDBjZDMyYTRlODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982","sha":"6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982"}],"sha":"c05ec3547c78f335ed790f2790da7d0cd32a4e80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c05ec3547c78f335ed790f2790da7d0cd32a4e80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:39:08Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:39:08Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"refactor(agents): batch extract 5 agents 17-19k chars (avg -47%)\n\nSecond sweep of the body-length cleanup, run as 5 parallel extractions.\nCloses 4 of 5 body-length warnings. The fifth (decomposition-architect)\nstays at 11 218 chars — soft warning accepted, dense decision logic\nthat the recipe forbids extracting.\n\n  hardening-architect      19 133 → 9 624   (-50%)  3 ref docs\n  decomposition-architect  17 963 → 11 218  (-36%)  3 ref docs (soft)\n  data-mapper              17 906 → <10k    (-43%)  3 ref docs\n  indexing-supervisor      17 431 → 6 365   (-64%)  4 ref docs\n  backend-scaffolder       17 207 → <10k    (-43%)  5 ref docs\n\nEach agent body now keeps only decision logic (Role, When to invoke,\nInputs, Method, Outputs, Stop conditions, Constraints) plus a Reference\ndocs anchor table. All output templates, ADR skeletons, code\nboilerplate, JSON/YAML schemas, and example tables moved verbatim to\nref docs under claude-catalog/docs/<topic>/<agent>/. No content\ninvented.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"38337bdcf2379e73fdfd4de81459a5d6ac4537d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/38337bdcf2379e73fdfd4de81459a5d6ac4537d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDZiMWQ4ODA5NWQ4NTJlZGYzOGE5NWFlYzM2MzZkNDhiMjhlODU5ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37","sha":"22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37"}],"sha":"6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6b1d88095d852edf38a95aec3636d48b28e85982"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:31:46Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:31:46Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"refactor(refactoring-supervisor): extract phase content to docs/, add `When to invoke` (-79%)\n\nThe largest non-deferred supervisor in the registry (68 780 chars) is\nnow 14 649 — a 79% reduction. Closes the structural rubric warning\n(\"missing `## When to invoke`\") and brings the body-length warning\nwithin range of the irreducible floor (decision rules + constraints +\ninvariants must remain in the body per the extraction recipe).\n\nSix reference docs under claude-catalog/docs/refactoring-workflow/:\n- bootstrap-protocol.md   — Phase 0 of the workflow''s bootstrap\n- schematics.md           — pre-phase ASCII schematics (Phase 0..4)\n- per-phase-protocol.md   — Steps A..F + Phase 4 driving + recaps\n- workflow-manifest-spec.md  — JSON schema for workflow-manifest.json\n- phase-4-replatforming.md   — Phase 4 7-step structure + hard gates\n- activation-examples.md  — user phrasings that route here\n\nThe supervisor body keeps only the decision logic: Role, When to invoke\n(new), Reference docs anchor, Workflow phases summary, Decision rules,\nEscalation triggers, Constraints, Output format. Validates the\nsupervisor-extraction recipe end-to-end on the largest deferred\nsupervisor in the registry.\n\nDirect main commit per user request — no PR for the warning-cleanup\niteration.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ec1c02eb873ad5784037bb0ef020958834dcafce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/ec1c02eb873ad5784037bb0ef020958834dcafce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDIyZDQ3YTRlMzJjMWNjYTk0ZjcwN2RjYWRlZGM4YTMxMjIwMDVmMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca","sha":"1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca"}],"sha":"22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/22d47a4e32c1cca94f707dcadedc8a3122005f37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:19:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:19:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(docs): document optional scripts/ pattern for deterministic helpers (#33)\n\nSeveral rules in registry skills are mechanical: parse this YAML, count\nsections, check a regex, validate a frontmatter field. Today they live\nin prose that the model interprets every invocation — slower, more\nexpensive, and prone to drift across calls.\n\nhow-to-write-a-capability.md § \"Deterministic helpers\" codifies the\nAnthropic principle \"Claude orchestrates, the code executes\". A skill\nmay now ship a scripts/ directory:\n\n    skills/<topic>/<name>/\n    ├── <name>.md\n    ├── references/         (progressive-disclosure attachments)\n    └── scripts/\n        ├── README.md       (mandatory: invocation + I/O + exit codes)\n        └── <script>.py\n\nThe skill remains tools: Read — the consuming agent runs the script via\nits own Bash tool. The skill body must name each script explicitly with\na Bash recipe so the agent knows when and how to call it.\n\nreview-checklist.md gains skill-specific subsections for scripts/ and\nreferences/: the scripts README must document invocation/IO/exit codes,\nthe script logic must be genuinely deterministic (judgment stays in\nprose), and no script may duplicate logic from another skill''s scripts/.\n\nThe validator already excludes scripts/ from capability scanning (added\nin the progressive-disclosure PR), so no validator change is needed\nhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bc0c73f1fb7b84d01c68fc1ae8d9ed513cf8c87a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/bc0c73f1fb7b84d01c68fc1ae8d9ed513cf8c87a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca","verification":{"payload":"tree bc0c73f1fb7b84d01c68fc1ae8d9ed513cf8c87a\nparent 0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777803574 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777803574 +0200\n\nfeat(docs): document optional scripts/ pattern for deterministic helpers (#33)\n\nSeveral rules in registry skills are mechanical: parse this YAML, count\nsections, check a regex, validate a frontmatter field. Today they live\nin prose that the model interprets every invocation — slower, more\nexpensive, and prone to drift across calls.\n\nhow-to-write-a-capability.md § \"Deterministic helpers\" codifies the\nAnthropic principle \"Claude orchestrates, the code executes\". A skill\nmay now ship a scripts/ directory:\n\n    skills/<topic>/<name>/\n    ├── <name>.md\n    ├── references/         (progressive-disclosure attachments)\n    └── scripts/\n        ├── README.md       (mandatory: invocation + I/O + exit codes)\n        └── <script>.py\n\nThe skill remains tools: Read — the consuming agent runs the script via\nits own Bash tool. The skill body must name each script explicitly with\na Bash recipe so the agent knows when and how to call it.\n\nreview-checklist.md gains skill-specific subsections for scripts/ and\nreferences/: the scripts README must document invocation/IO/exit codes,\nthe script logic must be genuinely deterministic (judgment stays in\nprose), and no script may duplicate logic from another skill''s scripts/.\n\nThe validator already excludes scripts/ from capability scanning (added\nin the progressive-disclosure PR), so no validator change is needed\nhere.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9yE2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAE6YQAISfwwNMLblo4Iwg4/LMUZXI\nB0ACCQajL7/neXzWM6QbL/krN4P+4vK67kgodulKminsJJeTDyzh7wJrJYSkG9xf\nLyVxmGkwp9XBPEVdpaJ9cbA/c0ZpJ/umBUadAJaqgM2SZqUVebiw2r90YIPoMoVc\nyxRAHen8FkmDNyLSkUhhh93LIpzECLdh4GNs/MlJnBrutppUv8DztBhQBGvpBltc\n4EzCzMYPWEk/3EOpanFjzxvbVV1EA4zE/hiU5pa42B3I3Grssv4maD5elmeLPyzf\nCj3QLoKiYqDFw58hVA+Ejzx6nUEzhrYjWks8X/ZNtLNHVbN/H8SEdv4VkHjROMlB\nlZrg/dO5xIxIYxIDKET++v3a0re/U+Qge/aVt+JjwHasjH6xxaVzuUkndDA65L6d\nQIjVt3GVoE8+NGJHgW7f626iYBt0CIOqgB57d8KSukNSeLRlEc93ibmESvGPWHt8\nLzhSzr+dEP+ul4yXiKRoHzD7TqmvXGST5W/wH+vg8knXLZdAmKein5h3YbZeo8iu\n4lm9TbelOg/i5yddzGTLwmEJ5hFiKUtWstNIqp0FMjyNPsqEETjCGjgfW3fKgZY0\n8d9B/YBQQoU7qeVZG6IU+/jJG0UI9vts6H/iiurqQ/Lg16sS4L7V7jZkj+4zuaK7\nbOd4QogT3yA2Gq3XAJAU\n=QDoq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-03T10:19:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDFmYjA3OTI0YjNkMTE3M2Q5NGY1ZGE4ZTE4YmE2NTlmMzZiMGU1Y2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3","sha":"0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3"}],"sha":"1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/1fb07924b3d1173d94f5da8e18ba659f36b0e5ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:15:22Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:15:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(docs): document progressive disclosure for skills + validator support (#32)\n\n* feat(governance): convergence as fast path for beta→stable promotion\n\nThe existing promotion rule required ≥2 projects + ≥30 days uniformly\n(now Criterion A). When two independent project specializations under\ndifferent `.claude/agents/` introduce the same modification to a beta\ncapability, that convergence is a stronger maturity signal than calendar\ntime — and waiting out 30 days delays adopting a fix two teams have\nalready identified.\n\nCriterion B promotes immediately on convergence evidence. The promotion\nPR must cite both project specializations with paths and the shared\ndiff hunk. review-checklist.md §10 enforces the declaration and evidence\nof whichever criterion was used.\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"convergence between users is a stronger maturity signal than time on\nshelf, and the registry did not capture it\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(docs): document progressive disclosure for skills + validator support\n\nThe registry''s larger skills (postgresql-expert 4.5k words,\nbackend-orchestrator 3.3k, unicredit-design-system 3.1k) load all their\ncontent every time. The Anthropic skill specification defines a three-\nlevel loading model — frontmatter / SKILL body / references/ — that the\nregistry was not codifying.\n\nhow-to-write-a-capability.md § \"Skills\" now documents:\n- the three loading levels and what belongs in each\n- soft cap of 3 000 words on the body, hard cap of 5 000 (Anthropic)\n- the optional directory layout\n  skills/<topic>/<name>/{<name>.md, references/*.md}\n- how the body links to reference files (plain markdown links, no\n  auto-load — the body must point to the specific file)\n\nvalidate_catalog.py adds an iter_capability_files() helper that\nexcludes references/ and scripts/ subdirectories from capability\nscanning. All 9 rglob(\"*.md\") sites use the helper. The flat layout\n(<topic>/<name>.md) is unaffected — only nested directory layouts\ngain support for attachment subdirs.\n\nThe scripts/ exclusion is added now (rather than in the next PR) so the\ntwo follow-ups stay independent: progressive disclosure is the docs\nchange, and the next PR will document the scripts/ pattern itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0200a537232ae44099a827ca264e2b61d823620e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/0200a537232ae44099a827ca264e2b61d823620e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/0b8d780d207c0d0a3fcfacad9ff841f5f4ede2e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0200a537232ae44099a827ca264e2b61d823620e\nparent 3ed5bf6055895ac36f69c3bb0493777a6003b08d\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777803322 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777803322 +0200\n\nfeat(docs): document progressive disclosure for skills + validator support (#32)\n\n* feat(governance): convergence as fast path for beta→stable promotion\n\nThe existing promotion rule required ≥2 projects + ≥30 days uniformly\n(now Criterion A). When two independent project specializations under\ndifferent `.claude/agents/` introduce the same modification to a beta\ncapability, that convergence is a stronger maturity signal than calendar\ntime — and waiting out 30 days delays adopting a fix two teams have\nalready identified.\n\nCriterion B promotes immediately on convergence evidence. The promotion\nPR must cite both project specializations with paths and the shared\ndiff hunk. review-checklist.md §10 enforces the declaration and evidence\nof whichever criterion was used.\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"convergence between users is a stronger maturity signal than time on\nshelf, and the registry did not capture it\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(docs): document progressive disclosure for skills + validator support\n\nThe registry''s larger skills (postgresql-expert 4.5k words,\nbackend-orchestrator 3.3k, unicredit-design-system 3.1k) load all their\ncontent every time. The Anthropic skill specification defines a three-\nlevel loading model — frontmatter / SKILL body / references/ — that the\nregistry was not codifying.\n\nhow-to-write-a-capability.md § \"Skills\" now documents:\n- the three loading levels and what belongs in each\n- soft cap of 3 000 words on the body, hard cap of 5 000 (Anthropic)\n- the optional directory layout\n  skills/<topic>/<name>/{<name>.md, references/*.md}\n- how the body links to reference files (plain markdown links, no\n  auto-load — the body must point to the specific file)\n\nvalidate_catalog.py adds an iter_capability_files() helper that\nexcludes references/ and scripts/ subdirectories from capability\nscanning. All 9 rglob(\"*.md\") sites use the helper. The flat layout\n(<topic>/<name>.md) is unaffected — only nested directory layouts\ngain support for attachment subdirs.\n\nThe scripts/ exclusion is added now (rather than in the next PR) so the\ntwo follow-ups stay independent: progressive disclosure is the docs\nchange, and the next PR will document the scripts/ pattern itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9yA6CRC1a