me modification to a beta\ncapability, that convergence is a stronger maturity signal than calendar\ntime — and waiting out 30 days delays adopting a fix two teams have\nalready identified.\n\nCriterion B promotes immediately on convergence evidence. The promotion\nPR must cite both project specializations with paths and the shared\ndiff hunk. review-checklist.md §10 enforces the declaration and evidence\nof whichever criterion was used.\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"convergence between users is a stronger maturity signal than time on\nshelf, and the registry did not capture it\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a00c29804efcf8dfa50f601d0b5fb59bc1306ed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/a00c29804efcf8dfa50f601d0b5fb59bc1306ed3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/3ed5bf6055895ac36f69c3bb0493777a6003b08d","verification":{"payload":"tree a00c29804efcf8dfa50f601d0b5fb59bc1306ed3\nparent 9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777802930 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777802930 +0200\n\nfeat(governance): convergence as fast path for beta→stable promotion (#31)\n\nThe existing promotion rule required ≥2 projects + ≥30 days uniformly\n(now Criterion A). When two independent project specializations under\ndifferent `.claude/agents/` introduce the same modification to a beta\ncapability, that convergence is a stronger maturity signal than calendar\ntime — and waiting out 30 days delays adopting a fix two teams have\nalready identified.\n\nCriterion B promotes immediately on convergence evidence. The promotion\nPR must cite both project specializations with paths and the shared\ndiff hunk. review-checklist.md §10 enforces the declaration and evidence\nof whichever criterion was used.\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"convergence between users is a stronger maturity signal than time on\nshelf, and the registry did not capture it\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9x6yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ2QQAD3BdNbmH7JQm6wpF0Se8hOm\n98n/VjXCvDkgH9M/E07wiyTkNRQ0zh/8+be4Y4IkWCdIm8Ok7MzFFNclHU+hOLQQ\n+MFqhN0ZJeSbJyDotVcjc0egHAy/3vyF4ZP95iww+yl97jhNho0vUmo62XvYqdKX\njLsMiUwF09cbojlDmh5Jgy8K4hpshv0yylmCwggADjOq39N4WqpvBs3wqV3ekpZu\ns73ifh2GaKITtU7bHb+/LnxOkQ8Tffk7wrCPPLEttIspVOtC1xcye7DGjd7gpPWy\nMcwyvvDDQNgDMlv947WJ1x30pxEekOrikRC05yPoKYHQQB0vg2L9UqF9GUqIHrpn\nsmYVhS4ZElJN+h7fiFF2SK+9ltjYrZuDGsbK+PXLD3TGcqRI9Wj6bRng9ec579af\nvmU/ewsSYfiBm4mILl+GGP+R4j2p70hUIXv12nGdZH+3pz/KZ1Y3iber6NWG/I7S\nUAXMhpjri0WUON//Jre7wvLH6edn6vBoLw9UCY/gr12WnSIrfwuF0i29YVLgdpsO\nx6+fE7vkkai5zfspP4Z56xSpUMyj/Km1+YAU6WWHi2HjelxjrLIR6XvGN1WGZwpl\nKDEr5novl5BucrfsPTC1j/ARTuw6eevySvpNpRcW2knHmPIeu74nLHIpK0vyyuZ/\n+8+8d5q3nb0vIq4nRDIz\n=+ZdA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-03T10:08:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/3ed5bf6055895ac36f69c3bb0493777a6003b08d","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDNlZDViZjYwNTU4OTVhYzM2ZjY5YzNiYjA0OTM3NzdhNjAwM2IwOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8","sha":"9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8"}],"sha":"3ed5bf6055895ac36f69c3bb0493777a6003b08d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/3ed5bf6055895ac36f69c3bb0493777a6003b08d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:03:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T10:03:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(governance): add ANTI-PATTERNS.md negative-knowledge log (#30)\n\nDeprecating a capability used to remove the rationale together with the\nfile 90 days after the deprecation notice. Future contributors proposing\na similar capability had no way to find the precedent.\n\nANTI-PATTERNS.md captures what was tried, why it failed, what replaced\nit, and the conditions under which a retry would be valid (the\n\"Do not retry unless\" clause).\n\nThree governance hooks make the lookup mandatory:\n- GOVERNANCE.md: deprecation PRs must add the entry in the same PR\n- review-checklist.md §9: reviewers must search the file before approval\n- README files: the new log is listed alongside CHANGELOG.md\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"deprecated patterns lose their motivation when the file is removed\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c2fd82a1f36dd34059cc6a421e94049ba59efce0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/c2fd82a1f36dd34059cc6a421e94049ba59efce0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8","verification":{"payload":"tree c2fd82a1f36dd34059cc6a421e94049ba59efce0\nparent 55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777802637 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777802637 +0200\n\nfeat(governance): add ANTI-PATTERNS.md negative-knowledge log (#30)\n\nDeprecating a capability used to remove the rationale together with the\nfile 90 days after the deprecation notice. Future contributors proposing\na similar capability had no way to find the precedent.\n\nANTI-PATTERNS.md captures what was tried, why it failed, what replaced\nit, and the conditions under which a retry would be valid (the\n\"Do not retry unless\" clause).\n\nThree governance hooks make the lookup mandatory:\n- GOVERNANCE.md: deprecation PRs must add the entry in the same PR\n- review-checklist.md §9: reviewers must search the file before approval\n- README files: the new log is listed alongside CHANGELOG.md\n\nCloses the gap identified by the Anthropic auto-improving-agents review:\n\"deprecated patterns lose their motivation when the file is removed\".\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9x2NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg4gQACaJ3hyf+M7xRrYdkGgfVDWn\nSdCT3RwpjG5cE+lediqC36oZMo9lsgC+ZcWEY6AXqCxjnLSlJcTssBtir+YR2LIX\ncc53NKqkqGLcQ2PW75hGc6XPk5hqBQqaTpC4waRkMocRcqTuqMzv4GR6q0U9NCWS\naB+5ausNvfIOI3oN49mO/eTns+BTmmHTTY49GDBOZXJP7X5VtORC041ECvdkAfoT\nMM/ScWGWPkZqC6R+6VNpR2ZbIjJLmRqvp7gpSSefLtrK7f2VXlLcV7ssLCMupere\nrCptJJiNCYgnD+HKBMKqC+s3U5OYRtg7//+GKLyFGDWckU4RsdPh4kSdJ6Oj9TeR\nisvkRSVCI2f0sPYg+aFsIVe4qT5sZRQMGemYKwDq5NryEXqxo+KHcpSPrt050aQS\nfwEjqrsDsuvWDBgccGm6ci32S0I9zcOxK+tfeynDFkJn6v0N09yGdm0n0azXqwRL\nVyvskOPnv9mk7XeAzYZ0yGmq1UgAXG0IxKo4civz+hxDgH4NqktFmTaNOQ5LfdgY\ng5D2J7T/dlr54FXr5pzk9XahIcVvpiLaNqT0QUMiHVj6IjYuGWnAWIlIk9ZSbDEM\nBBiTqNAkNiUUknnRDq4IrfBuTst8F/9iwiAUamjf7C0TapLFSFzvMGzTF3yak8Pl\nz7pcQ8SOxym6tpsiKPMP\n=dL4q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-03T10:03:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDliMzc2ZWVmZTQ5NDgyYmYwOTI1NWRkYjBlMzA5NDg1OTQ1MTEzZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7","sha":"55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7"}],"sha":"9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/9b376eefe49482bf09255ddb0e309485945113e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T12:31:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T12:31:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(supervisors): extract phase narrative from 4 medium supervisors (avg -54%) (#29)\n\nApplies the supervisor-extraction recipe (PR #28) to all 4 remaining\nmedium-large phase supervisors:\n\n- baseline-testing-supervisor:    32 622 → 14 789 chars (-55%)\n- tobe-testing-supervisor:        32 860 → 15 485 chars (-53%)\n- technical-analysis-supervisor:  30 087 → 14 060 chars (-53%)\n- functional-analysis-supervisor: 29 855 → 12 968 chars (-57%)\n\nEach gains a `## Reference docs` anchor table linking 3-5 reference\ndocs under `claude-catalog/docs/<topic>/`:\n- output-layout.md (output dir tree + frontmatter contract)\n- policies.md / dispatch-mode.md (Q1/Q2/Q3 modes, dispatch decision)\n- phase-plan.md (Phase 0 bootstrap + per-wave dispatch)\n- dispatch-prompt-template.md (worker prompt boilerplate, framework blocks)\n- recap-templates.md (per-wave + final recap schemas, where applicable)\n\nTotal: 16 new reference docs in 4 topic folders.\n\nSupervisor bodies retain only decision logic (escalation triggers,\ndecision rules, drift / preservation checks, manifest update, hard\nconstraints). Phase narrative, mode descriptions, prompt boilerplate,\noutput-layout schemas, and recap templates are now read on demand.\n\nValidator unchanged at 45 warnings (-1 supervisor over 30k → -1 over\nceiling, others moved within band; bodies still over 10k by design —\nfixing would force extraction of decision logic, which the recipe\nforbids). Marketplace validation passes clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04f08442f269341a91986b0d05634050a3a95189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/04f08442f269341a91986b0d05634050a3a95189"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/55d93cf77d5efd6e4364c29875bd52e57a05b6d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 04f08442f269341a91986b0d05634050a3a95189\nparent 596365d97fb3bb6f6777b685caa1978ff62832bf\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777638717 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777638717 +0200\n\nrefactor(supervisors): extract phase narrative from 4 medium supervisors (avg -54%) (#29)\n\nApplies the supervisor-extraction recipe (PR #28) to all 4 remaining\nmedium-large phase supervisors:\n\n- baseline-testing-supervisor:    32 622 → 14 789 chars (-55%)\n- tobe-testing-supervisor:        32 860 → 15 485 chars (-53%)\n- technical-analysis-supervisor:  30 087 → 14 060 chars (-53%)\n- functional-analysis-supervisor: 29 855 → 12 968 chars (-57%)\n\nEach gains a `## Reference docs` anchor table linking 3-5 reference\ndocs under `claude-catalog/docs/<topic>/`:\n- output-layout.md (output dir tree + frontmatter contract)\n- policies.md / dispatch-mode.md (Q1/Q2/Q3 modes, dispatch decision)\n- phase-plan.md (Phase 0 bootstrap + per-wave dispatch)\n- dispatch-prompt-template.md (worker prompt boilerplate, framework blocks)\n- recap-templates.md (per-wave + final recap schemas, where applicable)\n\nTotal: 16 new reference docs in 4 topic folders.\n\nSupervisor bodies retain only decision logic (escalation triggers,\ndecision rules, drift / preservation checks, manifest update, hard\nconstraints). Phase narrative, mode descriptions, prompt boilerplate,\noutput-layout schemas, and recap templates are now read on demand.\n\nValidator unchanged at 45 warnings (-1 supervisor over 30k → -1 over\nceiling, others moved within band; bodies still over 10k by design —\nfixing would force extraction of decision logic, which the recipe\nforbids). Marketplace validation passes clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFc