every supervision step.\n\nBody still over the 10 000-char rubric ceiling (16 890) but down by\nhalf — further trimming would extract decision logic, which the recipe\nexplicitly forbids.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9FB1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA59sQACePgVbxR8xeR1gXcPz499oT\nhs/0JaBcaVbc8ftkiKxWK/qgv7rqgZLbtheWJfajncxLL9gEoy/CVqXCUYXUMVy5\nsCiD1z3lvNSeeiswMe7BBNlD+pOhSf66PubRYk/DuvOaPGIj8tV+62FxcUVmuhAS\nQ4KbJasIcrN//ir65KBVuOApR26bXbwo5B13ryZWRVAOAcbE5UDEzX1wRubLQvkw\nfYEfZLNQjPmMXdB1Rxi4ZiUYT92Beii5Rd6lf2RkMYzW+WeJkButlVCnAm+Ha7ze\nOz4zUCQk4JC5RvTeF+caEM60vmkkiyQP5Kjt/XWzgk2nmziuX6iP4kw/TozMg1a/\nxo8F8UYSZtKRF7yP29S6ZdzA0WUuX0wQD0mxrsP60CJPTEYxkT605xBqDlgp9x/q\nx5RnRE988J89z5Nwa65437aoKKJ0NxB9P2hz3RxHFJGJeTXw2Ug8ie+vBs28yY8R\n09AyGZMuq9bEm6lzP4DXlmV4rEMc5t9Ts38PU3F2rV/gPVX1WJcsf3qAZa5CWh8A\njX/PiwSRsqENNkwsSEvn3TQ4y4l8AEd0fHEH0+O0exB4CzBEnoyen1hmvTKBxsni\nKyewCiHDrwm8A3/Dc5o7pfxHgv4vbBxXg+niyLHZmA3lOFfZ7F2He611m99j1c2X\n0UELa2UWoNEUQmJLvM3t\n=gcM8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-01T07:04:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/596365d97fb3bb6f6777b685caa1978ff62832bf","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDU5NjM2NWQ5N2ZiM2JiNmY2Nzc3YjY4NWNhYTE5NzhmZjYyODMyYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/6bf0a03ea0cf4bb28a44641391215f0fe5b68124","sha":"6bf0a03ea0cf4bb28a44641391215f0fe5b68124","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6bf0a03ea0cf4bb28a44641391215f0fe5b68124"}],"sha":"596365d97fb3bb6f6777b685caa1978ff62832bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/596365d97fb3bb6f6777b685caa1978ff62832bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/6bf0a03ea0cf4bb28a44641391215f0fe5b68124/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T06:29:40Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T06:29:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Align registry to Anthropic rubrics (skills A, agents A−, CLAUDE.md A 97/100) (#27)\n\n* release: registry-auditor@0.1.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''registry-auditor'' version 0.1.0 to beta tier.\n\n* refactor(registry): align 41 skill descriptions + validator to Anthropic rubrics\n\nFirst sweep after the registry-auditor baseline. Closes the highest-impact\ntrigger-reliability gap: every skill description now starts with\n\"This skill should be used when...\" (or the pushy \"ALWAYS use this skill\nwhen...\" for orchestrators), carries 2-3 verbatim trigger phrases, and an\nexplicit \"Do not use...\" scope-out clause.\n\nValidator extended to enforce the new format on skills going forward, and\nto flag agent rubric gaps (missing `## When to invoke`, body > 10k chars)\nas warnings — gradual rollout, no regressions blocked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-2 — When-to-invoke for 7 supervisors, color normalisation, scaffold rubric\n\nCloses the next slice of registry-auditor findings:\n\n- `## When to invoke` added to the 7 top-level supervisors (orchestrator\n  + 6 phase supervisors). 68/76 agents still missing — refactoring-supervisor\n  deferred for v3.0.0; the rest will land via the new scaffold template.\n\n- Scaffold templates in new-capability.sh aligned to Anthropic rubrics:\n  every new agent now ships with the When-to-invoke skeleton; every new\n  skill ships with the \"This skill should be used when...\" prefix + triggers\n  + scope-out clause. Eliminates regression risk going forward.\n\n- Color frontmatter tightened to Anthropic spec (red/blue/green/yellow/\n  magenta/cyan). 9 files normalised, validator updated.\n\n- 5 skill bodies de-drifted to imperative voice.\n\n- CLAUDE.md refreshed: capability list current, conventions codify the\n  rubric so future contributors don''t need the auditor to learn the rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-3 — bulk close A1+A4+A5; agents 0/76 → 75/76 rubric-shaped\n\nCloses the three highest-residual agent rubric gaps in one sweep:\n\n- Pattern A1 (description openers): 76/76 agents now start with the\n  Anthropic-spec form `Use this agent when/to/for ...`. Validator updated\n  to accept both new and legacy prefix.\n\n- Pattern A4 (missing color): 39 agents that omitted color get their\n  topic supervisor''s colour. Catalog is now 100 % spec-color-compliant.\n\n- Pattern A5 (rubric pointer): 75/76 descriptions end with\n  `See \"When to invoke\" in the agent body for worked scenarios.`\n\n- Pattern A2 (missing When-to-invoke): 75/76 agents now carry the\n  section. Pipeline workers (47) got topic-templated content with\n  output_hint extracted from description; standalone agents (20) got\n  bespoke per-file content. refactoring-supervisor deliberately\n  skipped — to be done with its v3.0.0 restructure.\n\nValidator warnings down from 107 (iter-2) to 49 (-54%). The 48\nremaining body>10k warnings are intentional (the 6 phase supervisors)\nplus ~40 deep workers; all queued for follow-up extraction PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-4 — bespoke 47 pipeline When-to-invoke; backfill Typical triggers; skill voice polish\n\nCloses the auditor''s iter-3 findings:\n\n- A6 (content quality of 47 pipeline workers): bulk-templated content\n  replaced with hand-authored 2-bullet scenarios per agent, structured\n  along the auditor''s recommended archetypes. Removes verbatim\n  repetition, self-contradictions, broken-English substitutions, and\n  the 1782-char wall-of-text on codebase-mapper.\n\n- A2-NEW (rubric middle clause): `Typical triggers include …` clause\n  backfilled in 75 descriptions, derived from `## When to invoke`\n  bullet titles with acronym preservation.\n\n- S2/S4 (skill voice drift): 9 imperative-voice fixes across 5 skills.\n  `## Role\\n\\nYou are` openers preserved as registry convention.\n\nValidator warnings: 49 → 45 (~10% incremental drop after the much\nlarger iter-3 jump). Agent rubric structural defects fully closed at\n75/76 (only refactoring-supervisor still deferred for v3.0.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-5 — drift to 0; supervisor-extraction template; CLAUDE.md actionability\n\nCloses the auditor''s iter-4 quick wins #1, #2, #5:\n\n- 9 final second-person drifts in skill bodies fixed. Pattern split:\n  - 4 Role-boundary `You do not X — you provide Y` rewritten as\n    `Does not X — provides Y` (rest-api-standards, java-spring-standards,\n    accenture-branding, testing-standards).\n  - 4 targeted single-line fixes (spring-architecture, angular-expert,\n    functional-reconstruction, uml-diagram-generator).\n  - 1 fix in browser-automation.\n  Residual drift = registry idioms only (Role opener, What-you-X headings,\n  code comments).\n\n- claude-catalog/docs/supervisor-extraction-template.md added with a\n  fully worked Phase 4 W1 example. CLAUDE.md links to it from the\n  agent-rubric convention. Closes the auditor''s \"Actionability 14/15\"\n  gap and gives the next contributor extracting a supervisor a\n  copy-adapt starting point.\n\nValidator unchanged at 45 warnings (the drift fixes don''t trigger\nwarnings; body-length warnings remain until extraction lands).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6293816b04bcf23f319c1c4036347f926b799b28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/6293816b04bcf23f319c1c4036347f926b799b28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/6bf0a03ea0cf4bb28a44641391215f0fe5b68124","verification":{"payload":"tree 6293816b04bcf23f319c1c4036347f926b799b28\nparent 8d97433fdff111a77f7d974752b6e05d59e779c7\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777616980 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777616980 +0200\n\nAlign registry to Anthropic rubrics (skills A, agents A−, CLAUDE.md A 97/100) (#27)\n\n* release: registry-auditor@0.1.0 → beta\n\nPublished capability ''registry-auditor'' version 0.1.0 to beta tier.\n\n* refactor(registry): align 41 skill descriptions + validator to Anthropic rubrics\n\nFirst sweep after the registry-auditor baseline. Closes the highest-impact\ntrigger-reliability gap: every skill description now starts with\n\"This skill should be used when...\" (or the pushy \"ALWAYS use this skill\nwhen...\" for orchestrators), carries 2-3 verbatim trigger phrases, and an\nexplicit \"Do not use...\" scope-out clause.\n\nValidator extended to enforce the new format on skills going forward, and\nto flag agent rubric gaps (missing `## When to invoke`, body > 10k chars)\nas warnings — gradual rollout, no regressions blocked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-2 — When-to-invoke for 7 supervisors, color normalisation, scaffold rubric\n\nCloses the next slice of registry-auditor findings:\n\n- `## When to invoke` added to the 7 top-level supervisors (orchestrator\n  + 6 phase supervisors). 68/76 agents still missing — refactoring-supervisor\n  deferred for v3.0.0; the rest will land via the new scaffold template.\n\n- Scaffold templates in new-capability.sh aligned to Anthropic rubrics:\n  every new agent now ships with the When-to-invoke skeleton; every new\n  skill ships with the \"This skill should be used when...\" prefix + triggers\n  + scope-out clause. Eliminates regression risk going forward.\n\n- Color frontmatter tightened to Anthropic spec (red/blue/green/yellow/\n  magenta/cyan). 9 files normalised, validator updated.\n\n- 5 skill bodies de-drifted to imperative voice.\n\n- CLAUDE.md refreshed: capability list current, conventions codify the\n  rubric so future contributors don''t need the auditor to learn the rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-3 — bulk close A1+A4+A5; agents 0/76 → 75/76 rubric-shaped\n\nCloses the three highest-residual agent rubric gaps in one sweep:\n\n- Pattern A1 (description openers): 76/76 agents now start with the\n  Anthropic-spec form `Use this agent when/to/for ...`. Validator updated\n  to accept both new and legacy prefix.\n\n- Pattern A4 (missing color): 39 agents that omitted color get their\n  topic supervisor''s colour. Catalog is now 100 % spec-color-compliant.\n\n- Pattern A5 (rubric pointer): 75/76 descriptions end with\n  `See \"When to invoke\" in the agent body for worked scenarios.`\n\n- Pattern A2 (missing When-to-invoke): 75/76 agents now carry the\n  section. Pipeline workers (47) got topic-templated content with\n  output_hint extracted from description; standalone agents (20) got\n  bespoke per-file content. refactoring-supervisor deliberately\n  skipped — to be done with its v3.0.0 restructure.\n\nValidator warnings down from 107 (iter-2) to 49 (-54%). The 48\nremaining body>10k warnings are intentional (the 6 phase supervisors)\nplus ~40 deep workers; all queued for follow-up extraction PRs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-4 — bespoke 47 pipeline When-to-invoke; backfill Typical triggers; skill voice polish\n\nCloses the auditor''s iter-3 findings:\n\n- A6 (content quality of 47 pipeline workers): bulk-templated content\n  replaced with hand-authored 2-bullet scenarios per agent, structured\n  along the auditor''s recommended archetypes. Removes verbatim\n  repetition, self-contradictions, broken-English substitutions, and\n  the 1782-char wall-of-text on codebase-mapper.\n\n- A2-NEW (rubric middle clause): `Typical triggers include …` clause\n  backfilled in 75 descriptions, derived from `## When to invoke`\n  bullet titles with acronym preservation.\n\n- S2/S4 (skill voice drift): 9 imperative-voice fixes across 5 skills.\n  `## Role\\n\\nYou are` openers preserved as registry convention.\n\nValidator warnings: 49 → 45 (~10% incremental drop after the much\nlarger iter-3 jump). Agent rubric structural defects fully closed at\n75/76 (only refactoring-supervisor still deferred for v3.0.0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(registry): iter-5 — drift to 0; supervisor-extraction template; CLAUDE.md actionability\n\nCloses the auditor''s iter-4 quick wins #1, #2, #5:\n\n- 9 final second-person drifts in skill bodies fixed. Pattern split:\n  - 4 Role-boundary `You do not X — you provide Y` rewritten as\n    `Does not X — provides Y` (rest-api-standards, java-spring-standards,\n    accenture-branding, testing-standards).\n  - 4 targeted single-line fixes (spring-architecture, angular-expert,\n    functional-reconstruction, uml-diagram-generator).\n  - 1 fix in browser-automation.\n  Residual drift = registry idioms only (Role opener, What-you-X headings,\n  code comments).\n\n- claude-catalog/docs/supervisor-extraction-template.md added with a\n  fully worked Phase 4 W1 example. CLAUDE.md links to it from the\n  agent-rubric convention. Closes the auditor''s \"Actionability 14/15\"\n  gap and gives the next contributor extracting a supervisor a\n  copy-adapt starting point.\n\nValidator unchanged at 45 warnings (the drift fixes don''t trigger\nwarnings; body-length warnings remain until extraction lands).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9EhUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe24QAHrShkWi+CPEGThAAtLWfT65\nlVXpDisO