ls nest by framework where relevant\n  (skills/frontend/{angular,react,qwik,vue,vanilla}/). 114 catalog.json\n  entries had their `file` field rewritten to the new path.\n\n- validate_marketplace.py: accepts both flat and nested file paths under\n  every tier; orphan-file scan switched from glob to rglob.\n\n- publish.sh: gains --topic flag. Auto-resolves topic from --topic →\n  existing catalog entry → catalog source path. Removes stale copies of\n  the same capability under the same tier so re-grouping never leaves\n  orphan files behind.\n\n- setup-capabilities.sh: now reads the `file` field from catalog.json\n  directly. The field is the single source of truth — no more path\n  inference from <tier>/<name>.md.\n\n- Project CLAUDE.md, claude-marketplace/README.md,\n  claude-marketplace/docs/how-to-consume.md,\n  claude-catalog/release-process.md, claude-catalog/docs/quick-start.md,\n  wiki/Contributing.md, wiki/What-is-Claude-Registry.md updated with the\n  new path conventions. The \"marketplace stays FLAT\" rule has been\n  removed; replaced with a \"Marketplace topics\" section enumerating the\n  topic vocabulary and the rule for spawning a new topic folder.\n\nNo behaviour change for capability consumers: every agent/skill ID is\nidentical; only the on-disk path changed. setup-capabilities.sh\ncontinues to install agents flat under ~/.claude/agents/ exactly as\nbefore — Claude Code does not care where the source lived in the\nregistry.\n\nValidated:\n- python3 .github/scripts/validate_catalog.py    → all checks passed\n- python3 .github/scripts/validate_marketplace.py → all checks passed\n- bash setup-capabilities.sh <tmpdir> all         → 114 files installed,\n  114 Agent rules added to settings.json (smoke test)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bfae8bab98b67bbc7d553e16a028c9c29c11aaea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/bfae8bab98b67bbc7d553e16a028c9c29c11aaea"},"u