ific design\n  system (mandatory check)`. Detects UniCredit deliveries from the\n  prompt, package.json, pom.xml, repo name, Git remote, README, or\n  existing --uc-* tokens, and loads the new skill on top of the\n  generic design-expert / css-expert. Asks once when ambiguous.\n\n- catalog.json: new skill entry; developer-frontend bumped to 0.3.0\n  with unicredit-design-system added to dependencies. README and\n  CHANGELOG updated.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c44168f16b993251d9d9b05c18f1ac8f9ac5f0ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/c44168f16b993251d9d9b05c18f1ac8f9ac5f0ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/0ee09fc8ecc532ee068b9323ed1cf281765e6120","verification":{"payload":"tree c44168f16b993251d9d9b05c18f1ac8f9ac5f0ba\nparent 5b342501d43429fba9d76e6dd2fd424e1ce021af\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777482211 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777482211 +0200\n\nfeat(skills): add unicredit-design-system + auto-load on UniCredit clients (#23)\n\n- New skill `unicredit-design-system@1.0.0` reconstructing UniCredit''s\n  public brand and Bricks design system: logo rules, palette (#E30613\n  red + neutrals + functional states), typography fallback stack\n  (Dax / FS Joey / Inter), 8px spacing grid, ~70 Bricks components,\n  ready-to-paste --uc-* CSS tokens, EN 301 549 / WCAG 2.1 AA\n  accessibility targets, tone of voice. Sources: UniCredit corporate\n  site, public 2012 brand book, BrandingStyleGuides, Tangity case\n  studies (public website, Bricks ecosystem, mobile app, accessibility\n  evolution). The gated WeAreDesign zeroheight portal is referenced\n  explicitly so reviewers can override any reconstructed value.\n\n- `developer-frontend@0.3.0` gains `Step 3.1 — Client-specific design\n  system (mandatory check)`. Detects UniCredit deliveries from the\n  prompt, package.json, pom.xml, repo na