r":{"date":"2026-04-29T14:26:21Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T14:26:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(validator): clear all 8 catalog warnings via inline justifications (#22)\n\nEliminates every warning emitted by validate_catalog.py on a fresh\ncheckout. After this PR, the validator output is \"All checks passed\"\nwith no warnings.\n\n1. streamlit-analyzer description now starts with \"Use to analyze ...\"\n   (was \"Framework-specific analyzer for ...\") — satisfies the validator\n   rule that descriptions start with \"Use when/for/to\" so Claude Code''s\n   automatic delegation can route correctly.\n\n2. Validator now accepts an inline model_justification: frontmatter\n   field. When present and >= 40 chars, the \"model: opus — justify in\n   the PR description\" warning is suppressed. The justification lives\n   with the agent definition (durable) instead of the PR description\n   (which decays after merge). model_justification added to\n   KNOWN_FRONTMATTER_KEYS.\n\n3. Inline model_justification: added to all 7 phase supervisors that\n   run on opus:\n   - indexing-supervisor              (Phase 0)\n   - functional-analysis-supervisor   (Phase 1)\n   - technical-analysis-supervisor    (Phase 2)\n   - baseline-testing-supervisor      (Phase 3)\n   - refactoring-tobe-supervisor      (Phase 4)\n   - tobe-testing-supervisor          (Phase 5)\n   - refactoring-supervisor           (top-level workflow)\n\n   Each justification names the wave structure, the cross-cutting\n   reasoning required, and what would degrade if the agent were\n   downgraded to sonnet. The meta-orchestrator (orchestrator) does\n   not need a justification — opus is mandatory for it by validator\n   rule.\n\nCLAUDE.md governance section updated to document the new convention.\ncatalog and marketplace mirrored.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"daa05d837312723d0c9b4aae18ccfa21295a6d97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/daa05d837312723d0c9b4aae18ccfa21295a6d97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/5b342501d43429fba9d76e6dd2fd424e1ce021af","verification":{"payload":"tree daa05d837312723d0c9b4aae18ccfa21295a6d97\nparent 349697ae1ce59035f3550833dd930986d6a0db4d\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777472781 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777472781 +0200\n\nchore(validator): clear all 8 catalog warnings via inline justifications (#22)\n\nEliminates every warning emitted by validate_catalog.py on a fresh\ncheckout. After this PR, the validator output is \"All checks passed\"\nwith no warnings.\n\n1. streamlit-analyzer description now starts with \"Use to analyze ...\"\n   (was \"Framework-specific analyzer for ...\") — satisfies the validator\n   rule that descriptions start with \"Use when/for/to\" so Claude Code''s\n   automatic delegation can route correctly.\n\n2. Validator now accepts an inline model_justification: frontmatter\n   field. When present and >= 40 chars, the \"model: opus — justify in\n   the PR description\" warning is suppressed. The justification lives\n   with the agent definition (durable) instead of the PR description\n   (which decays after merge). model_justification added to\n   KNOWN_FRONTMATTER_KEYS.\n\n3. Inline model_justification: added to all 7 phase supervisors that\n   run on opus:\n   - indexing-supervisor              (Phase 0)\n   - functional-analysis-supervisor   (Phase 1)\n   - technical-analysis-supervisor    (Phase 2)\n   - baseline-testing-supervisor      (Phase 3)\n   - refactoring-tobe-supervisor      (Phase 4)\n   - tobe-testing-supervisor          (Phase 5)\n   - refactoring-supervisor           (top-level workflow)\n\n   Each justification names the wave structure, the cross-cutting\n   reasoning required, and what would degrade if the 