_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/dc054337800544a0f2b0e929401b4c47f5f23e43","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKGRjMDU0MzM3ODAwNTQ0YTBmMmIwZTkyOTQwMWI0YzQ3ZjVmMjNlNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829","sha":"245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d","sha":"57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d"}],"sha":"dc054337800544a0f2b0e929401b4c47f5f23e43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/dc054337800544a0f2b0e929401b4c47f5f23e43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T17:02:51Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T11:03:11Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"fix(phase2): forbid Bash heredoc/redirect for content output across all phase pipelines\n\nThe state-runtime-analyst sub-agent in Phase 2 produced 48 accidental files in\nthe repo root by passing Mermaid syntax through a Bash heredoc. Shell\nmetacharacters in Mermaid (`A[label]`, `B{cond?}`, `A --> B`) were interpreted\nas redirection, glob expansion, and word splitting — Git Bash / MSYS2 on\nWindows is especially fragile. One redirected filename (`return`) intercepted\nthe output of an unrelated `store` command found on $PATH.\n\nAdds a non-negotiable File-writing rule:\n- Mandates Write/Edit for all file content output\n- Forbids Bash heredoc/echo redirect/tee/printf > file\n- Restricts Bash to read-only inspection and existing-script execution\n\nApplied to:\n- The offender (state-runtime-analyst) and its Mermaid-producing cousins\n  (data-access-analyst, integration-analyst)\n- All five phase supervisors'' sub-agent dispatch prompt templates so the rule\n  propagates at runtime to every worker (technical-analysis-supervisor,\n  functional-analysis-supervisor, indexing-supervisor,\n  refactoring-tobe-supervisor, baseline-testing-supervisor)\n- All other Mermaid-producing sub-agents (ui-surface-analyst,\n  user-flow-analyst, decomposition-architect, migration-roadmap-builder,\n  business-logic-analyst, streamlit-analyzer)\n\n14 capabilities bumped to .X.1; CHANGELOG.md updated; marketplace files\nmirrored. Reference: incident report dated 2026-04-28.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23dc0716b5b814af1d2c348616fa77b67f7ce1d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/23dc0716b5b814af1d2c348616fa77b67f7ce1d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDI0NTYzN2Y5Zjk4MWNlY2YyYWYyMDRlZjc2MTk1ODY3ZTZkZWE4Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6","sha":"d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6"}],"sha":"245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/245637f9f981cecf2af204ef76195867e6dea829"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T09:11:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T09:11:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"refactor: update functional-analysis-supervisor to read stack manifest from canonical codebase-mapper output","tree":{"sha":"1a2dab0ddb37d7d3dd02a12b39425afaeeec508a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/1a2dab0ddb37d7d3dd02a12b39425afaeeec508a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d","node_id":"C_kwDOSGvX_NoAKDU3Zjk4OThmYjkxYTFjOTI1NDdjOGIxMjYxMjZhYTBlMDk3Mzg3MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose/claude-registry/commit/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6","sha":"d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6"}],"sha":"57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/57f9898fb91a1c92547c8b126126aa0e0973871d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/186711793?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:55:57Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:55:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(pipeline): PR-02 — Phase 0 indexing language-agnostic + canonical stack.json (#18)\n\nImplements PR-02 of the language-agnostic migration plan documented in\nclaude-catalog/docs/language-agnostic-design.md (landed in PR-01).\n\nPhase 0 indexing pipeline sheds all hardcoded Python assumptions. The\nnew canonical AS-IS stack manifest is 02-structure/stack.json, produced\nby codebase-mapper, consumed by every downstream phase. Framework-\nspecific analyzers (today only streamlit-analyzer) are gated on\nstack.frameworks — they run only when their framework is detected.\nPolyglot repos are first-class citizens.\n\n7 agents updated:\n\n- indexing-supervisor 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0: frontmatter description rewritten\n  to drop \"Python codebase\"; Phase 0 bootstrap extended with generic\n  stack pre-detection; Phase 1 dispatch reads stack.json and cross-\n  checks framework-specific analyzers; default skip list now language-\n  aware (Python __pycache__/.venv; JVM .gradle/target; Rust target;\n  Go vendor; .NET bin/obj; Ruby vendor/bundle; PHP vendor; TS/JS\n  coverage/.next/.nuxt); decision rule generalized \"framework X not\n  detected -> skip its analyzer entirely\"; dispatch prompt template\n  now includes Stack info block; escalation triggers generalized.\n\n- codebase-mapper 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten language-\n  agnostic. Detects all major languages by extension + content + build\n  manifest. Emits 02-structure/stack.json (machine-readable, schema in\n  language-agnostic-design.md) — the single source of truth for AS-IS\n  stack. Framework detection covers Streamlit/FastAPI/Django/Flask/\n  Spring Boot/Micronaut/Quarkus/Angular/Next.js/Nuxt/Qwik/Vue/\n  Axum/Actix-web/Gin/Chi/Laravel/Symfony/Rails/Sinatra/ASP.NET Core.\n  Test framework detection (pytest, JUnit 5, TestNG, xUnit, NUnit,\n  MSTest, RSpec, Minitest, PHPUnit, Pest, Jest, Vitest, Playwright,\n  Cypress). Polyglot via languages[] + primary by LOC.\n\n- dependency-analyzer 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. Manifest\n  readers per language (Maven/Gradle, Cargo, Go mod, NuGet, Bundler,\n  Composer, npm/pnpm/yarn, Swift). Import-declaration patterns per\n  language. Categorisation extended (SQLAlchemy + JPA + Diesel + EF\n  Core + ActiveRecord + Eloquent + Prisma all under \"ORM\").\n\n- module-documenter 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. Per-language\n  \"surface\" markers (Python __init__, JVM package decls, Go capital\n  identifiers, Rust pub items, C# public types, Ruby modules, PHP\n  namespaces, TS exports). Per-language signature/doc-comment\n  extraction. Side-effect classification heuristics per language.\n\n- business-logic-analyst 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: validation patterns now in a\n  per-language table (Pydantic; Bean Validation; validator-rs; Data\n  Annotations + FluentValidation; Rails validates; FormRequest /\n  Symfony Validator; class-validator/zod/yup); domain-concept\n  extraction with per-language type-definition keywords (data class,\n  record, sealed class, value class, struct, trait, etc.). Magic\n  number / state machine / workflow heuristics remain universal.\n\n- data-flow-analyst 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. DB access\n  patterns table (SQLAlchemy/JPA/jOOQ/Exposed/sqlx/Diesel/sea-orm/\n  EF Core/Dapper/ActiveRecord/Sequel/Eloquent/Doctrine/Prisma/TypeORM/\n  Drizzle/Mongoose/raw). HTTP client patterns table. File I/O, env-\n  var, and config patterns per language.\n\n- streamlit-analyzer 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1: frontmatter clarified — gating on\n  streamlit in stack.frameworks made explicit. Agent itself remains\n  framework-specific by design (canonical pattern for any future\n  framework-specific analyzer).\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green.\n\nPhase 1 (functional analysis) is PR-03; Phase 2-5 follow in PRs 04-07;\nthe top-level supervisor is PR-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a02611082374139855eba3c99a8880c01dd27065","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/a02611082374139855eba3c99a8880c01dd27065"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/d053a6346f04b3eda8888647eb96b8a2b0d0e4f6","verification":{"payload":"tree a02611082374139855eba3c99a8880c01dd27065\nparent 56dcbf78ef1e4dd38b86e5edbec669440ef13058\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777452957 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777452957 +0200\n\nrefactor(pipeline): PR-02 — Phase 0 indexing language-agnostic + canonical stack.json (#18)\n\nImplements PR-02 of the language-agnostic migration plan documented in\nclaude-catalog/docs/language-agnostic-design.md (landed in PR-01).\n\nPhase 0 indexing pipeline sheds all hardcoded Python assumptions. The\nnew canonical AS-IS stack manifest is 02-structure/stack.json, produced\nby codebase-mapper, consumed by every downstream phase. Framework-\nspecific analyzers (today only streamlit-analyzer) are gated on\nstack.frameworks — they run only when their framework is detected.\nPolyglot repos are first-class citizens.\n\n7 agents updated:\n\n- indexing-supervisor 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0: frontmatter description rewritten\n  to drop \"Python codebase\"; Phase 0 bootstrap extended with generic\n  stack pre-detection; Phase 1 dispatch reads stack.json and cross-\n  checks framework-specific analyzers; default skip list now language-\n  aware (Python __pycache__/.venv; JVM .gradle/target; Rust target;\n  Go vendor; .NET bin/obj; Ruby vendor/bundle; PHP vendor; TS/JS\n  coverage/.next/.nuxt); decision rule generalized \"framework X not\n  detected -> skip its analyzer entirely\"; dispatch prompt template\n  now includes Stack info block; escalation triggers generalized.\n\n- codebase-mapper 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten language-\n  agnostic. Detects all major languages by extension + content + build\n  manifest. Emits 02-structure/stack.json (machine-readable, schema in\n  language-agnostic-design.md) — the single source of truth for AS-IS\n  stack. Framework detection covers Streamlit/FastAPI/Django/Flask/\n  Spring Boot/Micronaut/Quarkus/Angular/Next.js/Nuxt/Qwik/Vue/\n  Axum/Actix-web/Gin/Chi/Laravel/Symfony/Rails/Sinatra/ASP.NET Core.\n  Test framework detection (pytest, JUnit 5, TestNG, xUnit, NUnit,\n  MSTest, RSpec, Minitest, PHPUnit, Pest, Jest, Vitest, Playwright,\n  Cypress). Polyglot via languages[] + primary by LOC.\n\n- dependency-analyzer 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. Manifest\n  readers per language (Maven/Gradle, Cargo, Go mod, NuGet, Bundler,\n  Composer, npm/pnpm/yarn, Swift). Import-declaration patterns per\n  language. Categorisation extended (SQLAlchemy + JPA + Diesel + EF\n  Core + ActiveRecord + Eloquent + Prisma all under \"ORM\").\n\n- module-documenter 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. Per-language\n  \"surface\" markers (Python __init__, JVM package decls, Go capital\n  identifiers, Rust pub items, C# public types, Ruby modules, PHP\n  namespaces, TS exports). Per-language signature/doc-comment\n  extraction. Side-effect classification heuristics per language.\n\n- business-logic-analyst 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: validation patterns now in a\n  per-language table (Pydantic; Bean Validation; validator-rs; Data\n  Annotations + FluentValidation; Rails validates; FormRequest /\n  Symfony Validator; class-validator/zod/yup); domain-concept\n  extraction with per-language type-definition keywords (data class,\n  record, sealed class, value class, struct, trait, etc.). Magic\n  number / state machine / workflow heuristics remain universal.\n\n- data-flow-analyst 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: completely rewritten. DB access\n  patterns table (SQLAlchemy/JPA/jOOQ/Exposed/sqlx/Diesel/sea-orm/\n  EF Core/Dapper/ActiveRecord/Sequel/Eloquent/Doctrine/Prisma/TypeORM/\n  Drizzle/Mongoose/raw). HTTP client patterns table. File I/O, env-\n  var, and config patterns per language.\n\n- streamlit-analyzer 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1: frontmatter clarified — gating on\n  streamlit in stack.frameworks made explicit. Agent itself remains\n  framework-specific by design (canonical pattern for any future\n  framework-specific analyzer).\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green.\n\nPhase 1 (functional analysis) is PR-03; Phase 2-5 follow in PRs 04-07;\nthe top-level supervisor is PR-08.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8cedCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXskQALHGYVrmF5b1cSB+DmL3Mhd/\nZyv1gXP7pmd7gPF8XtyvvR6wSd8mb9cwx2v8M/5PssNR5/mEHyDUDzxVc0Pxi3mM\nIuNrKpsu7YeJXrTCnE4MSbWID/X8MutLVNZmwI4jGw/hMaHChQrk18/RHOOVY5iV\nm0iv93TWzhosfP8M0EEVB3ziYb9MySnJgwp3gSQV5ViiWAVAzdc4Lexg2sYK6Kal\nqT+AUzRqXk5/2Ouq7njxhuD1u/7owW+fV7CaIXSbbPfvt/ZlaIZMuLpruqvq1qh/\nf5vmXQGhuT/ImsKEMw5+3QG2k/t4pahGCYXJGPvrMMXV5wU7Wu7VCPbknuJDnJoV\nGj4XeupCtS634S/wlUaZAA7j3dFfnNH+bUUqenFZ/7bCt35qsazrf4YZHNMoUBAi\npMZpC6lAtC47wPpzecKVywK47b+4l7GcqGDZ17y9KXfAq81pM37yCy5c7WfGnyMZ\ny+hNSjr7nXOub/DXWgAqMc5/6eFgSKRrkHhC0S8Z1HRQCECQnMFOjx1k4IJK