s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/luketherose","id":186711793,"login":"luketherose","node_id":"U_kgDOCyD-8Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/56dcbf78ef1e4dd38b86e5edbec669440ef13058/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:42:13Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"Luke The Rose"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:42:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(pipeline): PR-01 — group developers under developers/ + design doc for language-agnostic supervisors (#17)\n\n* refactor(pipeline): PR-01 — group developers under developers/ + design doc for language-agnostic supervisors\n\nOpens the language-agnostic refactoring of refactoring-supervisor and\nits six phase supervisors (Phases 0-5). This PR contains organizational\nchanges and the design document only — NO logic changes. Logic refactor\nproceeds in PR-02 through PR-08, one per phase.\n\nChanges in this PR:\n\n1. Move 9 developer-* agents into claude-catalog/agents/developers/\n   for catalog hygiene. Marketplace layout (flat, claude-marketplace/beta/)\n   is unchanged; catalog.json file fields are unchanged; validation\n   already scans recursively. README structure section updated.\n\n2. New design doc: claude-catalog/docs/language-agnostic-design.md\n   - Goals + non-goals\n   - Architecture: single source of truth for AS-IS stack via\n     codebase-mapper''s stack: block in _meta/manifest.json\n   - Stack detection schema with markers per language/framework\n   - Canonical dispatch table: language -> developer agent + skills\n   - TO-BE handling: read from ADR-002 (decision-driven), no defaults;\n     Phase 5 re-detects on the generated TO-BE codebase\n   - Per-agent change description for each supervisor + sub-agents\n   - 8-PR migration plan\n   - Risks, mitigations, open questions, acceptance criteria\n\nThe design fixes that:\n- Supervisors will read stack from manifest, never hardcode language\n- Streamlit-only assumptions in Phase 0 become framework-conditional\n- Phase 4 reads ADR-002 produced by decomposition-architect; user\n  confirms target stack at HITL checkpoint before code generation\n- Phase 5 re-detects on backend/ + frontend/ to pick the right\n  test framework dispatcher\n- Adding a 10th language = 1 row in dispatch table + 1 developer\n  agent + optional skills (no supervisor changes)\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green (only pre-existing\nopus-justification warnings on supervisors).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update README structure + CHANGELOG for PR-01\n\nForgotten files in the prior commit. README structure section now lists\ndevelopers/ subdirectory; CHANGELOG [Unreleased] notes the developer\nfolder reorganization and the language-agnostic design doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(agent): BREAKING — rename developer-java-spring to developer-java (2.0.0)\n\nPer design doc decision: the Java agent is generalised to support\nmultiple Java frameworks. Spring Boot 3 remains the default (it is the\ndominant enterprise case), but Micronaut, Quarkus, Helidon, and plain\nJava SE are now first-class options when the user declares the\nframework explicitly. Future siblings (developer-java-micronaut,\ndeveloper-java-quarkus) can specialise per framework as demand grows.\n\nFiles renamed:\n- agents/developers/developer-java-spring.md -> developer-java.md\n- marketplace/stable/developer-java-spring.md -> stable/developer-java.md\n- evals/developer-java-spring-eval.md -> evals/developer-java-eval.md\n- examples/developer-java-spring-example.md -> examples/developer-java-example.md\n\nCatalog manifest:\n- name: developer-java-spring -> developer-java\n- version: 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0 (MAJOR — name change is always breaking\n  because Claude uses the name for delegation routing)\n- file: stable/developer-java-spring.md -> stable/developer-java.md\n- description generalised\n- tags expanded (java, spring-boot, micronaut, quarkus, backend,\n  developer)\n\nCross-references updated in 15 files: README capability table, design\ndoc dispatch table + open questions (4 questions resolved with\nrecorded decisions), CHANGELOG, GOVERNANCE example, NAMING-CONVENTIONS\nexamples, how-to-write-a-capability example, review-checklist naming\nexample, eval index + software-architect-eval cross-refs, settings\nexample, pitch deck, quick-start, marketplace consumer docs, marketplace\nversioning example.\n\nMigration for consumers: pull the registry, re-run\n`setup-capabilities.sh`, replace any `Agent(developer-java-spring)`\nin your settings.json with `Agent(developer-java)`. The old name is\ndeleted (not deprecated) — clean rename with version 2.0.0.\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2fe26d57690d163b3fe36c88e5b9bf29db00e6cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/2fe26d57690d163b3fe36c88e5b9bf29db00e6cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/56dcbf78ef1e4dd38b86e5edbec669440ef13058","verification":{"payload":"tree 2fe26d57690d163b3fe36c88e5b9bf29db00e6cd\nparent c75e1a080d6f51c35c7904989a3ac42536224734\nauthor Luke The Rose <luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com> 1777452133 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777452133 +0200\n\nrefactor(pipeline): PR-01 — group developers under developers/ + design doc for language-agnostic supervisors (#17)\n\n* refactor(pipeline): PR-01 — group developers under developers/ + design doc for language-agnostic supervisors\n\nOpens the language-agnostic refactoring of refactoring-supervisor and\nits six phase supervisors (Phases 0-5). This PR contains organizational\nchanges and the design document only — NO logic changes. Logic refactor\nproceeds in PR-02 through PR-08, one per phase.\n\nChanges in this PR:\n\n1. Move 9 developer-* agents into claude-catalog/agents/developers/\n   for catalog hygiene. Marketplace layout (flat, claude-marketplace/beta/)\n   is unchanged; catalog.json file fields are unchanged; validation\n   already scans recursively. README structure section updated.\n\n2. New design doc: claude-catalog/docs/language-agnostic-design.md\n   - Goals + non-goals\n   - Architecture: single source of truth for AS-IS stack via\n     codebase-mapper''s stack: block in _meta/manifest.json\n   - Stack detection schema with markers per language/framework\n   - Canonical dispatch table: language -> developer agent + skills\n   - TO-BE handling: read from ADR-002 (decision-driven), no defaults;\n     Phase 5 re-detects on the generated TO-BE codebase\n   - Per-agent change description for each supervisor + sub-agents\n   - 8-PR migration plan\n   - Risks, mitigations, open questions, acceptance criteria\n\nThe design fixes that:\n- Supervisors will read stack from manifest, never hardcode language\n- Streamlit-only assumptions in Phase 0 become framework-conditional\n- Phase 4 reads ADR-002 produced by decomposition-architect; user\n  confirms target stack at HITL checkpoint before code generation\n- Phase 5 re-detects on backend/ + frontend/ to pick the right\n  test framework dispatcher\n- Adding a 10th language = 1 row in dispatch table + 1 developer\n  agent + optional skills (no supervisor changes)\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green (only pre-existing\nopus-justification warnings on supervisors).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update README structure + CHANGELOG for PR-01\n\nForgotten files in the prior commit. README structure section now lists\ndevelopers/ subdirectory; CHANGELOG [Unreleased] notes the developer\nfolder reorganization and the language-agnostic design doc.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(agent): BREAKING — rename developer-java-spring to developer-java (2.0.0)\n\nPer design doc decision: the Java agent is generalised to support\nmultiple Java frameworks. Spring Boot 3 remains the default (it is the\ndominant enterprise case), but Micronaut, Quarkus, Helidon, and plain\nJava SE are now first-class options when the user declares the\nframework explicitly. Future siblings (developer-java-micronaut,\ndeveloper-java-quarkus) can specialise per framework as demand grows.\n\nFiles renamed:\n- agents/developers/developer-java-spring.md -> developer-java.md\n- marketplace/stable/developer-java-spring.md -> stable/developer-java.md\n- evals/developer-java-spring-eval.md -> evals/developer-java-eval.md\n- examples/developer-java-spring-example.md -> examples/developer-java-example.md\n\nCatalog manifest:\n- name: developer-java-spring -> developer-java\n- version: 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0 (MAJOR — name change is always breaking\n  because Claude uses the name for delegation routing)\n- file: stable/developer-java-spring.md -> stable/developer-java.md\n- description generalised\n- tags expanded (java, spring-boot, micronaut, quarkus, backend,\n  developer)\n\nCross-references updated in 15 files: README capability table, design\ndoc dispatch table + open questions (4 questions resolved with\nrecorded decisions), CHANGELOG, GOVERNANCE example, NAMING-CONVENTIONS\nexamples, how-to-write-a-capability example, review-checklist naming\nexample, eval index + software-architect-eval cross-refs, settings\nexample, pitch deck, quick-start, marketplace consumer docs, marketplace\nversioning example.\n\nMigration for consumers: pull the registry, re-run\n`setup-capabilities.sh`, replace any `Agent(developer-java-spring)`\nin your settings.json with `Agent(developer-java)`. The old name is\ndeleted (not deprecated) — clean rename with version 2.0.0.\n\nValidation: catalog + marketplace both green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8cRlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALHYQAAbOxJmfdVoMqN2Oj1KMZcgu\nT+dxPrmo3FCRD77/wyd55VRzn6Pnosa8OmjEyNvSRzS+FnLDDH4SXnXIx5oRqSD1\nklMvta4yvf4z+qpI4fzwLwXEPmI2fiyvJPfpqEhc7+a5X0OTmbLs8JKipGxcSTOl\nnBatFUHFuQ4T1H7F/b+A8JDidug1TrclC8bu1DJuxlYEmb5M5F2ydd1Gr8g0TBC1\nC6VZ+4b/+cRRE8U6nPE9ETm/M9KcF15N/kNL7Q5wPCc9YLguNd3viIGQv1eu9ohb\nXS8cVlsLRie5T1FZHKIYxKmO/SgQueLP8nXOulfmrRgt/19rssIWSV1X/F+Y7fTO\nWc4kngF+C2fpWmSEZ9aK6UKTMGYW00/uJ2h9TNkzVaYKMOCKWuuegQOVgGBnDTVx\nGpOa1Gd2RZleX/FeAoT7OOob2HJR7W5yxc48xewdAD1uaNxzCn+uktpJbGBIPT6K\nvn6RfWJ2xGiB9br/4/GxjS/ZpZm0TX5TJuQRdzahPorVJGL1YNz1K7fdPyCORraP\nd/BpzVG1K5IjCGK1OOS+CxbzG1wfheDRxUQW83X8qit6Rnx7ZgEiWgX/YgvqbmOY\nubTJvHU0LC4i33LvicuEQx5698crbIDdBGzUl+6ohqH+MFBxY1szWDAyOrnFjc8K\nLx0p66jKUUKUT03PpZoL\n=pItr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-29T08:42:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f