users/luketherose/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/c75e1a080d6f51c35c7904989a3ac42536224734/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:15:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T08:15:44Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"feat: add wiki-writer agent, project wiki, and 6 new developer agents\n\nSquash of three sequentially stacked PRs (#14 → #15 → #16). Capability\ncount: 58 → 65 agents.\n\n1. wiki-writer agent (PR #14)\n   Authors GitHub wikis organised around the Diataxis framework\n   (Tutorials, How-to, Reference, Explanation). Reads the codebase and\n   existing docs; produces Home / _Sidebar / _Footer / topic pages as\n   Markdown in <repo>/wiki/ for PR review. Adapts tone to five audience\n   profiles. Two non-negotiable safety rails: (1) push policy — never\n   pushes to the wiki remote without explicit user authorization in the\n   same session; (2) File-writing rule — all output via Write/Edit, never\n   via Bash heredoc/redirect (carries the 2026-04-28 hardening). Each\n   page carries HTML-comment front matter (audience, diataxis, last-\n   verified, verified-against commit SHA) for stale-content audits.\n\n2. Project wiki content (PR #15)\n   14 wiki pages for claude-registry, authored to wiki-writer''s\n   conventions:\n   - Navigation chrome: Home, _Sidebar, _Footer\n   - Explanation: What-is-Claude-Registry, Architecture, Governance\n   - Tutorial: Quick-start\n   - How-to: Installation, Usage, Contributing\n   - Reference: Capability-catalog, Reference, FAQ, Changelog\n   Committed under wiki/ in the main repo for PR review. Sync to the\n   luketherose/claude-registry.wiki remote is a separate explicit user\n   action.\n\n3. Six new developer-* agents (PR #16)\n   All sonnet, beta. Each carries the post-2026-04-28 File-writing rule.\n   - developer-go@0.1.0 — net/http, chi, gin, cobra; stdlib first;\n     log/slog; context propagation; errors-as-values; golangci-lint.\n   - developer-rust@0.1.0 — stable Rust only; thiserror/anyhow;\n     no unwrap()/expect() in library/service code; tokio with\n     structured concurrency; axum + tracing; sqlx compile-time-checked\n     queries; cargo clippy -D warnings.\n   - developer-kotlin@0.1.0 — Spring Boot 3 with Kotlin idioms or Ktor;\n     coroutines + structured concurrency; sealed hierarchies; value\n     classes; never !! in production; mockk + JUnit 5; ktlint + detekt.\n   - developer-csharp@0.1.0 — ASP.NET Core 8+ controllers + minimal\n     APIs; Nullable + TreatWarningsAsErrors; records for DTOs;\n     IOptions<T> with validation; ILogger<T> + LoggerMessage source\n     generators; xUnit + Testcontainers; NetArchTest assertions.\n   - developer-ruby@0.1.0 — Rails 7+ with service/form/query objects;\n     Sidekiq idempotent jobs; strong-migrations; RSpec + factory_bot;\n     RuboCop with rails/rspec/performance plugins.\n   - developer-php@0.1.0 — PHP 8.2+ with declare(strict_types=1);\n     typed properties + readonly; PHP 8.1 enums; Laravel 10/11\n     (Domain/Application/Infrastructure layering) or Symfony 6/7\n     data-mapper; PHPStan level 8; Pest or PHPUnit 10.\n\nAll capabilities mirrored to claude-marketplace/beta. catalog.json,\nREADME.md, and CHANGELOG.md updated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad14b1c4f6eff15132cd434c45f1a656b2b947fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/ad14b1c4f6eff15132cd434c45f1a656b2b947fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/commits/c75e1a080d6f51c35c7904989a3ac42536224734","verificati