iptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luketherose","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/commits/7ffbbca24a7ca58da77934015da98daf8bf8bfb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T15:34:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T15:34:34Z","email":"luca.la.rosa.dev@gmail.com","name":"luke"},"message":"feat: add exports-only resume mode for Phases 1 and 2\n\nWhen functional or technical analysis is complete on disk but the\nAccenture-branded PDF/PPTX export is missing, the supervisor now\ndetects the state and offers to regenerate ONLY the missing\nexport(s) without re-running the full analysis pipeline.\n\nfunctional-analysis-supervisor 0.2.0 -> 0.3.0\ntechnical-analysis-supervisor 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0:\n- bootstrap classifies the run as `exports-only-eligible` if the\n  manifest reports complete and at least one of the two export\n  files is missing\n- prompts the user with [exports-only / full-rerun / skip]\n  (default: exports-only)\n- when chosen, skips W1/W2/W3 entirely and dispatches only\n  document-creator and/or presentation-creator for the missing\n  file(s); existing analysis is preserved untouched\n- manifest tracks new resume_mode field\n\nrefactoring-supervisor 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0:\n- detection table adds sub-state `complete-but-exports-missing`\n  for Phases 1 and 2 (analysis complete + at least one export\n  file absent)\n- per-phase prompt offers a fourth choice `regenerate-exports`\n  alongside skip / re-run / revise when the sub-state is detected\n- selecting it dispatches the phase supervisor with\n  Resume mode: exports-only\n- choice is refused for Phases 0/3/4 (no PDF/PPTX exports there)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9c48d7b0732b8155a3fdae1c6b88dd07ddf4667b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/luketherose/claude-registry/git/trees/9c48d7b0732b815